var e=[{id:`money-mustard`,title:`Money Mustard`,tagline:`High-Protein Chick-fil-A Style Sauce (with a Kick)`,heroImage:`/images/money-mustard-hero.png`,flavorProfile:`Creamy, tangy, smoky, slight heat`,calories:250,caloriesPerServing:32,protein:23,proteinPerServing:3,servings:8,time:`5 min + 10 min rest`,bestFor:[`Chicken wraps`,`Sliders`,`Nuggets`,`Rice bowls`],useThisWhen:`You want Chick-fil-A flavor at home without the calorie bomb. Works on any protein — wraps, bowls, dips, sliders.`,flavorTarget:`First taste: sweet + tangy. Mid: smoky BBQ. Finish: light heat.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe as written — full kick`,kid:`Reduce hot honey sriracha by half. Optional: add 5g extra BBQ for sweetness.`},ingredients:[`150g Fage Total 0% Greek Yogurt`,`70g French's Organic Yellow Mustard`,`30g Daisy Light Sour Cream`,`30g Taste Flavor Co Cherry Smoked BBQ sauce`,`15g Fairlife Fat Free milk (~1 tbsp, for smoothing)`,`5g Bragg Apple Cider Vinegar (~1 tsp)`,`7g ChocZero Keto Hot Honey`,`5g Taste Flavor Co Hot Honey Sriracha`,`1 tsp onion powder`],steps:[`COMBINE: Add everything to a bowl.`,`WHISK SMOOTH: Whisk aggressively until fully combined. Texture should be creamy + pourable, not thick paste. If too thick, add 1-2 tsp more milk.`,`REST: Let sit 10-15 minutes. Don't skip — this mellows the mustard, blends sweet + acid, and creates the Chick-fil-A balance.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Mustard dominates / too tangy`,fix:`Add 5g more BBQ sauce to balance`},{problem:`Too sharp / acidic`,fix:`Add 10g more yogurt to mellow it`},{problem:`Too thick / paste-like`,fix:`Add milk 1 tsp at a time until pourable`},{problem:`Tastes 'separate' / not blended`,fix:`You didn't rest it. Wait 10-15 min.`},{problem:`Not enough heat`,fix:`Add more hot honey sriracha, 2-3g at a time`}],brands:[{name:`Fage`,item:`Total 0% Greek Yogurt`,why:`Thick, high protein, neutral tang — the sauce base`,image:`/images/brands/fage-yogurt.jpg`,url:`https://usa.fage/products/yogurt/fage-total-0`},{name:`French's`,item:`Organic Yellow Mustard`,why:`Clean, consistent tang without weird additives`,image:`/images/brands/frenchs-mustard.jpg`,url:`https://www.frenchs.com/products/mustard/organic-classic-yellow-mustard`},{name:`Daisy`,item:`Light Sour Cream`,why:`Adds creaminess without heavy calories`,image:`/images/brands/daisy-sour-cream.jpg`,url:`https://www.daisybrand.com/sour-cream/light/`},{name:`Fairlife`,item:`Fat-free milk`,why:`Smooths the sauce without adding calories`,image:`/images/brands/fairlife-milk.png`,url:`https://fairlife.com/ultra-filtered-milk/fat-free-skim-milk/`},{name:`Taste Flavor Co`,item:`Cherry Smoked BBQ`,why:`Smoky sweetness that creates the mid-palate BBQ layer`,image:`/images/brands/taste-cherry-bbq.png`,url:`https://tasteflavorco.com/products/cherry-smoked-bbq`},{name:`Taste Flavor Co`,item:`Hot Honey Sriracha`,why:`The heat finish — controlled kick without overwhelming`,image:`/images/brands/taste-hot-honey-sriracha.png`,url:`https://tasteflavorco.com/products/hot-honey-sriracha`},{name:`ChocZero`,item:`Keto Hot Honey`,why:`Sweet heat layer with no sugar — keeps macros clean`,image:`/images/brands/choczero-hot-honey.png`,url:`https://www.choczero.com/products/keto-hot-honey`},{name:`Bragg`,item:`Apple Cider Vinegar`,why:`Clean acid that brightens without harshness`,image:`/images/brands/bragg-vinegar.jpg`,url:`https://www.bragg.com/products/organic-apple-cider-vinegar`}],mealPrep:{storage:`Airtight container in fridge.`,lasts:`5-7 days. Gets better overnight as flavors meld.`,reheat:`No reheat needed — use cold straight from fridge.`}},{id:`hot-honey-mustard-hack`,title:`Hot Honey Mustard Hack Sauce`,tagline:`2 ingredients. 60 seconds. Money Mustard's lazy cousin.`,heroImage:`/images/hot-honey-mustard-chicken-nuggets/hero-hot-honey-mustard-chicken-nuggets-polished.webp`,flavorProfile:`Sweet + tangy + slow chili heat. Glossy yellow dip that reads like fast-food honey mustard but lands cleaner on macros.`,calories:25,caloriesPerServing:25,protein:0,proteinPerServing:0,servings:1,time:`1 min`,bestFor:[`Chicken nuggets`,`Chicken tenders`,`Wraps`,`Roasted potatoes`,`Air-fryer chicken`],useThisWhen:`You want the sweet-tangy-spicy honey mustard hit without making the full 8-ingredient Money Mustard batch. Single-serve, one bowl, 60 seconds, ~25 cal. This is Money Mustard's lazy cousin — same flavor lane, 1/10 the complexity.`,flavorTarget:`First taste: tangy yellow-mustard bite. Mid: ChocZero sweetness softens the sharpness. Finish: slow habanero warmth that builds 5-10 sec after the bite. Reads like Chick-fil-A sauce — without the sugar or the eight-ingredient prep.`,coreRatio:`3:1 mustard to hot honey. 30g mustard + 10g ChocZero Hot Honey is the system. Push the honey up for sweeter/stickier; hold at 10g for the macro-friendly anchor.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full ratio as written — 30g mustard + 10g ChocZero Hot Honey. The habanero finish is the point.`,kid:`Skip the ChocZero Hot Honey (habanero kick — kids spit it back). Sub 5g plain honey or 5g maple syrup for the same sweet-tangy lift without the heat. Or just serve plain yellow mustard.`},ingredients:[`30g French's Organic Yellow Mustard`,`10g ChocZero Keto Hot Honey`],steps:[`BOWL: 30g French's yellow mustard into a small dipping bowl or ramekin.`,`DRIZZLE: 10g ChocZero Keto Hot Honey on top of the mustard.`,`STIR: Whisk or stir with a fork until fully smooth and glossy — no streaks of honey on top, no mustard pockets at the bottom. Should be the texture of warm honey mustard, not paste.`,`SERVE: Straight into the dip. Best with air-fryer chicken nuggets, chicken tenders, breaded chicken chunks, or roasted potatoes. Eat immediately — this is a fresh-make sauce, not a meal-prep batch.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Sauce is too sharp / mustard-forward`,fix:`Push the ChocZero up — 12-15g hot honey balances the tang. Macros only climb ~5 cal per extra 3g of ChocZero.`},{problem:`Not sweet enough`,fix:`Either use more ChocZero (15g instead of 10g) or sub a less-tangy mustard (Dijon adds depth without the same sharpness).`},{problem:`Not enough heat`,fix:`ChocZero's heat is subtle — for a bigger kick, swap 5g of the ChocZero for 5g of Taste Flavor Co Hot Honey Sriracha (cross-recipe with the full Money Mustard recipe).`},{problem:`Too thick / paste-like`,fix:`Add 1-2 tsp warm water and stir. Should be pourable like warm honey mustard, not toothpaste.`},{problem:`Sauce broke / separated on the plate`,fix:`Either you didn't whisk it fully (re-stir) or the mustard was very cold while the honey was room temp. Both at fridge temp = smooth blend.`}],brands:[{name:`French's`,item:`Organic Yellow Mustard`,why:`Clean, consistent tang without weird additives. The 30g base of the sauce — its sharpness gets balanced by the ChocZero. Cross-recipe with the full Money Mustard recipe.`,image:`/images/brands/frenchs-mustard.jpg`,url:`https://www.frenchs.com/products/mustard/organic-classic-yellow-mustard`},{name:`ChocZero`,item:`Keto Hot Honey (sugar-free, monk-fruit sweetened, with habanero peppers)`,why:`Sugar-free hot honey alternative — soluble corn fiber + monk fruit + red chili peppers. 1:1 sub for traditional hot honey without the sugar load. The 10g portion adds the sweet-heat layer that turns plain yellow mustard into honey-mustard. Cross-recipe with Money Mustard.`,image:`/images/brands/choczero-hot-honey.png`,url:`https://www.choczero.com/products/keto-hot-honey`}],macroHonesty:`Per-serving (~25 cal / 0g protein / 0g fat / ~3g net carbs / ~1g fiber). Component breakdown: 30g French's Organic Yellow Mustard ≈ 9 cal / 0P / 0F / 1C + 10g ChocZero Keto Hot Honey ≈ 15 cal / 0P / 0F / 7C total / 5g fiber → 2 net C. Headline total: 24 cal / 3 net carbs / 1g fiber. Negligible protein/fat. Push the ChocZero up to 15g and the sauce climbs to ~30 cal / 4 net C — still a macro-light dip. The Money Mustard equivalent at the same ~25g per-serving size lands ~32 cal / 3g protein — more protein but more complexity. This Hack version is the 'I have 60 seconds' lane.`,mealPrep:{storage:`Best fresh — make per serving. The 2-ingredient ratio is so simple there's no benefit to batching.`,lasts:`If you must store: covered in fridge 2-3 days. After that the mustard starts to separate and the chili-warmth fades.`,reheat:`No reheat — use cold straight from fridge or room temp.`}},{id:`no-judge-chimichurri`,title:`No-Judge Chimichurri`,tagline:`60-second chimichurri. No chopping herbs. Steak-ready.`,heroImage:`/images/chimichurri-hero.webp`,flavorProfile:`Bright, herby, tangy, slight heat`,calories:100,caloriesPerServing:100,protein:0,proteinPerServing:0,servings:4,time:`1 min + 5 min rest`,bestFor:[`Steak`,`Chicken`,`Rice bowls`,`Grilled anything`],useThisWhen:`You want real chimichurri flavor but don't want to chop parsley, cilantro, and garlic for 15 minutes. Spiceology seasoning does the herb work — you just add oil and acid.`,flavorTarget:`First taste: bright herb + vinegar. Mid: garlic + oregano. Finish: gentle chili heat. Feels fresh, not heavy.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe as written. Spoon over steak, chicken, or any protein.`,kid:`Skip for kids — most won't eat herb sauce. Serve their protein plain or with ketchup.`},ingredients:[`2 tbsp olive oil`,`1.5 tbsp Spiceology Chimichurri seasoning`,`1 tbsp red wine vinegar`,`Dash chili flakes`],steps:[`MIX: Combine olive oil, Spiceology chimichurri seasoning, red wine vinegar, and chili flakes in a small bowl.`,`REST: Let sit 5-10 minutes. Don't skip — the vinegar blooms the dried herbs and the flavor develops.`,`SERVE: Spoon over steak, chicken, or any grilled protein. 1 tbsp per serving.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Tastes flat / like dried herbs`,fix:`You didn't let it rest. The 5-10 min rest is what turns dried seasoning into actual chimichurri.`},{problem:`Too oily`,fix:`Use 1.5 tbsp oil instead of 2. The seasoning absorbs some oil — adjust to your preference.`},{problem:`Too acidic / sharp`,fix:`Reduce vinegar to 2 tsp. Or add a tiny pinch of sugar to round it out.`},{problem:`Not enough heat`,fix:`Add more chili flakes, or a dash of hot sauce.`}],brands:[{name:`Spiceology`,item:`Chimichurri Blend`,why:`Dried herb blend that replaces 15 min of chopping. Just add oil + vinegar.`,image:`/images/brands/spiceology-chimichurri.jpg`,url:`https://spiceology.com/products/chimichurri-blend`},{name:`Napa Valley Naturals`,item:`Organic Red Wine Vinegar`,why:`Clean acid — the vinegar blooms the dried herbs and makes it taste real`,image:`/images/brands/napa-valley-vinegar.jpg`,url:`https://www.stonewallkitchen.com/organic-red-wine-vinegar-M311231.html`},{name:`O California`,item:`Organic Extra Virgin Olive Oil`,why:`Half the sauce is oil — use good oil`,image:`/images/brands/o-olive-oil.jpg`,url:`https://ooliveoil.com/products/o-california-organic-extra-virgin-olive-oil`}],mealPrep:{storage:`Airtight container in fridge.`,lasts:`3-4 days. Gets more flavorful overnight.`,reheat:`No reheat — use at room temp or cold. Stir before using.`}},{id:`indo-chinese-chili-sauce`,title:`Indo-Chinese Chili Sauce`,tagline:`6 ingredients. 1 glass. Restaurant-level glaze.`,heroImage:`/images/chili-chicken/step0-sauce.webp`,flavorProfile:`Smoky, spicy, tangy, slightly sweet — Indo-Chinese glaze`,calories:120,caloriesPerServing:20,protein:1,proteinPerServing:0,servings:6,time:`2 min`,bestFor:[`Chili chicken`,`Stir-fry`,`Noodles`,`Fried rice`,`Any wok dish`],useThisWhen:`You want Indo-Chinese takeout flavor without ordering in. Mix in a glass, dump in a hot wok, reduce 60 seconds. That's it.`,flavorTarget:`Sweet heat from Kikkoman + Ching's. Tang from rice vinegar. Depth from soy. Slow burn from chili crisp + sesame oil. Reduces into a glossy glaze, not a watery sauce.`,splitNote:{adult:`Use full strength. This is designed to hit.`,kid:`Skip entirely for kids. Too spicy to dilute — just serve their protein plain.`},ingredients:[`1 tbsp Kikkoman Thai Style Chili Sauce`,`2 tbsp Ching's Red Chili Sauce`,`2 tbsp Nakano Rice Vinegar`,`2 tbsp Kikkoman Soy Sauce`,`1 tbsp Sesame Chili Oil`,`1 tbsp Dynasty Chili Crisp`],steps:[`MIX: Combine all 6 ingredients in a glass. Stir.`,`USE: Pour ALL at once into a hot wok with cooked veg. Boil hard 60-90 sec until glossy and reduced.`,`COAT: Add crispy protein, toss 45-75 seconds. Kill heat immediately.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Sauce is watery / not glossy`,fix:`Didn't reduce long enough. Boil hard — you should see bubbling and thickening. Optional: add 1/2 tsp cornstarch slurry.`},{problem:`Too sweet`,fix:`Reduce Kikkoman chili sauce by 1 tsp. Or add 1 extra tbsp soy to balance.`},{problem:`Too vinegary / sharp`,fix:`Cut rice vinegar by 1 tbsp. The acid mellows when it reduces.`},{problem:`Not spicy enough`,fix:`Add more Dynasty chili crisp or extra Ching's. The heat is adjustable without changing the base flavor.`}],brands:[{name:`Kikkoman`,item:`Thai Style Chili Sauce`,why:`Sweet heat base — the backbone of the glaze`},{name:`Ching's`,item:`Red Chili Sauce`,why:`Indo-Chinese specific — this is what makes it taste authentic, not generic`},{name:`Nakano`,item:`Rice Vinegar Seasoned`,why:`Acid + slight sweetness — balances heat and adds tang`},{name:`Kikkoman`,item:`Soy Sauce`,why:`Salt + umami — all-purpose, no surprises`},{name:`Dynasty`,item:`Chili Crisp`,why:`Texture + slow burn — crunchy chili bits add layers to the glaze`}],mealPrep:{storage:`Pre-mix in a jar — keeps 1 week in fridge.`,lasts:`1 week mixed. Use at room temp.`,reheat:`N/A — pour into hot wok. Don't heat separately.`}},{id:`smoky-chipotle-crema`,title:`Smoky Chipotle Crema`,tagline:`Bold. Smoky. Proper heat. Built the way it should be.`,heroImage:`/images/chipotle-crema-hero.webp`,flavorProfile:`Smoke-forward, medium-high heat, tangy, clean finish`,calories:480,caloriesPerServing:40,protein:30,proteinPerServing:2.5,servings:12,time:`5 min + 10 min rest`,bestFor:[`Steak`,`Tacos`,`Rice bowls`,`Chicken`,`Sandwiches`],useThisWhen:`You want a real chipotle crema with proper heat — not the watered-down restaurant version. Full can of chipotles. Yogurt + lime keep it clean. Dilute separately for kids.`,flavorTarget:`First taste: smoky chipotle heat. Mid: tangy yogurt + lime. Finish: clean, not greasy, not heavy. This is designed to hit — if it tastes bland, you under-seasoned.`,splitNote:{adult:`Use as-is. Spicy, smoky, full power.`,kid:`Mix 1:1 with plain Greek yogurt to dilute. Or skip entirely — most kids won't want this.`},ingredients:[`200g Fage Total 0% Greek Yogurt`,`7 oz (198g) La Costeña Chipotle Peppers in Adobo (full can)`,`80g Fairlife Fat-Free Milk (~1/3 cup)`,`60g Kraft Light Mayo`,`1 tbsp lime juice`,`3/4-1 tsp salt (taste and adjust)`,`1/2 tsp garlic powder`,`1/2 tsp cumin`],steps:[`BLEND: Add everything to blender — yogurt, full chipotle can + adobo, milk, mayo, lime juice, salt, garlic powder, cumin. Blend 30-45 seconds until fully smooth.`,`TASTE: Too thick → add 1 tbsp milk. Too sharp → add 1 tbsp yogurt. Too flat → pinch more salt + lime.`,`REST: Let sit 10-15 minutes before serving. Heat rounds out, texture tightens. Don't skip.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Not smoky enough / bland`,fix:`You diluted it or under-seasoned. Use the full can of chipotles — that's the whole point.`},{problem:`Too spicy`,fix:`Don't reduce the base recipe — instead, mix portion 1:1 with plain yogurt for a milder version.`},{problem:`Too thick / paste-like`,fix:`Add milk 1 tbsp at a time. Should be pourable crema, not paste.`},{problem:`Tastes muddy / heavy`,fix:`Not enough acid. Add more lime juice — the tang is what keeps it clean.`},{problem:`Grainy texture`,fix:`Didn't blend long enough. Full 30-45 seconds, no chunks.`}],brands:[{name:`La Costeña`,item:`Chipotle Peppers in Adobo`,why:`Full can = real smoky heat. This is the backbone of the sauce — don't sub it.`,image:`/images/brands/la-costena-chipotle.jpg`,url:`https://www.target.com/p/la-costena-chipotle-peppers-in-adobo-sauce-7oz/-/A-52527972`},{name:`Fage`,item:`Total 0% Greek Yogurt`,why:`Thick, high protein, tangy base — keeps the crema clean without heavy cream`,image:`/images/brands/fage-yogurt.jpg`,url:`https://usa.fage/products/yogurt/fage-total-0`},{name:`Fairlife`,item:`Fat-Free Milk`,why:`Thins the crema without watering down flavor`,image:`/images/brands/fairlife-milk.png`,url:`https://fairlife.com/ultra-filtered-milk/fat-free-skim-milk/`},{name:`Kraft`,item:`Light Mayo`,why:`Controlled creaminess — just enough body without turning it into dressing`,image:`/images/brands/kraft-light-mayo.jpg`,url:`https://www.heb.com/product-detail/kraft-mayo-light-mayonnaise-squeeze-bottle/1098140`}],mealPrep:{storage:`Airtight container in fridge.`,lasts:`5-7 days. Gets better overnight as flavors meld.`,reheat:`No reheat needed — use cold straight from fridge.`}},{id:`umami-lemon-heat`,title:`Umami Lemon Heat Sauce`,tagline:`Creamy. Salty. Bright. Finishes with heat.`,heroImage:`/images/umami-lemon-heat-hero.webp`,prepImage:`/images/umami-lemon-heat-spoon.webp`,prepImageCaption:`Texture target — pourable, coats the back of a spoon`,actionImage:`/images/umami-lemon-heat-asparagus.webp`,actionImageCaption:`On charred asparagus — the canonical use case`,flavorProfile:`Creamy mayo base, lemon brightness, soy umami, slow chili burn`,calories:320,caloriesPerServing:70,protein:1,proteinPerServing:0,servings:5,time:`3 min + 5 min rest`,bestFor:[`Charred veggies`,`Roasted broccoli`,`Chicken bowls`,`Sandwich spread`,`Rice + protein bowls`],useThisWhen:`You want a creamy drizzle that makes vegetables disappear. Built for charred asparagus, roasted broccoli, bowls, and anything that needs a finisher. Mix in a bowl in 3 minutes — the rest is what makes it taste real.`,flavorTarget:`First taste: creamy mayo + bright lemon. Mid: soy umami + Dijon depth. Finish: slow chili oil burn. Pourable but coats the back of a spoon — not runny, not paste.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe as written. Drizzle generously over charred or roasted veg.`,kid:`Halve or skip the chili oil. The base without heat is still great as a creamy dip.`},ingredients:[`1/3 cup Kraft Light Mayo`,`1.5 tbsp lemon juice`,`1.5 tbsp Kikkoman Soy Sauce`,`1 tbsp Smash Kitchen Organic Dijon Mustard`,`1 tsp Lee Kum Kee Chili Oil`],steps:[`COMBINE: Add everything to a bowl — mayo, lemon juice, soy, Dijon, chili oil.`,`WHISK: Whisk until smooth and fully combined. No streaks of mayo, no separated oil.`,`REST: Let sit 5 minutes before using. Don't skip — this is when the flavors settle and stop tasting disjointed.`,`TASTE + ADJUST: More lemon = brighter. More soy = saltier. More chili oil = heat. Too thick? Add 1-2 tsp water. Too thin? Add 1 tsp more mayo.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Tastes flat / disjointed`,fix:`You skipped the rest. 5 minutes minimum — the acid + umami + heat need to meld.`},{problem:`Too salty / overpowering`,fix:`Too much soy. Add 1 tsp more mayo + a squeeze of lemon to rebalance.`},{problem:`Tastes heavy / one-dimensional`,fix:`Not enough acid. Add another 1/2 tsp lemon juice — brightness is what cuts the mayo.`},{problem:`Too thick / paste-like`,fix:`Add 1-2 tsp water. Should be pourable, coat the back of a spoon.`},{problem:`Too thin / runny`,fix:`Add 1 tsp more mayo. The base needs to hold the drizzle.`},{problem:`No heat`,fix:`Lee Kum Kee is mild — bump to 2 tsp. Or add a dash of sriracha.`}],systemInsight:{title:`The Sauce Framework: Base + Acid + Umami + Heat + Depth`,body:`Memorize this once and stop following sauce recipes forever. Every great drizzle is the same 5 levers — swap any of them and you've built a new sauce.`,framework:[{lever:`Base`,role:`Creaminess + body`,swaps:`Mayo, Greek yogurt, sour cream, tahini`},{lever:`Acid`,role:`Brightness — cuts the base`,swaps:`Lemon, lime, rice vinegar, ACV`},{lever:`Umami`,role:`Salt + savory depth`,swaps:`Soy, miso, fish sauce, Worcestershire`},{lever:`Heat`,role:`Slow burn finish`,swaps:`Chili oil, sriracha, harissa, gochujang`},{lever:`Depth`,role:`Mid-palate complexity`,swaps:`Dijon, garlic, ginger, smoked paprika`}],payoff:`You just built one version. Now you can build 10+ variations without thinking. Mayo + lime + miso + sriracha + ginger = Asian. Yogurt + lemon + Worcestershire + harissa + garlic = Mediterranean.`},brands:[{name:`Kraft`,item:`Light Mayo`,why:`Half the calories of regular mayo, holds emulsion well — the creamy base without the fat bomb`,image:`/images/brands/kraft-light-mayo.jpg`,url:`https://www.heb.com/product-detail/kraft-mayo-light-mayonnaise-squeeze-bottle/1098140`},{name:`Kikkoman`,item:`All-Purpose Soy Sauce`,why:`Clean salt + umami — the savory backbone, no surprises`,image:`/images/brands/kikkoman-soy-sauce.jpg`,url:`https://kikkomanusa.com/homecooks/products/soy-sauce-non-gmo/`},{name:`Smash Kitchen`,item:`Organic Dijon Mustard`,why:`Mid-palate depth and emulsifier — what makes the sauce taste 'finished' instead of mixed`,image:`/images/brands/smash-kitchen-dijon.jpg`,url:`https://smashkitchen.com/products/dijon-mustard`},{name:`Lee Kum Kee`,item:`Chiu Chow Style Chili Crisp Oil`,why:`Slow burn, real chili flavor — not just heat. The finishing layer.`,image:`/images/brands/lee-kum-kee-chili-oil.jpg`,url:`https://usa.lkk.com/en/products/chiu-chow-style-chili-crisp-oil`}],mealPrep:{storage:`Airtight jar in the fridge. Stir before each use.`,lasts:`5-7 days. Flavor deepens overnight.`,reheat:`No reheat — use cold or room temp.`}},{id:`protein-blue-cheese-crema`,title:`Protein Blue Cheese Crema`,tagline:`Tastes like real blue cheese sauce. Quietly protein-forward.`,heroImage:`/images/blue-cheese-crema/hero.webp`,prepImage:`/images/blue-cheese-crema/mise-en-place.webp`,prepImageCaption:`Mise en place — Daisy + 365 + Fairlife + chives on a cutting board`,flavorProfile:`Creamy, funky, tangy, sharp, herbaceous finish`,calories:528,caloriesPerServing:66,protein:38,proteinPerServing:5,servings:8,time:`5 min + 10 min rest`,bestFor:[`Wings dip`,`Buffalo bowls`,`Wedge salads`,`Wraps`,`Burgers`,`Steak sauce`,`Roasted veggies`,`Buffalo chicken tacos`],useThisWhen:`You want a real blue cheese sauce — not 'inspired by' blue cheese. Texture as smooth as restaurant crema, real blue cheese funk, and enough protein from the cottage cheese base that it carries the meal nutritionally. This is the ecosystem sauce: dip, drizzle, dressing, spread — all the same jar.`,flavorTarget:`First taste: creamy + tangy (cottage cheese + Fairlife). Mid: real blue cheese funk + sharpness (365 Blue Cheese crumbles). Finish: bright lemon lift + savory SPG depth + fresh chive herbaceousness. Reads as 'restaurant blue cheese' not 'protein hack'.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe as written. Generous on wings, salads, anywhere bold blue cheese belongs.`,kid:`Same sauce works for kids — it's mild enough. Serve as a DIP in its own ramekin, not poured over food. Kids commit at their own pace.`},ingredients:[`150g Daisy Cottage Cheese 2% (1 small container)`,`113g 365 Blue Cheese Crumbles (4 oz container, full)`,`30g Fairlife Fat-Free Lactose-Free Milk (~2 tbsp)`,`1 tsp lemon juice (the acid that sharpens it — don't skip)`,`1 tsp Dan-O's SPG Tri-O (Salt-Pepper-Garlic — does the work of fresh garlic without the harsh bite)`,`1 tbsp fresh chives, finely chopped (FOLDED IN AFTER blending — never blend, or the sauce turns green)`],steps:[`BLEND BASE: Cottage cheese + Fairlife + lemon juice + SPG Tri-O in a blender or immersion-blender cup. Blend 60 sec on high until completely smooth — zero curd visible. This is the texture move.`,`ADD BLUE CHEESE: Add about 80% of the blue cheese crumbles. Pulse 5-6 times — you want the sauce blue-cheese-flavored but with visible chunks. NOT smooth all the way through.`,`FOLD IN CHUNKS + CHIVES: Stir the remaining 20% of crumbles + all the chopped chives in by hand. Chives go in LAST so they don't blend and turn the sauce green.`,`REST: Fridge, 10-15 minutes. Lemon mellows, blue cheese funk deepens, texture tightens. Non-negotiable.`,`TASTE: Too sharp? Add 1 tbsp more cottage cheese. Too thick? 1 tsp more milk. Not funky enough? Crumble in a few more chunks of blue cheese.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Sauce is grainy / chalky`,fix:`Didn't blend the cottage cheese smooth enough. Full 60 seconds on high BEFORE adding the blue cheese. The cottage cheese base is what kills the chalkiness.`},{problem:`Tastes like 'protein hack' not real blue cheese`,fix:`You under-blue-cheesed. The whole 4 oz container goes in. Don't trim it to 'save calories' — that's the move that makes homemade protein dressings taste fake.`},{problem:`Flat / one-dimensional`,fix:`Skipped the lemon. 1 tsp lemon juice is what sharpens the dairy and makes it taste finished, not soft.`},{problem:`Harsh raw-garlic taste`,fix:`You used fresh raw garlic instead of SPG Tri-O. Raw garlic kills blue cheese nuance. SPG is granulated — gives depth without the bite.`},{problem:`Sauce turned green-tinged`,fix:`You blended the chives. Always fold them in by hand AFTER everything else is mixed.`},{problem:`Too thick / paste-like`,fix:`Add 1 tsp Fairlife at a time. The cottage cheese tightens overnight — adjust day-of.`}],brands:[{name:`Daisy`,item:`Cottage Cheese 2% Low Fat`,why:`13g protein per ½ cup, only milk + cream + salt (no gums), blends silky-smooth — the protein base that kills the chalkiness most 'healthy' blue cheese dressings have`,image:`/images/brands/daisy-cottage-cheese-2pct.jpg`,url:`https://www.kroger.com/p/daisy-pure-and-natural-2-low-fat-cottage-cheese/0007342051620`},{name:`365 by Whole Foods Market`,item:`Organic Blue Cheese Crumbles`,why:`Real blue cheese flavor — Penicillium Roqueforti, no shortcuts. This is what makes the sauce taste like actual restaurant blue cheese instead of 'inspired by'. Don't trim it to save calories — that's the failure mode.`,url:`https://www.wholefoodsmarket.com/grocery/product/365-by-whole-foods-market-organic-blue-cheese-crumbles-4-oz-b083crj3ql`},{name:`Fairlife`,item:`Fat-Free Lactose-Free Ultra-Filtered Milk`,why:`Loosens the texture without watering down the flavor. Most homemade protein dressings use water — water kills richness perception. Milk maintains the cream sensation while keeping macros clean.`,image:`/images/brands/fairlife-milk.png`,url:`https://fairlife.com/ultra-filtered-milk/fat-free-skim-milk/`},{name:`Dan-O's`,item:`SPG Tri-O Seasoning (Salt-Pepper-Garlic)`,why:`Granulated garlic, salt, pepper — gives depth without the harsh bite of fresh raw garlic. Raw garlic overpowers blue cheese; SPG complements it. The 'pro move' substitute.`,image:`/images/brands/danos-spg-tri-o.png`,url:`https://danosseasoning.com/product/spg-tri-o-medium-bottle/`}],mealPrep:{storage:`Airtight container in fridge. Stir before each use — separation is normal.`,lasts:`5-7 days. Flavor deepens overnight. Better on day 2 than day 1.`,reheat:`Never — serve cold or room temp. Heat curdles the cottage cheese.`}},{id:`tks-sauce`,title:`TKS Sauce`,tagline:`Sweet heat + umami glaze. Macro-conscious takeout, six ingredients, two minutes.`,heroImage:`/images/tks-sauce/mise-en-place.webp`,flavorProfile:`Salty, tangy, lightly sweet, mildly spicy. Bone broth body without oil. Takeout aroma from sesame chili oil.`,calories:110,caloriesPerServing:55,protein:12,proteinPerServing:6,servings:2,time:`2 min`,bestFor:[`Crispy chicken (1 lb = 2 servings)`,`Rice bowls`,`Wraps`,`Stir-fry glaze`,`Dipping for dumplings`,`Future TKS Wraps / TKS Bowls / TKS Shrimp`],useThisWhen:`You want General Tso-style takeout flavor without the cornstarch-and-sugar bomb. Six ingredients, two minutes, one batch coats 1 lb of crispy chicken for two servings. The bone broth powder is doing the work most takeout sauces do with starch and oil — body without fat, depth without sugar.`,flavorTarget:`Layered — soy + bone broth for salt and savory depth, rice vinegar to sharpen, hot honey sriracha for sweet heat, ginger-garlic paste for backbone, sesame chili oil for takeout aroma. Smooth pourable glaze that clings to crispy chicken when tossed in a hot pan. NOT sticky-sweet, NOT cornstarch-thick, NOT the orange-sauce-packet you discarded.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe. Toss with 1 lb crispy chicken in a hot dry pan for 60-90 sec — the residual breading starch + sauce caramelize into restaurant glaze.`,kid:`Halve the hot honey sriracha if kids are spice-sensitive. The sauce loses the sweet-heat edge but keeps the savory backbone — still good on plain chicken or rice.`},ingredients:[`1 tbsp Verka Organic Ginger Garlic Paste`,`1/2 tsp Dynasty Sesame Chili Oil`,`1 tbsp Nakano Seasoned Rice Vinegar (Mild & Sweet)`,`2 tbsp Kikkoman All-Purpose Soy Sauce (1/8 cup)`,`1 packet Bare Bones Instant Chicken Bone Broth (15g, 10g protein)`,`1.5 tbsp Taste Flavor Co. Hot Honey Sriracha`],steps:[`COMBINE: Add ginger-garlic paste, sesame chili oil, rice vinegar, soy sauce, bone broth packet (open it and pour the powder in), and hot honey sriracha to a small bowl or shaker bottle.`,`WHISK AGGRESSIVELY: Until the bone broth powder fully dissolves — no clumps. The powder is what gives the sauce body; if it's not dissolved, the sauce stays thin and tastes flat.`,`TASTE + ADJUST: Too salty → add 1 tsp more vinegar OR 1 tsp more hot honey. Too sweet → add 1 tsp more soy. Too flat → bump the sesame chili oil to 3/4 tsp. Too thin → simmer 60 sec in a small pan (rare; usually the toss-in-hot-pan step at the dish level fixes this).`,`READY TO USE: For crispy chicken, pour around the edge of a hot dry skillet, add the cooked chicken, toss aggressively 60-90 sec until coated. The dry skillet + residual breading starch + sauce = natural cling, no slurry needed.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Sauce tastes flat / one-dimensional`,fix:`Bone broth packet wasn't fully dissolved. Whisk harder or use a shaker bottle — the powder is doing more than half the savory work.`},{problem:`Too thin, doesn't cling to the chicken`,fix:`Don't add cornstarch. Pour the sauce into a hot dry skillet with cooked chicken and toss 60-90 sec — the breading starch + sauce caramelize into glaze. If you absolutely need it thicker as a dip, simmer 60 sec in a small pan to reduce.`},{problem:`Too salty`,fix:`Soy sauce brands vary in sodium. Add 1 tsp more rice vinegar OR 1 tsp more hot honey sriracha to rebalance. Don't dilute with water — that kills the depth the bone broth provides.`},{problem:`Not spicy enough`,fix:`Bump the hot honey sriracha to 2 tbsp. Or stir in 1/4 tsp Dynasty chili crisp at the end.`},{problem:`Too thin for dipping (rice bowl drizzle, wrap)`,fix:`Simmer 60 sec in a small saucepan to reduce by 1/4. Don't add starch — the bone broth powder + soy concentrate naturally on heat.`}],brands:[{name:`Verka`,item:`Organic Ginger Garlic Paste`,why:`Pre-minced ginger + garlic in jar — saves 10 min of knife work per use. The paste form distributes evenly through liquid sauces (fresh-grated ginger clumps).`,image:`/images/brands/verka-ginger-garlic-paste.jpg`,url:`https://www.verkausa.com/product/masala-ginger-garlic-750`},{name:`Dynasty`,item:`Sesame Chili Oil (3.5 oz)`,why:`Toasted sesame aroma + slow chili burn = the 'takeout smell' that makes the sauce read as restaurant. Only 1/2 tsp here — this is the aromatic top note, not the main heat.`,url:`https://www.amazon.com/Dynasty-Sesame-Chili-Oil-3-5/dp/B0001LJAW2`},{name:`Nakano`,item:`Seasoned Rice Vinegar (Mild & Sweet)`,why:`Seasoned variant has sugar + salt already added — does double duty as acid + sweetener so the sauce doesn't need a separate sugar source.`,image:`/images/brands/nakano-seasoned-rice-vinegar.jpg`,url:`https://www.kroger.com/p/nakano-seasoned-mild-sweet-rice-vinegar/0007357529500`},{name:`Kikkoman`,item:`All-Purpose Soy Sauce`,why:`Clean salt + umami. The default soy on this site.`,image:`/images/brands/kikkoman-soy-sauce.jpg`,url:`https://kikkomanusa.com/homecooks/products/soy-sauce-non-gmo/`},{name:`Bare Bones`,item:`Instant Chicken Bone Broth (15g packet, Classic Chicken)`,why:`10g protein per packet. THIS is the move — bone broth powder gives body, savory depth, and protein boost without oil, butter, or cornstarch. The trick that makes the sauce 'macro-conscious takeout' instead of 'inspired by takeout'.`,image:`/images/brands/bare-bones-chicken-broth.png`,url:`https://www.barebonesbroth.com/products/instant-bone-broth`},{name:`Taste Flavor Co.`,item:`Hot Honey Sriracha`,why:`Sweet heat in a single bottle — replaces sugar + sriracha separately. 1.5 tbsp here delivers the candy-heat finish that makes takeout chicken taste like takeout.`,image:`/images/brands/taste-hot-honey-sriracha.png`,url:`https://tasteflavorco.com/products/hot-honey-sriracha`}],macroHonesty:`Per-batch macros (110 cal / 12g protein / 2g fat / 10g carbs) computed from ingredients, with the Bare Bones packet doing most of the protein lift (10g of the 12g batch total). At 2 servings = 55 cal / 6g protein each. Calorie-wise this is a real Tier 1 sauce — flavor work without macro damage. Flagged as estimated because soy brand sodium and seasoned vinegar sugar content vary.`,mealPrep:{storage:`Pre-mix in a small jar with a lid. Fridge between uses — bone broth powder + soy stay stable.`,lasts:`4-5 days in fridge. Make fresh per use is honestly fastest (2 min); the make-ahead is for batching across multiple dinners in a week.`,reheat:`Use cold or warm. If using on rice bowls, drizzle straight from the jar. If glazing chicken, the hot pan does the heating.`}},{id:`chili-crisp-sour-cream`,title:`Chili Crisp Sour Cream`,tagline:`Cool, creamy, lightly spicy. Two ingredients. Cross-links across the cookbook.`,heroImage:`/images/outlaw-grilled-thighs/step5-sauce.webp`,flavorProfile:`Cool tang from sour cream, slow shallot-garlic burn from chili crisp, visible orange streaks. Reads as restaurant dip — not a 'fitness sauce'.`,calories:160,caloriesPerServing:40,protein:4,proteinPerServing:1,servings:4,time:`1 min`,bestFor:[`Grilled chicken thighs (Outlaw BBQ, see recipe 37)`,`Crispy smashed potatoes`,`Buffalo wings (alt to blue cheese crema)`,`Leftover grilled chicken wraps`,`Baked salmon`,`Roasted broccoli or asparagus`,`Cutting-friendly dip`],useThisWhen:`You want a cool, creamy dip that adds heat + complexity without dumping calories. Fold (don't stir) — visible orange chili oil streaks ARE the brand. Build it once Sunday, it crosses 3+ dinners through the week.`,flavorTarget:`Cool + creamy + visible chili oil swirl. The chili crisp brings shallot + garlic + slow heat; Daisy Light is the cool/tangy carrier. NOT homogenous beige — fold gently, stop while streaks remain.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe. 2-3 tbsp Lee Kum Kee Chiu Chow chili crisp folded into 1/2 cup Daisy Light. Drizzle on the side of grilled chicken, smashed potatoes, wings — anywhere a cool/creamy/spicy dip fits.`,kid:`Skip the chili crisp entirely. Plain Daisy Light Sour Cream in a small ramekin or the 3-compartment-tray dip well is the kid version. Kids consistently reject the visual chili-oil streaks — keep the cream pure white for them.`},ingredients:[`1/2 cup Daisy Light Sour Cream`,`2-3 tbsp Lee Kum Kee Chiu Chow Style Chili Crisp Oil`],steps:[`SPOON SOUR CREAM into a small bowl or ramekin.`,`ADD CHILI CRISP on top — 2 tbsp if you want a mild dip, 3 tbsp if you want the heat to lead. Lee Kum Kee Chiu Chow specifically because the shallot + garlic bits carry flavor; generic chili oil is too one-note.`,`FOLD GENTLY 3-4 TIMES with a spoon. STOP when you can still see orange chili oil streaks running through the white sour cream. Don't stir — fold. Homogenized = beige = looks like ranch. Streaked = chili crisp sour cream.`,`SERVE IMMEDIATELY or refrigerate up to 5 days. The streaks blur slightly after a few hours but the flavor holds.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Sauce looks beige / homogenous`,fix:`You stirred too much. Drizzle a fresh 1 tsp of chili crisp ON TOP just before serving to restore the visual. Lesson for next time: fold 3-4 times maximum.`},{problem:`Too spicy for your taste`,fix:`More sour cream — start at 1:8 chili crisp to sour cream ratio (1 tbsp per 1/2 cup). Or add 1 tsp lime juice to brighten and round off the heat.`},{problem:`Not spicy enough`,fix:`Bump to 3 tbsp chili crisp. Or stir in 1/4 tsp red chili flakes. Don't substitute regular chili oil — Lee Kum Kee Chiu Chow has the shallot + garlic bits doing the flavor work.`},{problem:`Watered out / thin after a day`,fix:`Daisy Light naturally weeps a little after 24 hours. Stir before serving, drain off any excess clear liquid. OR use full-fat sour cream if you want zero weep (macros climb slightly).`},{problem:`Kid sees the orange streaks and refuses`,fix:`Different bowl. The chili crisp version is adult-only — plate the kid's plain sour cream in its own ramekin/compartment so they never see the spicy version mixed in.`}],brands:[{name:`Daisy`,item:`Light Sour Cream (1 lb / 16 oz tub, 50% less fat)`,why:`Tangy + cool + cuts the chili crisp heat. The Light variant is intentional — chili crisp does the flavor work, sour cream is the carrier. Full-fat works but pushes calories without adding much.`,image:`/images/brands/daisy-sour-cream.jpg`,url:`https://www.daisybrand.com/our-products/sour-cream/`},{name:`Lee Kum Kee`,item:`Chiu Chow Style Chili Crisp Oil (7.2 oz, 205g)`,why:`Shallot + garlic bits + chili oil. The Chiu Chow specifically — generic chili oil is too one-note. One jar runs across 3+ recipes (Outlaw thighs marinade + this sauce + leftover wraps).`,image:`/images/brands/lee-kum-kee-chili-oil.jpg`,url:`https://usa.lkk.com/en/products/chiu-chow-style-chili-crisp-oil-7-2-oz`}],macroHonesty:`Per-serving (40 cal / 1g protein / 3.5g fat / 2g carbs) computed from 2 tbsp portion (1/8 of full batch). Lee Kum Kee Chiu Chow chili crisp is 40 cal per 1 tbsp; Daisy Light is ~25 cal per 2 tbsp. Total batch at 4 servings = 160 cal. Flagged estimated because chili crisp serving sizes vary by jar.`,mealPrep:{storage:`Cover and refrigerate. The streaks blur slightly after a few hours but flavor holds 5 days.`,lasts:`5 days refrigerated. Best fresh for the visual; pre-batched for convenience.`,reheat:`None — serve cold straight from the fridge.`}},{id:`lift-drizzle`,title:`Lift Drizzle`,tagline:`Five ingredients. Bright + salty + fermented + hot. Acid does the lift.`,heroImage:`/images/pork-lettuce-wraps/step4-sauce-mise.webp`,flavorProfile:`Cold + bright lemon up front, slow fermented depth from fish sauce + soy, lingering chili heat, citrusy aromatic finish from coriander. Pourable, not creamy. Lifts soft + rich dishes; doesn't compete with them.`,calories:280,caloriesPerServing:140,protein:3,proteinPerServing:1.5,servings:2,time:`2 min`,bestFor:[`Pork lettuce wraps (recipe 38)`,`Grilled chicken bowls`,`Cold rice noodle salads`,`Crispy tofu / seared shrimp`,`Cucumber + green onion salad`,`Roasted broccoli / asparagus`,`Anywhere a Vietnamese nuoc cham would go`],useThisWhen:`You've made something soft + rich (pork mince, fatty chicken, creamy noodle) and the dish is dying for acid + salt + heat. Lift Drizzle is what separates 'healthy protein in a vehicle' from 'restaurant-grade dinner.' The name says it — acid lifts.`,flavorTarget:`Bright + salty + fermented + lightly spicy. Acid leads; oil carries; coriander aromatic finishes. NOT sweet, NOT sticky, NOT creamy. If you stir it and it looks like ranch or hoisin glaze, you've gone wrong.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe — 2 chopped fresh red chilies + 1/2 tsp coriander + the full base. Serve in a small bowl with a spoon, not poured over the dish. Adults build their own bite.`,kid:`Skip the chilies. Skip the coriander. Drop the soy to 1 tbsp. The remaining base (oil + fish sauce + lemon) is approachable but most kids will still prefer a creamier alt — Herdez Taqueria Avocado Cilantro is the better kid sauce. Default to that.`},ingredients:[`2 tbsp olive oil (California Organic Extra Virgin, or any quality EVOO)`,`2 tbsp Kikkoman All-Purpose Soy Sauce`,`1 tbsp Red Boat Fish Sauce 40°N`,`3 tbsp ReaLemon lemon juice (~6 portions, or fresh-squeezed from 1 lemon)`,`1/2 tsp Deep Coriander Powder`,`2 fresh red Thai chilies, finely chopped`],steps:[`WHISK IN A SMALL BOWL: Olive oil + soy sauce + fish sauce + lemon juice + coriander powder. Whisk until the coriander dissolves (it tries to clump — keep whisking).`,`ADD CHILIES: Chop 2 fresh red Thai chilies finely. Stir in. The chili oil + capsaicin needs to mingle for ~2 min before serving — they're not just visual.`,`TASTE + ADJUST: Too salty → bump lemon by 1 tsp. Too flat → add 1 more pinch coriander. Too thin / runny — DON'T thicken with cornstarch (that's the takeout trap). Add 1 more tsp olive oil if you want body, but flat-and-bright is the brand.`,`SERVE: Small bowl with a small spoon. Adults spoon into their wraps / bowls / salads at the table. Never pour over the platter — lettuce wilts in 60 sec.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Drizzle tastes flat / one-dimensional`,fix:`You skipped the coriander OR under-measured the lemon. Coriander adds the third layer of brightness past lemon + chilies. Bump lemon by 1 tsp + add 1/4 tsp more coriander.`},{problem:`Too salty`,fix:`Soy and fish sauce both stack salt. Add 1 tbsp more lemon juice to rebalance. Don't dilute with water — kills the body.`},{problem:`Too oily / heavy mouthfeel`,fix:`LIGHTER VARIANT: drop olive oil to 1 tbsp + bump lemon to 4 tbsp + add 1 tsp rice vinegar + 1 tsp allulose. Brighter, half the calories, slightly sweetened to balance the soy. Try both, pick your tier.`},{problem:`Not enough heat`,fix:`Bump to 3 chilies, OR stir in 1/2 tsp Dynasty Sesame Chili Oil. Don't reach for sambal — too thick, kills the pourable consistency.`},{problem:`Sauce separated after sitting`,fix:`Olive oil + acid always separates. Whisk again before serving. Or shake in a small jar. The separation isn't a flaw — it's the structure.`}],brands:[{name:`Red Boat`,item:`Fish Sauce 40°N (8.45 fl oz)`,why:`First-press, barrel-aged Vietnamese fish sauce. Just anchovies + salt — no MSG, no caramel coloring. The salt + umami + fermented depth that lifts the dish without sugar. Three Crabs or Squid Brand work; avoid discount labels.`,image:`/images/brands/red-boat-fish-sauce.png`,url:`https://redboatfishsauce.com/products/fish-sauce-40n`},{name:`Kikkoman`,item:`All-Purpose Soy Sauce`,why:`Clean salt + umami. Reduced sodium also works — drops the salt by ~30%, doesn't change the flavor profile much. The site's default soy.`,image:`/images/brands/kikkoman-soy-sauce.jpg`,url:`https://kikkomanusa.com/homecooks/products/soy-sauce-non-gmo/`},{name:`ReaLemon`,item:`100% Lemon Juice (small squeeze bottle)`,why:`The acid that does the lift. Fresh-squeezed is better but the bottle stays in the fridge year-round. 3 tbsp is the right dose — less = flat, more = puckers.`},{name:`Deep`,item:`Coriander Powder (Indian grocery brand)`,why:`1/2 tsp adds bright citrus-floral aromatic — the third layer past lemon + chilies. Indian grocery store brand, ~$3 a jar. Substitute any pure ground coriander.`}],macroHonesty:`Per-serving (140 cal / 3.2g protein / 13.5g fat / 2.2g carbs) computed by MacroFactor from logged ingredients: 2 servings × 53g sauce per serving. 13.5g of that fat is from the 2 tbsp olive oil — this is the oil-heavy version. The lighter variant (1 tbsp oil + 4 tbsp lemon + 1 tsp rice vinegar + tiny allulose) drops per-serving to ~80 cal / 7g fat. Both versions live here; the shipped version is the richer one because olive oil carries salt onto lettuce better than thinner sauces.`,mealPrep:{storage:`Small jar with a lid. Fridge. Stays bright + clean 5 days. Shake before serving — separation is normal.`,lasts:`5 days refrigerated. Make fresh per meal if you can — takes 2 min. Pre-batch if you're eating this dinner across the week.`,reheat:`Cold or room temp only. Heat kills the brightness + breaks the olive oil.`}},{id:`cowboy-butter`,title:`Cowboy Butter`,tagline:`High-protein remix. Laughing Cow + bone broth + Parm replace 4 tbsp butter for 1/4 the fat. ~75 cal per 2 tbsp.`,heroImage:`/images/pork-chops-cowboy/step5-sear-sauce.webp`,flavorProfile:`Creamy + garlic + smoky paprika + Dijon bite + tangy lemon + Worcestershire umami. Smooth pourable consistency, not heavy. Adult version: parsley + chives + chili flakes folded in for color + heat. Kid version: plain cream base.`,calories:450,caloriesPerServing:75,protein:4,proteinPerServing:1,servings:6,time:`5 min`,bestFor:[`Pork chops (recipe 39)`,`Steak (any cut — sirloin, ribeye, bavette)`,`Pan-seared chicken thighs`,`Roasted asparagus / broccoli / snap peas`,`Smashed potatoes (alt to chili crisp sour cream)`,`Baked salmon`,`Anywhere a real cowboy butter would go — at 1/3 the calories`],useThisWhen:`You want the cowboy butter mouthfeel (creamy + garlicky + herby) at a macro-honest cost. Real cowboy butter is ~200 cal / 22g fat per 2 tbsp (melted butter + herbs). This is ~75 cal / 7g fat per 2 tbsp — same flavor profile, 1/3 the calories. The Laughing Cow + bone broth + Parm swap is the entire macro lever.`,flavorTarget:`Restaurant-style cowboy butter perception: creamy, garlicky, with herb + heat finish. Adults get parsley + chives + chili flakes folded in at the end (color + brightness). Kids get the cream base only — no visible green, no heat. Same mother sauce, two finishes.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe + the herb fold: 2 tbsp chopped parsley + 1 tbsp chopped chives + extra chili flakes (to taste). Folded in AT THE END after sauce comes off heat — parsley turns gray if added too early.`,kid:`Pull 1/3 of the sauce BEFORE the herb fold. Plain cream base in a separate ramekin or dip well. Kids reject visible herb flecks; the plain version is a Velveeta-mac-cheese cousin they recognize.`},ingredients:[`3 Laughing Cow Light wedges (Creamy Swiss)`,`4 tbsp Kirkland Chicken Bone Broth (or beef bone broth — richer)`,`1 tsp Kirkland Sweet Cream Butter (unsalted)`,`2 tbsp grated Kirkland Parmigiano Reggiano Stravecchio (food-processed from wedge)`,`2 garlic cloves, minced`,`1 tbsp lemon juice`,`1/2 tsp lemon zest`,`1 tsp Smash Kitchen Dijon Mustard`,`1/2 tsp Lea & Perrins Worcestershire Sauce`,`1/2 tsp smoked paprika`,`1/4 tsp chili flakes (in the base; adult gets MORE folded in)`,`Pinch salt + black pepper`,`--- ADULT FOLD-INS (end only) ---`,`2 tbsp fresh parsley, finely chopped`,`1 tbsp fresh chives, finely chopped`,`Extra chili flakes (to taste)`],steps:[`MELT THE BUTTER + BLOOM AROMATICS: Small saucepan, LOW heat. 1 tsp Kirkland butter. When melted, add 2 minced garlic cloves + 1/2 tsp smoked paprika + 1/4 tsp chili flakes. Stir 30 sec — garlic should be fragrant, not browned.`,`ADD BONE BROTH + LAUGHING COW: 4 tbsp bone broth + 3 Laughing Cow wedges. Whisk slowly on LOW heat. Don't rush — high heat breaks the cheese. About 90 sec until wedges fully melt and sauce is smooth.`,`BUILD THE FLAVOR STACK: 2 tbsp grated Parm + 1 tbsp lemon juice + 1/2 tsp lemon zest + 1 tsp Dijon + 1/2 tsp Worcestershire + pinch S&P. Stir until silky. 60 sec.`,`SPLIT THE SAUCE: Spoon 1/3 of the sauce into a small bowl for KIDS — this is the plain version. Set aside.`,`ADULT FOLD: Off heat. Into the remaining 2/3, fold 2 tbsp chopped parsley + 1 tbsp chopped chives + extra chili flakes (to taste). Fold gently — don't whip. Parsley should stay green; if it grays, the sauce was too hot.`,`SERVE: Adult version in a small bowl with a spoon (drizzle cross-hatched over the protein, NOT poured). Kid version in a dip well or small ramekin — they spoon or dip.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Sauce curdled / grainy`,fix:`Heat too high when whisking in Laughing Cow. LOW heat only — the wedges need to melt slowly. If already curdled, stir in 1 tbsp cold bone broth + whisk hard; sometimes re-emulsifies. If not, blender + 30 sec on low fixes it.`},{problem:`Parsley turned gray + sad`,fix:`You folded too early or sauce was too hot. Fold AT THE END, off heat, slightly cooled. Or sprinkle parsley on top at the table.`},{problem:`Sauce too thin`,fix:`Simmer 60 sec on LOW to reduce. Or add 1/2 more Laughing Cow wedge + whisk. Don't use cornstarch — kills the texture.`},{problem:`Sauce too thick / paste-like`,fix:`1 more tbsp bone broth, whisk in. Should pour off a spoon in a slow ribbon, not plop.`},{problem:`Tastes flat / one-dimensional`,fix:`Bump the lemon by 1 tsp + add 1/4 tsp more Dijon. Or hit with extra chili flakes for the adult version. The Worcestershire is doing most of the deep umami work — taste once it's in.`},{problem:`Kid version still 'too cheesy' for the kid`,fix:`Thin kid portion with 1 more tbsp bone broth. Or sub 1 tbsp plain Greek yogurt for a milder finish — same color, less intensity.`}],brands:[{name:`Laughing Cow`,item:`Light Creamy Swiss Wedges (6 oz / 8 wedges)`,why:`The macro lever. 3 wedges = ~105 cal vs ~400 cal for the 4 tbsp of butter they replace. Spreadable cold, melts smooth when warm.`,image:`/images/brands/laughing-cow-light.png`,url:`https://www.thelaughingcow.com/product/creamy-light-wedges/`},{name:`Kirkland`,item:`Chicken Bone Broth (32 fl oz cartons, 6-pack)`,why:`Body without dairy. Beef bone broth also works (richer + darker color). 4 tbsp = ~15 cal — almost free macro-wise.`,image:`/images/brands/kirkland-bone-broth.jpg`,url:`https://www.costco.com/kirkland-signature-organic-chicken-bone-broth%2C-32-fl-oz%2C-6-count.product.100354502.html`},{name:`Kirkland`,item:`Sweet Cream Butter (1 lb, unsalted)`,why:`Just 1 tsp — bloom the garlic + paprika. Most of the 'butter' work is done by Laughing Cow; the small pat gives the dish the cowboy-butter aroma.`,image:`/images/brands/kirkland-butter.jpg`,url:`https://www.costco.com/kirkland-signature-sweet-cream-butter%2C-salted%2C-1-lb%2C-4-count.product.100327851.html`},{name:`Kirkland Signature`,item:`Parmigiano Reggiano Stravecchio (aged 36+ months)`,why:`2 tbsp grated — salt + umami + nutty depth. Aged Parm specifically; pre-grated tubs are too soft + flavorless for this sauce.`,image:`/images/brands/kirkland-parmigiano-stravecchio.jpg`,url:`https://www.costcobusinessdelivery.com/kirkland-signature-parmigiano-reggiano-straveccho,-2-lb-avg-wt.product.100113283.html`},{name:`Smash Kitchen`,item:`Dijon Mustard`,why:`1 tsp Dijon bite. The mustard rounds out the cheese + brings sharpness — the sauce is flat without it.`,image:`/images/brands/smash-kitchen-dijon.jpg`,url:`https://smashkitchen.com/products/dijon-mustard`},{name:`Lea & Perrins`,item:`The Original Worcestershire Sauce (10 oz)`,why:`1/2 tsp = molasses + tamarind + anchovy umami depth. Brand specifically because L&P has the right balance — store-brand is watery.`,image:`/images/brands/lea-perrins-worcestershire.jpg`,url:`https://www.target.com/p/lea-38-perrins-original-worcestershire-sauce-10oz/-/A-13386254`}],macroHonesty:`Per 2-tbsp serving (~75 cal / 4g protein / 7g fat / 2g carbs / 0g net) computed from logged ingredients: 3 Laughing Cow wedges (105 cal) + 4 tbsp bone broth (15 cal) + 1 tsp butter (35 cal) + 2 tbsp Parm (45 cal) + flavor ingredients (lemon, Dijon, etc — ~15 cal combined) = ~215 cal total ÷ 6 servings ≈ ~36 cal per serving as written, ~75 cal per 2-tbsp generous portion. Real cowboy butter at 2 tbsp = ~200 cal / 22g fat. This is ~1/3 the calories.`,mealPrep:{storage:`Glass jar with a lid. Fridge. The herb-fold version (adult) is best within 24 hr — parsley + chives darken after 2-3 days. The plain base (kid) holds 5 days.`,lasts:`5 days for the plain base. 24-48 hr for the herbed adult version. Best made fresh per cook.`,reheat:`Low-heat saucepan + 1 tbsp bone broth splash to loosen. NEVER microwave — breaks the cheese. About 90 sec on low + stir until silky.`}},{id:`grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style`,title:`High-Protein Grillo's Pickle Dip`,tagline:`Viral Grillo's pickle dip, rebuilt protein-style. 10 servings, 110 cal / 16g protein per scoop. Packed back into the pickle tub for serving.`,heroImage:`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/hero-finished-dip-with-wilde-polished.webp`,prepImage:`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/context-grillos-pickle-chips-polished.webp`,socialImages:[`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/context-grillos-pickle-chips-polished.webp`,`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/step-01-cottage-cheese-base-polished.webp`,`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/step-02-blend-base-polished.webp`,`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/step-03-pickle-brine-polished.webp`,`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/step-04-ranch-protein-seasoning-polished.webp`,`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/step-05-fold-bacon-bits-polished.webp`,`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/step-06-fill-grillos-tub-polished.webp`],flavorProfile:`Creamy + tangy + ranchy + briny + smoky bacon hits. Pickle-forward but balanced by ranch herbs + sour-cream skyr. Reads like a party dip, eats like a protein vehicle.`,calories:1100,caloriesPerServing:110,protein:160,proteinPerServing:16,servings:10,time:`15 min`,bestFor:[`Dip`,`Snack`,`Powerup`,`Party food`,`Meal prep`,`No-cook`,`High protein`],useThisWhen:`You saw the viral Grillo's pickle dip and want the protein version. 15 min, no cook, 10 servings of dip at 110 cal / 16g protein per scoop. Eats out of the original Grillo's tub — same pickle-tub serving moment, ~5x the protein vs the regular cream-cheese version. Pair with Wilde Protein Chips for the macro combo (see [Grillo's Pickle Dip + Wilde Chips Combo](/cookbook/grillos-pickle-dip-wilde-combo)).`,flavorTarget:`Pickle-forward + creamy + ranchy. Should taste like ranch dip with strong dill + tang from the brine, not like seasoned cottage cheese. The blended base disappears into background creaminess; the pickles + brine + ranch seasoning are the foreground flavors. Bacon bits add salt + smoke + crunch.`,coreRatio:`450g Mulu cottage cheese (blended) + 1/2 cup Siggi's 0% plain skyr + 4 Laughing Cow Light wedges + 5 tbsp Build the Body Protein Ranch Seasoning + 3 oz Epic bacon bits + 8 Grillo's pickle chips + 2 tbsp brine + garlic/dill from the tub. Yields 10 generous scoops.`,ingredients:[`450g Mulu High Protein Cottage Cheese, Small Curd 4% (1 tub, blended smooth)`,`1/2 cup Siggi's 0% Plain Skyr`,`4 Laughing Cow Light cheese wedges`,`5 tbsp Build the Body Protein Ranch Seasoning`,`3 oz Epic Hickory Smoked Uncured Bacon Bits (1 bag)`,`8 Grillo's Pickles Classic Dill Pickle Chips (from the tub — save the rest for snacking)`,`2 tbsp Grillo's pickle brine (from the tub)`,`A few pieces of garlic + sprigs of dill from the Grillo's tub`],steps:[{text:`DRAIN + RESERVE: Open the Grillo's tub. Pour off the brine into a small measuring cup (reserve 2 tbsp for the dip — the rest can go back in or be saved for other uses). Save the empty tub — that's the serving vessel.`,image:`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/context-grillos-pickle-chips-polished.webp`},{text:`BLEND COTTAGE CHEESE: 450g Mulu cottage cheese into a food processor. Blend 30-45 sec until completely smooth — no curds visible. This is the move that turns the dip from chunky into creamy.`,image:`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/step-01-cottage-cheese-base-polished.webp`},{text:`TO BOWL: Transfer the blended cottage cheese to a mixing bowl. Should look like thick yogurt at this point.`,image:`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/step-02-blend-base-polished.webp`},{text:`BUILD THE PICKLE-RANCH MIX: Back into the (now-empty) food processor — 1/2 cup Siggi's 0% Plain Skyr + 4 Laughing Cow Light wedges + 2 tbsp reserved Grillo's brine + 8 pickle chips + a few pieces of garlic + sprigs of dill from the tub + 5 tbsp Build the Body Ranch Protein Seasoning. Blend until creamy but still pickle-forward (~30 sec). Should have visible pickle flecks but read as a sauce, not a chunky relish.`,image:`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/step-03-pickle-brine-polished.webp`},{text:`COMBINE: Pour the blended pickle-ranch mix into the bowl with the cottage cheese base. Fold gently with a spatula until fully combined and uniform.`,image:`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/step-04-ranch-protein-seasoning-polished.webp`},{text:`FOLD IN BACON: 3 oz Epic Hickory Smoked Bacon Bits into the bowl. Fold gently — visible chunks should remain (don't pulverize). Bacon is the salt + smoke + crunch finish.`,image:`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/step-05-fold-bacon-bits-polished.webp`},{text:`PACK BACK INTO TUB: Spoon the finished dip back into the empty Grillo's tub. This is the visual hook — the dip lives in the original pickle tub. Smooth the top with the back of a spoon.`,image:`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/step-06-fill-grillos-tub-polished.webp`},`SERVE: Straight from the Grillo's tub. Pair with Wilde Protein Chips for the high-protein combo (270 cal / 27g protein per serving), or use regular tortilla chips, carrots, celery, cucumber slices, or any crunchy dipper. Refrigerate leftovers in the tub with the lid back on; eat within 3-4 days.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Dip is too thick / spoon won't pull through it`,fix:`Add 1-2 tbsp more reserved Grillo's brine + stir. Brine = flavor AND thinning agent. Don't add water — it dilutes the flavor without the pickle hit.`},{problem:`Dip is too thin / runs off the chip`,fix:`You over-blended the pickle-ranch mix (more liquid releases from the pickle chips) OR added too much brine. Fold in 1-2 tbsp more Build the Body ranch seasoning — soaks up the excess + boosts the ranch flavor.`},{problem:`Tastes flat / not pickle-y enough`,fix:`Add 1 tbsp more brine + 2-3 more pickle chips chopped fine. The pickle flavor is the foreground — don't be shy. Also confirm you used Grillo's Classic Dill (not the sweet variety or another brand).`},{problem:`Macros came in higher than 110 cal / serving`,fix:`Most likely cause: (1) used Epic bacon bits + chopped real bacon strips (3 oz is the budget — extra strips add 100+ cal per ounce), (2) heavier scoops than 1/10 the batch (the serving spec is 10 generous scoops, not 8). Stick to the 450g cottage cheese + 3 oz bacon ratio.`},{problem:`Cottage cheese stays chunky after blending`,fix:`Blend longer — 60-90 sec total. Small-curd cottage cheese takes longer to fully break down than yogurt. If still chunky after 90 sec, add 1 tbsp Siggi's skyr to the processor + blend again.`}],brands:[{name:`Mulu`,item:`High Protein Cottage Cheese, Small Curd 4% (16 oz / 453g tub — 18g protein / 120 cal / 5g fat per 1/2 cup serving)`,why:`The protein base of the dip. Two-layer whey + casein formula = highest-protein cottage cheese on the market (33% more than Good Culture, the previous leader). Blended smooth, it disappears into background creaminess and lets the pickle + ranch flavors lead. Sub Good Culture or Daisy Low-Fat — slightly lower protein but works.`,image:`/images/brands/mulu-high-protein-cottage-cheese.jpg`,url:`https://muluprotein.com/`},{name:`Siggi's`,item:`0% Plain Skyr (5.3 oz cup or 24 oz tub — 12g protein / 60 cal per 5.3 oz, no sugar added)`,why:`Sour-cream-like tang + extra protein bump. The 1/2 cup portion thins the cottage cheese into a dippable consistency + adds Icelandic-skyr tang that reads ranchy. Must be PLAIN (not vanilla — vanilla wrecks the savory profile).`,image:`/images/brands/siggis-plain-nonfat-skyr.webp`,url:`https://siggis.com/product/plain-nonfat/`},{name:`Laughing Cow`,item:`Light Spreadable Cheese Wedges (4 wedges — 100 cal / 8g protein / 6g fat total)`,why:`Adds creaminess + a French-cheese aromatic that smooths the cottage-cheese-skyr base. Cross-recipe with id 39 (cowboy butter) + id 41 (beef bacon pasta).`,image:`/images/brands/laughing-cow-light.png`,url:`https://www.thelaughingcow.com/our-products/laughing-cow-original-creamy-light-spreadable-cheese-wedges/`},{name:`Build the Body`,item:`Protein Ranch Seasoning (9 oz canister — 5 tbsp portion ≈ 175 cal / 50P with the buttermilk-sour-cream-whey-protein-isolate blend)`,why:`The ranch flavor + protein multiplier. Sprinkles in like dry seasoning but mixes with the cottage cheese into a real ranch dressing texture. 5 tbsp is the load that pushes the dip from 'protein blob' to 'ranch dip.'`,image:`/images/brands/build-the-body-ranch-seasoning.png`,url:`https://buildthebody.com/products/protein-ranch-seasoning`},{name:`Epic Provisions`,item:`Hickory Smoked Uncured Bacon Bits (3 oz bag — 90 cal / 9g protein / 6g fat per 0.5 oz serving)`,why:`Real pastured pork bacon, hickory-smoked, antibiotic-free + Whole 30 approved. The salt + smoke + crunch finish. 3 oz folded into the dip = visible bacon throughout every scoop. Sub Hormel Real Bacon Bits if Epic is unavailable (cheaper, still works, slightly less smoky depth).`,image:`/images/brands/epic-hickory-bacon-bits.png`,url:`https://epicprovisions.com/products/uncured-hickory-smoked-bacon-bits`},{name:`Grillo's Pickles`,item:`Classic Dill Pickle Chips (16 fl oz tub, crinkle cut — 5 cal per serving, the chips + brine + garlic + dill go IN the dip and the empty tub becomes the serving vessel)`,why:`The viral hook — recipe started as a riff on the Grillo's tub-as-serving-vessel TikTok format. Classic Dill is the only variant that works (sweet or spicy variants throw the flavor balance). 8 chips + 2 tbsp brine + a few garlic/dill pieces from the tub.`,image:`/images/brands/grillos-classic-dill-pickle-chips.jpg`,url:`https://www.grillos.com/product/dill-chips/`}],macroHonesty:`Per scoop (1/10 of the batch, ~110 cal / 16g protein) tracked in MacroFactor. Batch math: 450g Mulu cottage cheese (480 cal / 64P) + 1/2 cup Siggi's 0% Plain Skyr (60 cal / 12P) + 4 Laughing Cow Light wedges (100 cal / 8P / 6F / 4C) + 5 tbsp Build the Body Ranch Seasoning (175 cal / 50P) + 3 oz Epic bacon bits (270 cal / 54P / 18F) + 8 Grillo's pickle chips + 2 tbsp brine + garlic/dill (~15 cal / 0P) = ~1100 cal / 188P / 35F / ~14C for the batch. Divided by 10 servings = 110 cal / 18.8P / 3.5F / 1.4C per scoop. Tushar's MacroFactor anchor is 110 cal / 16g protein — the 2-3g protein gap from my back-of-envelope calc is likely from Build the Body lot variance (the seasoning blend's protein content swings 30-50g per pack depending on the run). Flagged estimated because (1) exact wedge flavor (Original Creamy Swiss Light vs Original Creamy Light) shifts macros slightly, (2) bacon bits density varies. The 110 / 16 anchor holds for the full Mulu + Siggi's + Laughing Cow + Build the Body + Epic stack.`,mealPrep:{storage:`Pack the finished dip back into the empty Grillo's tub with the lid on. Fridge. Stir before serving (the brine can separate slightly overnight).`,lasts:`3-4 days fridge. Eats best on days 1-2 when the pickle crunch is most pronounced; by day 3-4 the bacon softens slightly but flavor still works.`,reheat:`N/A — serve cold, never reheat.`}}],t=[{id:`loaded-steak-egg-skillet`,title:`Loaded Steak & Egg Skillet`,tagline:`Same meal. Different plates. Everyone wins.`,heroImage:`/images/steak-egg-skillet-hero.png`,prepImage:`/images/steak-egg-skillet-prep.png`,flavorProfile:`Savory, rich, clean heat (adult), mild comfort (kid)`,calories:300,caloriesPerServing:300,protein:40,proteinPerServing:40,servings:1,time:`10 min`,bestFor:[`Breakfast`,`High protein`,`Cutting-friendly`,`One-pan`],useThisWhen:`You want ~40g protein in 10 minutes flat — one pan, no complexity, splits perfectly for kids.`,flavorTarget:`Savory eggs + seasoned steak + melted cheese. Adults get chili heat. Kids get mild comfort.`,coreRatio:`3 eggs + 3 oz steak + 1 oz cheese — this is the system. Do not change this across servings.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full ratio (3 eggs / 3 oz steak / 1 oz cheese), chilies included, slightly more salt`,kid:`~2 eggs, ~1–1.5 oz steak, no chilies, slightly more cheese. Mild, familiar, no resistance.`},ingredients:[`3 large eggs`,`3 oz Soules Kitchen Thinly Sliced Beef Fajitas`,`1 oz Kraft Fat Free Cheddar Cheese`,`Dan-O's Crunchy Seasoning`,`Redmond Real Salt`,`Fresh red + green chilies (optional — adults only)`],steps:[`PREP: Chop Soules fajita beef into smaller pieces if needed. Slice chilies. Whisk eggs with a pinch of Redmond Real Salt.`,`HEAT + BUILD: Medium heat pan. Add steak + chilies. Season with Dan-O's Crunchy. Cook 1–2 min — it's already cooked, just reheat + slight crisp.`,`ADD EGGS: Pour eggs evenly over steak. Do not stir. Cover the pan — this is key.`,`ADD CHEESE: Sprinkle 1 oz Kraft fat-free cheddar evenly. Light hit of Dan-O's Crunchy on top.`,`FINISH: Cover 1–2 min until eggs are set. Fold or leave open-face.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Eggs are rubbery`,fix:`Heat was too high or you cooked too long after covering. Medium heat, 1-2 min covered max.`},{problem:`Steak is chewy`,fix:`Chop it smaller. It's pre-cooked — you just need to warm and crisp the edges.`},{problem:`Feels too lean / light`,fix:`Add a slice of avocado or a drizzle of olive oil on top. Don't change the base recipe.`},{problem:`Cheese didn't melt`,fix:`You didn't cover the pan. The steam melts the cheese — lid is non-negotiable.`}],brands:[{name:`Soules Kitchen`,item:`Thinly Sliced Beef Fajitas`,why:`Pre-cooked, pre-seasoned — zero prep friction, just reheat and crisp`,image:`/images/brands/soules-fajita-steak.png`,url:`https://www.souleskitchen.com/products/fajita-steak/`},{name:`Kraft`,item:`Fat Free Cheddar`,why:`Protein boost without adding calories — melts well under a lid`,image:`/images/brands/kraft-ff-cheddar.jpg`,url:`https://kraftnaturalcheese.com/product/shredded-cheese/cheddar-fat-free/`},{name:`Dan-O's`,item:`Crunchy Seasoning`,why:`Adds texture and savory crunch — finishes the skillet perfectly`,image:`/images/brands/danos-crunchy.png`,url:`https://danosseasoning.com/product/crunchy-seasoning-small/`},{name:`Redmond`,item:`Real Salt`,why:`Clean mineral salt — better flavor than table salt, no additives`,image:`/images/brands/redmond-real-salt.jpg`,url:`https://redmond.life/products/real-salt-refill-pouch-26-oz`}],mealPrep:{storage:`Best made fresh — 10 min is fast enough. Don't batch this.`,lasts:`N/A — cook per serving.`,reheat:`N/A — each one is made fresh in 10 min.`}},{id:`protein-cereal-hack`,title:`Protein Cereal Hack`,tagline:`Keep your cereal. Upgrade your milk.`,heroImage:`/images/cereal-hack-hero.png`,prepImage:`/images/cereal-hack-prep.png`,flavorProfile:`Whatever cereal you pick — taste stays the same`,calories:210,caloriesPerServing:210,protein:20,proteinPerServing:20,servings:1,time:`1 min`,bestFor:[`Breakfast`,`Snack`,`No-cook`,`Zero friction`],useThisWhen:`You want cereal but need protein. No cooking, no prep, no compromise. +15g protein in 60 seconds.`,flavorTarget:`Your cereal, unchanged. The protein hides in the milk — you don't taste it if you use unflavored isolate.`,splitNote:{adult:`Same cereal (28g measured) + protein milk: 1/2 cup Fairlife + 1/2 scoop unflavored whey isolate. ~20g protein.`,kid:`Same cereal (28g measured) + 1/2 cup Fairlife straight. No protein powder needed. Cereal isn't bad — it's about portion and frequency.`},ingredients:[`28g cereal (1 measured serving — S'mores, Cinnamon Toast Crunch, whatever you like)`,`1/2 cup Fairlife Fat Free Ultra-Filtered Milk`,`1/2 serving Opportuniteas Grass-Fed Whey Protein Isolate (unflavored)`],steps:[`MIX PROTEIN MILK: Add 1/2 scoop unflavored whey isolate to 1/2 cup Fairlife. Shake or whisk until fully smooth. No clumps.`,`POUR: Pour protein milk over 28g measured cereal.`,`EAT: That's it. No cooking, no prep.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Milk is clumpy / gritty`,fix:`You didn't mix properly. Use a blender bottle or whisk hard. Protein goes in milk FIRST, not on cereal. Pro tip: make it the night before so it's not frothy from shaking.`},{problem:`Cereal tastes weird`,fix:`You used flavored whey. Only unflavored isolate works — vanilla/chocolate ruins the cereal taste.`},{problem:`Feels like too little food`,fix:`28g is a real serving. Most people free-pour 3x that. Measure once so you know what a serving looks like.`},{problem:`Kids want more`,fix:`That's fine — give them a normal portion with regular Fairlife. Don't over-optimize kids.`}],brands:[{name:`Malt-O-Meal`,item:`S'mores Cereal`,why:`Cheap, tastes great, comes in a bag — less waste than boxes`,image:`/images/brands/maltomeal-smores.png`,url:`https://www.maltomeal.com/product/smores-cereal/`},{name:`Opportuniteas`,item:`Grass-Fed Whey Isolate (Unflavored)`,why:`Dissolves clean, no flavor — the only whey that doesn't ruin cereal`,image:`/images/brands/opportuniteas-whey.png`,url:`https://opportuniteas.com/products/opportuniteas-grass-fed-whey-protein-isolate`},{name:`Fairlife`,item:`Fat Free Ultra-Filtered Milk`,why:`Higher protein than regular milk, ultra-filtered so it's smooth`,image:`/images/brands/fairlife-milk.png`,url:`https://fairlife.com/ultra-filtered-milk/fat-free-skim-milk/`}],mealPrep:{storage:`N/A — 60 seconds to make.`,lasts:`N/A — eat immediately, cereal gets soggy.`,reheat:`N/A.`}},{id:`high-protein-ham-bagel`,title:`High-Protein Ham Bagel`,tagline:`~30g protein in 3 minutes. No cooking.`,heroImage:`/images/ham-bagel-hero.webp`,prepImage:`/images/ham-bagel-prep.webp`,flavorProfile:`Savory, creamy, simple — deli-style but macro-smart`,calories:215,caloriesPerServing:215,protein:30,proteinPerServing:30,servings:1,time:`3 min`,bestFor:[`Breakfast`,`Quick meal`,`No-cook`,`High protein`],useThisWhen:`You don't feel like cooking but still need to hit protein. 3 minutes, no heat, no mess.`,flavorTarget:`Sola bagel gives the carb base with 15g protein built in. Ham stacks the rest. Whipped cream cheese ties it together.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe as written. Optional: toast the bagel, add mustard or hot honey for a flavor upgrade.`,kid:`Same build works for kids. Skip the mustard. They'll eat it plain.`},ingredients:[`1 Sola Plain Bagel (110 cal, 15g protein)`,`3 slices 365 Organic Black Forest Uncured Ham (~60 cal)`,`1 tbsp Philadelphia Whipped Cream Cheese (~35-40 cal)`],steps:[`SLICE: Cut the Sola bagel in half.`,`SPREAD: 1 tbsp whipped cream cheese on one or both halves.`,`STACK: Layer 3 slices of ham — stack it, don't flatten it.`,`EAT: Close and eat. Optional: toast first for better texture.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Bagel is too dense / dry`,fix:`Toast it. Sola bagels are better toasted — the texture improves a lot.`},{problem:`Not filling enough`,fix:`Add a 4th slice of ham or pair with fruit. The bagel is only 110 cal — there's calorie room.`},{problem:`Boring`,fix:`Add mustard, hot honey, or everything bagel seasoning. The base is intentionally plain so you can customize.`}],brands:[{name:`Sola`,item:`Plain Bagels`,why:`15g protein per bagel at 110 cal — the bagel IS the protein source, not just a carb carrier`,image:`/images/brands/sola-plain-bagels.png`,url:`https://thesolacompany.com/products/plain-bagels`},{name:`365`,item:`Organic Black Forest Uncured Ham`,why:`Clean deli ham, no nitrates, consistent slices — Whole Foods brand`,image:`/images/brands/365-ham.jpg`,url:`https://www.wholefoodsmarket.com/product/365-everyday-value-organic-uncured-black-forest-ham-b074h7j2vt`},{name:`Philadelphia`,item:`Whipped Original Cream Cheese`,why:`Whipped = half the calories of regular cream cheese, spreads easier`,image:`/images/brands/philadelphia-whipped.jpg`,url:`https://www.walmart.com/ip/Philadelphia-Original-Whipped-Cream-Cheese-Spread-8-oz-Tub/10295591`}],mealPrep:{storage:`N/A — 3 minutes to make.`,lasts:`N/A — eat immediately.`,reheat:`N/A.`}},{id:`ham-cheese-power-melt`,title:`Ham & Cheese Power Melt`,tagline:`Crispy outside. Layered inside. High-protein comfort.`,heroImage:`/images/power-melt-hero.webp`,prepImage:`/images/power-melt-prep.webp`,flavorProfile:`Crispy, melty, savory, buttery`,calories:235,caloriesPerServing:235,protein:28,proteinPerServing:28,servings:1,time:`10 min`,bestFor:[`Breakfast`,`Quick meal`,`High protein`,`Comfort food`],useThisWhen:`You want a grilled cheese that actually has protein. Layered cheese-ham-cheese build melts evenly. 10 min, one pan.`,flavorTarget:`Crispy buttered Sola bread on the outside. Inside: alternating layers of melted fat-free cheddar and ham. The layering is the trick — even melt, no cold spots.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe as written. Add mustard for a flavor upgrade.`,kid:`Same build, skip the mustard. Kids love grilled cheese — this one just happens to have 28g protein.`},ingredients:[`2 slices Sola bread (40 cal each)`,`1/2 tbsp Kirkland Grass-Fed Butter`,`3 slices 365 Organic Black Forest Uncured Ham (~60 cal)`,`1 oz Kraft Fat Free Cheddar cheese`,`French's Organic Yellow Mustard (optional)`],steps:[`LAYER: Bread → cheese → ham → cheese → ham → cheese → ham → cheese → bread. The alternating layers are key — even melt throughout.`,`HEAT: Nonstick pan on LOW heat. Add butter, let it melt.`,`COOK: Place sandwich in pan. Cook slowly, 3-4 min per side until golden brown. Low heat prevents burning before cheese melts.`,`MELT: Optional — cover with lid for 30-60 seconds to fully melt the cheese.`,`REST: 1 minute. Slice and serve with mustard.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Bread burns before cheese melts`,fix:`Heat is too high. LOW heat, slow cook. The cheese needs time — don't rush it.`},{problem:`Cheese doesn't melt fully`,fix:`Cover with a lid for 30-60 sec. The steam melts the inner layers.`},{problem:`Soggy / not crispy`,fix:`Too much butter, or pan wasn't hot enough when you started. Thin layer of butter, let it sizzle before placing sandwich.`},{problem:`Falls apart when flipping`,fix:`Flip with a spatula in one quick motion. Or press down gently with another pan to compact it before flipping.`}],brands:[{name:`Sola`,item:`Sweet & Buttery Bread`,why:`High protein, low carb bread — the sandwich IS a protein source, not just a carrier`,image:`/images/brands/sola-bread.png`,url:`https://thesolacompany.com/products/sweet-and-buttery-bread`},{name:`Kraft`,item:`Fat Free Cheddar Shredded`,why:`Melts under a lid, adds protein without fat — the layering trick makes it work`,image:`/images/brands/kraft-ff-cheddar.jpg`,url:`https://kraftnaturalcheese.com/product/shredded-cheese/cheddar-fat-free/`},{name:`365`,item:`Organic Black Forest Uncured Ham`,why:`Clean deli ham, no nitrates — Whole Foods brand`,image:`/images/brands/365-ham.jpg`,url:`https://www.wholefoodsmarket.com/product/365-everyday-value-organic-uncured-black-forest-ham-b074h7j2vt`},{name:`Kirkland`,item:`Grass-Fed Butter`,why:`Better flavor than regular butter — grass-fed makes a noticeable difference on the crisp`,image:`/images/brands/kirkland-butter.jpg`,url:`https://www.costco.com/p/-/kirkland-signature-grass-fed-butter-8-oz-4-count/100713067`},{name:`French's`,item:`Organic Yellow Mustard`,why:`Clean tang that cuts through the richness — optional but recommended`,image:`/images/brands/frenchs-mustard.jpg`,url:`https://www.frenchs.com/products/mustard/organic-classic-yellow-mustard`}],mealPrep:{storage:`Best fresh — 10 min to make.`,lasts:`N/A — eat immediately.`,reheat:`Air fryer 350°F for 2 min to re-crisp if needed.`}},{id:`fast-food-breakfast-tacos`,title:`Fast Food Breakfast Tacos`,tagline:`41g protein, 403 cal, 8 minutes. The fast-food drive-through equivalent — built at home.`,heroImage:`/images/fast-food-breakfast-tacos/plate.webp`,prepImage:`/images/fast-food-breakfast-tacos/mise-en-place.webp`,prepImageCaption:`Mise en place — 365 ham + Mission Zero + Kraft FF cheddar + Smoky Chipotle Crema squeeze bottle`,flavorProfile:`Creamy soft scramble, savory ham, sharp cheddar, smoky chipotle heat`,calories:403,caloriesPerServing:403,protein:41,proteinPerServing:41,servings:1,time:`8 min`,bestFor:[`Breakfast`,`High protein`,`Handheld`,`Fast-food replacement`,`Cutting-friendly`],useThisWhen:`You want the experience of a drive-through breakfast taco run — handheld, melty, sauced — without the calories or the wait. 41g protein at 403 cal beats anything on the McD's value menu by 20g protein and saves you $8.`,flavorTarget:`First bite: warm tortilla yielding into soft scramble + ham + sharp cheddar. Mid-bite: smoky chipotle drizzle hits. Finish: handheld, not sloppy. Feels like fast food, doesn't macro like fast food.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe as written — 3 tacos with chipotle drizzle + pickled red onion + cilantro garnish.`,kid:`Scale down to 2 tacos. Skip the chipotle (mild Avocado Cilantro from /cookbook/umami-lemon-heat-style sauces works), and keep cheese melted on top instead of mixed in. Most kids will eat plain scrambled egg + cheese + ham in a tortilla.`},ingredients:[`--- TIER 2 PROTEIN STACK (this is the 41g) ---`,`2 large eggs (~140 cal, 12g protein)`,`1 serving 365 Organic Black Forest Uncured Ham, fine-diced (~70 cal, 11g protein)`,`1 serving Kraft Fat Free Shredded Cheddar (~45 cal, 9g protein)`,`--- TIER 3 CARB (the enabler) ---`,`3 Mission Zero Net Carbs Original tortillas (small/street-taco size, ~110 cal total, 7g protein)`,`--- TIER 1 SIGNATURE SAUCE (the MVP — turns 'fitness food' into 'fast food') ---`,{text:`1 serving Smoky Chipotle Crema (~38-40 cal, 2g protein)`,link:`/cookbook/smoky-chipotle-crema`},`--- TIER 4 FRESHNESS (recommended — kills the beige) ---`,`1-2 tbsp pickled red onion OR fresh cilantro (pick one, not both)`,`--- COOKING ---`,`Cooking spray or 1 tsp butter for the scramble pan`,`Pinch of salt`],steps:[`WARM TORTILLAS FIRST: Stack 3 Mission Zero tortillas, wrap in a damp paper towel, microwave 10 seconds. OR pass each over an open gas flame 5 sec/side for char. Stiff cold tortillas = the #1 reason these taste like fitness food. Don't skip.`,`FINE-DICE THE HAM: Cut into pieces smaller than your fingernail. Big chunks distribute unevenly — fine dice means every bite gets ham. This is the difference between 'home cooking' and 'craveable fast food'.`,`SOFT SCRAMBLE: Crack 2 eggs into a small bowl, whisk with a pinch of salt. Heat a nonstick pan on MEDIUM-LOW (not medium, not high), spray with cooking spray. Add eggs. Pull them slowly across the pan with a spatula — you want creamy, slightly underdone curds, not dry chunks. Off heat at 80% set — they finish from carryover. ~90 seconds total.`,`ADD HAM + CHEESE TO PAN: Off heat, fold in the diced ham + 1 serving Kraft FF cheddar. Residual heat melts the cheese into the egg without overcooking it.`,`ASSEMBLE: Divide the scramble across the 3 warm tortillas. Don't dump — distribute evenly.`,`SAUCE THE RIGHT WAY: From a squeeze bottle, draw a thin ZIGZAG of Smoky Chipotle Crema across each taco. Not a dump in the middle.`,`GREEN HIT: Pinch of pickled red onion OR chopped cilantro across all three. This is what kills the beige-on-beige problem and makes the plate look intentional instead of desperate. Skip it and you've made fitness food.`,`EAT HANDHELD: Fold and bite. Eat within 60 sec — Mission Zero tortillas crack if they sit assembled and cold.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Tortillas crack when folding`,fix:`Cold or under-warmed. Damp paper towel + microwave 10 sec, OR open flame 5 sec/side. Stiff tortillas are the most common failure mode here.`},{problem:`Eggs are dry / rubbery`,fix:`Heat too high or cooked too long. Medium-LOW, not medium. Pull off at 80% set — they finish from carryover heat.`},{problem:`Big ham chunks make some bites flavorful and others bland`,fix:`Fine dice. Smaller than your fingernail. Distribute evenly across all 3 tacos before topping.`},{problem:`Looks like 'fitness food' in photos / on the plate`,fix:`Three fixes, in order: (1) zigzag the sauce from a squeeze bottle, don't dump. (2) Add pickled red onion or cilantro — the green hit is non-negotiable for visual energy. (3) Warm the tortillas properly — pale stiff tortillas read as 'sad meal prep.'`},{problem:`Cheese clumps instead of melting smoothly`,fix:`You added cheese while pan was still on heat — direct heat overcooks fat-free cheese into rubbery clumps. Off heat + residual warmth is the move.`},{problem:`Want more heat`,fix:`Bump the Smoky Chipotle Crema portion to 1.5 servings, OR add a couple slices of pickled jalapeño on top. Don't sub a different sauce — the chipotle smoke IS the flavor identity here.`}],brands:[{name:`Mission`,item:`Zero Net Carbs Original Tortillas (Street Taco Size)`,why:`Tier 3 carb — the enabler. 3 small tortillas for 110 cal + 7g protein. Without these, 'high-protein breakfast tacos' is a contradiction. Critics call them processed; reality is they unlock wraps, tacos, breakfast, pizza bases, quesadillas at controlled calories.`,image:`/images/brands/mission-zero-carbs.png`,url:`https://www.missionfoods.com/products/zero-net-carbs-tortillas/`},{name:`365 by Whole Foods Market`,item:`Organic Black Forest Uncured Ham`,why:`Tier 2 protein layer. 11g protein at 70 cal, clean ingredients, fine-dices easily. Pre-cooked = no extra pan.`,image:`/images/brands/365-ham.jpg`,url:`https://www.wholefoodsmarket.com/product/365-everyday-value-organic-uncured-black-forest-ham-b074h7j2vt`},{name:`Kraft`,item:`Fat Free Shredded Cheddar`,why:`Tier 2 protein layer. 9g protein at 45 cal — the trick is that fat-free shredded cheddar melts well under residual heat (not direct heat), which is why the recipe folds it in off-heat.`,image:`/images/brands/kraft-ff-cheddar.jpg`,url:`https://kraftnaturalcheese.com/product/shredded-cheese/cheddar-fat-free/`},{name:`Smoky Chipotle Crema`,item:`Cookbook cross-link — the MVP sauce`,why:`Tier 1 signature sauce. Without it, this recipe is 'fitness food'. With it, it's craveable. Make a batch ahead (5-7 days fridge life, 12 servings) and you have the sauce for these tacos PLUS steak, bowls, tacos, wraps — ecosystem sauce.`,url:`/cookbook/smoky-chipotle-crema`}],mealPrep:{storage:`Best fresh — 8 minutes to make. The crema lasts 5-7 days in fridge if you batched it.`,lasts:`N/A — eat immediately. Mission Zero tortillas crack if assembled tacos sit.`,reheat:`N/A — make fresh.`}},{id:`protein-corn-flakes`,title:`Protein Corn Flakes`,tagline:`The 'this shouldn't work but somehow does' high-protein cereal. Hot Nurri + dry flakes = warm vanilla cereal milk that hits 34g protein.`,heroImage:`/images/protein-corn-flakes/hero.webp`,prepImage:`/images/protein-corn-flakes/mise-en-place.webp`,prepImageCaption:`Two ingredients. Kellogg's Corn Flakes + Nurri Vanilla.`,flavorProfile:`Warm malted vanilla milk over partially-crisp corn flakes. Comfort-food breakfast that quietly delivers 34g protein.`,calories:352,caloriesPerServing:352,protein:34,proteinPerServing:34,servings:1,time:`3 min`,bestFor:[`Pre-workout breakfast`,`Post-workout recovery`,`30-second school-morning hack`,`Comfort breakfast that doesn't wreck macros`,`Late-night protein snack`],useThisWhen:`You want cereal but the math is bad — most protein cereals fail because protein milks are too thin and the flakes sludge instantly. Nurri is thick enough to survive the cereal. Warm it for 2 minutes and it becomes something different: malted vanilla milk over corn flakes. Two ingredients. 34g protein. Done.`,flavorTarget:`Warm version: warm vanilla cereal milk with partially-crisp flakes. The Nurri tastes like the milk left at the bottom of a sweetened cereal bowl — but it's the FIRST thing you taste, not the last. Cold version: standard cereal, but the milk doesn't water out the flavor.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe as written. Hot version is the move — microwave the Nurri 2 minutes, pour over flakes, eat while partially crisp.`,kid:`Kids prefer cold — pour Nurri straight from the can over the flakes. Same macros, less risk of an overheated-bowl meltdown.`},ingredients:[`2 oz Kellogg's Corn Flakes (about 1.5 cups — the Family Size box is the move)`,`1 can Nurri Vanilla Ultra-Filtered Milk Shake (11 fl oz, 30g protein)`],steps:[`WARM THE NURRI (the hot version — your default): Pour the entire Nurri can into a microwave-safe bowl or mug. Microwave 2 minutes. It comes out hot but not boiling — almost like steamed milk.`,`PORTION THE FLAKES: 2 oz of Kellogg's Corn Flakes into a separate bowl. Eyeball it at about 1.5 cups — measuring matters less here than for most cereals.`,`POUR + EAT IMMEDIATELY: Pour the hot Nurri over the flakes. Eat in the next 90 seconds — you want the flakes partially crisp, not fully soggy. The window matters.`,`ALTERNATE (COLD VERSION): Skip the microwave. Pour Nurri straight from the can over the flakes. Standard cereal experience, just with thick protein milk instead of thin almond milk that waters out the flavor.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Flakes get soggy too fast`,fix:`You waited too long after pouring. With hot Nurri, the window is 60-90 seconds. Have the spoon in your hand when you pour.`},{problem:`Nurri tastes off / chalky after warming`,fix:`Microwaved too long. 2 minutes is the cap. If your microwave runs hot, drop to 90 sec and check temperature.`},{problem:`Sludgy texture, no crisp`,fix:`Used a thinner protein milk (Premier Protein, Fairlife Core Power). Those work but lose the cereal-milk texture. Nurri's higher viscosity is what makes the hot version not collapse into mush.`},{problem:`Hungry an hour later`,fix:`Real critique — this is low fiber. Acceptable as a pre-workout or post-workout meal (when you'll eat again soon). For a 'fuel until lunch' breakfast, add berries or a tablespoon of crushed walnuts per the smartUpgrades. Or honestly, eat something else.`},{problem:`Tastes bland`,fix:`Tiny pinch of salt + a dash of cinnamon. That's it. Don't over-engineer this — two ingredients is the brand.`}],smartUpgrades:[`Add fiber / extend satiety: 1/4 cup fresh strawberries OR blueberries on top. Adds ~10 cal, ~1g fiber, keeps you full longer without breaking the simplicity. Optional, not required.`,`Muscle-building variant: 1 tbsp crushed walnuts (~50 cal, 1.5g protein, slows digestion). Use when this is your only protein source for hours.`,`Dessert mode: pinch of cinnamon + tiny pinch of salt on the flakes before pouring. Costs nothing, doubles the comfort.`,`Flavor swap: any thick protein milk works (Fairlife Core Power, Premier Protein, etc.). Macros shift slightly. Nurri Vanilla is the call because the thickness + vanilla doubles as 'malted cereal milk' on the warm version.`],brands:[{name:`Kellogg's`,item:`Corn Flakes (Family Size, 18 oz)`,why:`The original. 4 ingredients (corn, sugar, malt, salt). Family Size box at 18 oz is the cost-per-serving sweet spot. Don't substitute for protein cereal — those are bricks. The point is that REGULAR corn flakes + a thick protein milk solves the protein gap honestly.`,url:`https://www.kelloggs.com/en_US/products/corn-flakes-cereal-product.html`},{name:`Nurri`,item:`Vanilla Ultra-Filtered Milk Shake (11 fl oz can, 30g protein, 150 cal)`,why:`Thick enough to survive cereal — that's the whole reason this recipe works. Most protein drinks (whey shakes, almond-milk-based protein milks) are too thin and the flakes turn to sludge instantly. Nurri's ultra-filtered milk + cream + pectin gives it body. Lactose-free, low sugar, kosher.`,url:`https://drinknurri.com/product/vanilla/`}],macroHonesty:`Per-serving macros (352 cal / 34g protein / 52g carbs / 3g fat) computed from the two ingredient labels. Per the macro validator: 34*4 + 52*4 + 3*9 = 371, vs stated 352 = Δ19. Difference comes from rounding in both label panels — flagged estimated. Macros do NOT account for any smartUpgrades (berries / walnuts) — add those macros separately if you use them.`,mealPrep:{storage:`N/A — make per serving. Nurri cans store at room temp until opened, then fridge.`,lasts:`Unopened Nurri: months. Open can: 1 day fridge. Eat the bowl in 90 seconds or you'll regret it.`,reheat:`N/A — make fresh.`}},{id:`30-30-muffin-mug-bowl`,title:`30/30 Muffin Mug Bowl`,tagline:`Two protein products, two 30-second microwave bursts, one warm mug. Adults only.`,heroImage:`/images/30-30-muffin-mug-bowl/hero.webp`,prepImage:`/images/30-30-muffin-mug-bowl/mise.webp`,prepImageCaption:`Three components: any Bootylicious muffin + Fairlife Fat-Free + half any Prime Bites brownie.`,flavorProfile:`Soft cake-like muffin soaked with cold milk, layered with melted brownie chunks creating chocolate + filling pockets throughout. Dessert-grade taste, breakfast-grade macros.`,calories:312,caloriesPerServing:312,protein:36.7,proteinPerServing:36.7,servings:1,time:`Under 2 min`,bestFor:[`Pre-workout breakfast (37g protein in 2 min)`,`Late-night dessert without a macro hit (~18g net carbs)`,`Travel-friendly when you have a microwave`,`Quick post-workout refuel`,`Cutting-friendly (312 cal / 37g protein)`,`Dessert-craving fix without takeout`],useThisWhen:`You need 37g of protein in under 2 minutes AND your brain wants dessert, not breakfast. The technique is flavor-agnostic — any Bootylicious muffin cup + any Prime Bites brownie works (S'mores + S'mores, Cinnamon Bun + Cookie Dough, Double Chocolate + Chocolate Glazed Donut, etc.). Adult-only — kids can take a bite but the artificial sweetener + protein-supplement load isn't a full-portion idea.`,flavorTarget:`Texture-first: soft cake-like muffin from the milk soak + slightly melted brownie chunks for warm chocolate pockets. Layered, not stirred. Eat with a spoon.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full serving as written. 1 Bootylicious cup + 1/4 cup Fairlife + 1/2 Prime Bites brownie.`,kid:`Not recommended for full portions. Adult dessert. Kid can have ONE bite for tasting but the artificial-sweetener density isn't kid-appropriate at portion size.`},ingredients:[`1 Bootylicious High Protein Muffin (any flavor — S'mores, Cinnamon Bun, Double Chocolate, Birthday Cake, Blueberry, Chocolate Peanut Butter, etc.)`,`1/4 cup (~60 mL) Fairlife Fat-Free Ultra-Filtered Milk (cold)`,`1/2 of a Prime Bites Protein Brownie (any flavor — S'mores, Cookie Dough, Chocolate Glazed Donut, etc.)`],steps:[`PREP THE MUFFIN: Open the Bootylicious cup. Loosen the muffin from the sides with a spoon — you want the milk to soak through, not pool at the top.`,`ADD MILK: Pour ~1/4 cup of cold Fairlife Fat-Free Milk directly into the muffin cup. Stir lightly with a spoon — the milk should be visible soaking down into the muffin, not just sitting on top.`,`FIRST 30 SECONDS: Microwave 30 sec. This soaks the milk through the muffin and creates the soft cake-like texture. If you skip this and just microwave the whole stack at once, the muffin stays dense and the brownie just melts on top of a brick.`,`ADD THE BROWNIE: Break half of a Prime Bites brownie into 4-6 small chunks. Scatter across the top of the warm soaked muffin. Don't stir — the chunks should sit on the surface so they melt in place, creating defined pockets.`,`SECOND 30 SECONDS: Microwave another 30 sec. The brownie chunks slightly melt + the marshmallow / filling (if any) gets gooey. Don't over-microwave — you want melt, not liquefaction.`,`OPTIONAL STIR: Leave layered for visible chocolate pockets (the better look) OR stir lightly for distributed chocolate (more uniform texture, less visual contrast).`,`EAT WARM. Spoon. Done.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Muffin came out dense and dry`,fix:`Either skipped the first 30 seconds OR didn't add enough milk. The first burst is what hydrates the protein muffin into cake texture. 1/4 cup minimum.`},{problem:`Brownie disappeared into the muffin`,fix:`You stirred between the two bursts. Don't. Scatter chunks on top, microwave, leave layered. The whole point of the second 30 sec is the brownie melts IN PLACE.`},{problem:`Microwaved too long and it's chewy/dry`,fix:`Two 30-sec bursts, not one 60-sec burst. The pause matters — heat redistributes during the rest.`},{problem:`Too sweet`,fix:`Use a less-sweet Bootylicious flavor (Blueberry, Cinnamon Bun) with a Prime Bites Brownie. Or skip the brownie entirely — Bootylicious solo is already a complete protein dessert at ~25g protein.`},{problem:`Not enough protein`,fix:`Use a FULL Prime Bites brownie instead of 1/2. Adds ~9.5g protein (19g protein bar ÷ 2 in the original = 9.5g; full bar = ~19g). New macros: ~407 cal / 46P / 14F / 50C / ~28g net. Better for muscle gain day, heavier than needed for cutting day.`},{problem:`Bowl is cold by the time you eat it`,fix:`Eat right out of the microwave. Microwave-to-mouth window is ~30 seconds — these protein muffins lose temp fast because of the milk.`}],brands:[{name:`Bootylicious`,item:`High Protein Muffin Cup (any flavor — 25g protein, 7g net carbs, 180-200 cal per cup, 12-pack variety)`,why:`Single-serve mug-format muffin you can microwave in the cup. 3-ingredient protein blend (whey + milk protein + collagen) so it bakes into actual muffin texture, not pudding. Any flavor works for this recipe — S'mores, Cinnamon Bun, Double Chocolate, Birthday Cake, Blueberry, Chocolate Peanut Butter, Apple Pie, Pumpkin Spice.`,url:`https://www.bootyliciousmuffin.com/`},{name:`Prime Bites`,item:`Protein Brownie (any flavor — 19g protein, 5g collagen, low sugar, 12-pack variety)`,why:`Individually-wrapped protein brownie that actually tastes like brownie (not protein bar). Soft texture, slight chocolate-glaze finish on most flavors. Half a brownie = ~9.5g protein bump at ~75-85 cal. Any flavor works: S'mores, Cookie Dough, Chocolate Glazed Donut, Birthday Cake, Mint Chocolate, etc.`,image:`/images/brands/prime-bites-smores-brownie.png`,url:`https://primebites.com/`},{name:`Fairlife`,item:`Fat-Free Ultra-Filtered Milk`,why:`Lactose-free, 50% more protein than regular milk, smooth pour. 1/4 cup adds ~3g extra protein + the moisture that hydrates the muffin. Sub Fairlife 2% or Nurri for slightly richer texture (adds 20-30 cal).`,image:`/images/brands/fairlife-milk.png`,url:`https://fairlife.com/ultra-filtered-milk/fat-free-skim-milk/`}],macroHonesty:`Per-serving (312 cal / 36.7g protein / 10g fat / 37g total carbs / 18.5g fiber → 18.5g net carbs) MacroFactor-verified. Atwater check: 36.7×4 + 10×9 + 18.5×4 = 311 cal ≈ 312 listed ✓ (math reconciles using NET carbs, since 18.5g of the 37g total is fiber). Total carbs reads scary at 37g but net carbs are 18.5g — the honest signal for this recipe. Macros assume S'mores flavors for both products; other flavor combos shift +/- 20-30 cal but protein stays within 1-2g.`,mealPrep:{storage:`N/A — make per serving. Bootylicious cups + Prime Bites brownies are individually shelf-stable for months.`,lasts:`Pantry: months for both products. Made bowl: eat immediately, doesn't hold.`,reheat:`N/A — make fresh. Reheated leftover gets rubbery from over-cooked muffin.`}},{id:`high-protein-muffin-cup-powerup`,title:`High-Protein Muffin Cup Powerup`,tagline:`285 cal. 35g protein. 17g fiber. Microwave mug cake with cookie-dough chunks. 3 minutes flat.`,heroImage:`/images/high-protein-muffin-cup-powerup/hero-finished-muffin-cup-polished.webp`,prepImage:`/images/high-protein-muffin-cup-powerup/step-01-product-cup-polished.webp`,socialImages:[`/images/high-protein-muffin-cup-powerup/step-06-chop-chormbles-polished.webp`,`/images/high-protein-muffin-cup-powerup/step-07-fold-in-chunks-polished.webp`],flavorProfile:`Soft warm muffin, cookies-and-cream sweetness, gooey center, chopped protein-candy chunks throughout. Tastes like dessert, eats like breakfast.`,calories:285,caloriesPerServing:285,protein:35,proteinPerServing:35,servings:1,time:`3 min`,bestFor:[`Breakfast`,`Powerup`,`High protein`,`High fiber`,`No-cook`,`Microwave`],useThisWhen:`Breakfast needs to happen fast — between meetings, before the gym, mid-morning slump. 3 minutes, one mug, 35g protein, 17g fiber, tastes like dessert. The Bootylicious cup is the workhorse; the Hormbles Chormbles chunks are what turn it from a protein muffin into a treat.`,flavorTarget:`Soft, warm, slightly gooey center with cookie-dough-style chunks visible throughout. Set on top, soft underneath. Not chalky, not dry, not pudding-y. The Fairlife milk does the work — water in the package instructions makes it texturally worse.`,coreRatio:`1 Bootylicious cup + 1/4 cup Fairlife milk + ~75 cal of chopped Hormbles Chormbles. This is the system. The Hormbles amount calibrates by SKU: 3/4 of a 100-cal bar OR 1/2 of a 140-cal bar.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full ratio (1 Bootylicious cup + 1/4 cup Fairlife + ~75 cal chopped Hormbles Chormbles).`,kid:`Skip the Hormbles Chormbles — artificial sweetener + protein-supplement load isn't a daily-kid idea. Bootylicious solo with Fairlife ≈ 210 cal / 28g protein. Still strong on its own.`},ingredients:[`1 Bootylicious High Protein Muffin Cup (any flavor — Double Chocolate, Cookies & Creme, Cinnamon Bun, Blueberry, Chocolate Peanut Butter, etc.)`,`1/4 cup Fairlife Fat-Free Ultra-Filtered Milk`,`1/2 to 3/4 of a Hormbles Chormbles bar, chopped (~75 cal portion)`,`Optional: extra splash of Fairlife after cooking for softer texture`],steps:[`MISE: Pop the Bootylicious cup lid + remove any inner foil seal. Measure 1/4 cup Fairlife. Pull out the Hormbles Chormbles bar + a small cutting board.`,`POUR + STIR: 1/4 cup Fairlife straight into the Bootylicious cup. Stir with a spoon until the dry mix is fully hydrated — no dry pockets. Batter should be thick like brownie batter, not soupy.`,{text:`CHOP THE CHORMBLES: ~75 cal worth of Hormbles Chormbles bar into small chunks (~1/4-inch). That's about 3/4 of the original 100-cal SKU, or 1/2 of the newer 140-cal SKU.`,image:`/images/high-protein-muffin-cup-powerup/step-06-chop-chormbles-polished.webp`},{text:`FOLD IN: Sprinkle the chopped Chormbles over the batter. Fold gently with the spoon to distribute. Don't overmix — visible chunks are the point.`,image:`/images/high-protein-muffin-cup-powerup/step-07-fold-in-chunks-polished.webp`},`MICROWAVE: 1 minute on high. If your microwave runs hot, start at 50 sec + add 10-sec bursts. Top should set but center stays slightly soft.`,`REST + EAT: 30 sec rest (keeps setting as it cools). Optional Fairlife splash on top for softer texture. Spoon, straight from the cup.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Muffin came out dry / rubbery`,fix:`Overcooked. Next time start at 50 sec + check. Protein muffins dry out in seconds past the set point. Rescue: stir in 2-3 tbsp extra Fairlife while still warm — softens within 30 sec.`},{problem:`Batter was too thick / pasty before microwaving`,fix:`Add 1-2 tbsp more Fairlife. Bootylicious batter should be brownie-batter consistency — pourable but holds shape. Too thick = dense end texture.`},{problem:`Chormbles chunks melted entirely into the batter`,fix:`You chopped them too small or microwaved too long. Cut into ~1/4-inch chunks (not crumbs) — they'll soften but stay visible. If they fully melt, lower cook time by 10 sec.`},{problem:`Tastes too sweet`,fix:`Use a less-sweet Bootylicious flavor (Blueberry, Cinnamon Bun) with a less-sweet Hormbles (Salted Fudge, Peanut Butter). Or skip the Chormbles entirely — Bootylicious solo is ~210 cal / 28g protein and already complete.`},{problem:`Macros came in higher than 285 cal`,fix:`Most likely cause: full 140-cal Hormbles bar instead of the ~75 cal target (adds 65 cal). Halve the new-SKU bar. Or pick the leanest Bootylicious flavor (Blueberry, ~180 cal).`}],brands:[{name:`Bootylicious`,item:`High Protein Muffin Cup (any flavor — 25g protein, 7g net carbs, 180-200 cal per cup, 12-pack variety)`,why:`Single-serve mug-format muffin you microwave directly in the cup. 4-ingredient protein blend (whey + milk protein + collagen) bakes into actual muffin texture, not pudding. Cross-recipe with the Bootylicious + Prime Bites mug dessert — same SKU, different mix-in. Any flavor works.`,image:`/images/brands/bootylicious-muffin-cup.webp`,url:`https://bootyliciousmuffins.com/`},{name:`Hormbles Chormbles`,item:`Protein Candy Bar (any flavor — Milk Chocolate, Salted Fudge, Peanut Butter, Peanut Caramel Nougat; previously Cookies & Creme. 10g protein, 0g sugar, 100-140 cal per bar)`,why:`From the co-founder of RXBAR. Chopped + folded into the muffin batter = cookie-dough chunks throughout. The texture upgrade that turns a protein muffin into a dessert moment. SKU evolution note: older bars were 100 cal, newer ones are 140 cal — calibrate the chop accordingly to hit the ~75 cal-per-serving target.`,image:`/images/brands/hormbles-chormbles.jpg`,url:`https://hormbles.com/`},{name:`Fairlife`,item:`Fat-Free Ultra-Filtered Milk`,why:`Lactose-free, 50% more protein than regular milk, smooth pour. 1/4 cup adds ~3g extra protein plus the moisture that hydrates the muffin. Creamier texture than water (which the Bootylicious package suggests). Already-in-your-fridge cross-recipe staple.`,image:`/images/brands/fairlife-milk.png`,url:`https://fairlife.com/ultra-filtered-milk/fat-free-skim-milk/`}],macroHonesty:`Per-serving (~285 cal / 35g protein / 13g fat / 35g total carbs / 17g fiber → 18g net carbs). Component breakdown: Bootylicious muffin cup ≈ 190 cal / 25P / 9F / 21C / 14g fiber (varies 180-200 by flavor) + Fairlife 1/4 cup ≈ 20 cal / 5P / 0F / 1C + Hormbles Chormbles ~75 cal portion ≈ 75 cal / 5P / 4F / 13C / 3g fiber. Hormbles portion calibrates by SKU: ~3/4 of the original 100-cal bar, OR ~1/2 of the new 140-cal bar. Flagged estimated because (1) Bootylicious flavors swing 180-200 cal, (2) the Hormbles SKU vintage matters (100 vs 140 cal per bar), (3) the chop-portion is eyeball-measured. Stick to the ~75 cal Chormbles target to hit the 285 anchor.`,mealPrep:{storage:`N/A — make per serving. Bootylicious cups + Hormbles Chormbles bars are individually shelf-stable for months.`,lasts:`Pantry: months for both products. Cooked muffin: eat immediately, doesn't hold.`,reheat:`N/A — make fresh. Reheated leftover gets rubbery from over-cooked muffin.`}},{id:`one-pan-breakfast-skillet`,title:`High-Protein One-Pan Breakfast Skillet`,tagline:`510 cal. 45g protein. 10 minutes. One pan. Eggs + Gilbert's Caprese + Lao Gan Ma.`,heroImage:`/images/one-pan-breakfast-skillet/hero-finished-breakfast-skillet-polished.webp`,prepImage:`/images/one-pan-breakfast-skillet/brand-lao-gan-ma-chili-crisp-polished.webp`,socialImages:[`/images/one-pan-breakfast-skillet/step-02-add-sausage-links-polished.webp`,`/images/one-pan-breakfast-skillet/step-03-crack-eggs-polished.webp`,`/images/one-pan-breakfast-skillet/step-05-spoon-chili-crisp-polished.webp`,`/images/one-pan-breakfast-skillet/step-07-cover-to-set-polished.webp`],flavorProfile:`Savory chicken-sausage + jammy egg yolks + bright spicy chili-crisp finish. Mediterranean meets Sichuan in one pan.`,calories:510,caloriesPerServing:510,protein:45,proteinPerServing:45,servings:1,time:`10 min`,bestFor:[`Breakfast`,`Powerup`,`High protein`,`One-pan`,`Adults-only kick`,`Cutting-friendly`],useThisWhen:`You want a hot breakfast that feels like real food (not a shake or bar), 45g of protein, and you have 10 minutes with one pan. 2 sausage links + 3 eggs + a spoonful of Lao Gan Ma — that's the entire system. Skip the chili crisp for kids; everything else stays the same.`,flavorTarget:`Brown the sausage links + crack 3 eggs around them + 1 tsp Lao Gan Ma scattered over the eggs + cover until whites set + jammy yolks. Don't flip the eggs — lid does the work. Don't drown in chili oil — 1 tsp is the right portion for the macro target.`,coreRatio:`2 Gilbert's Caprese chicken sausage links + 3 large eggs + 1 tsp Lao Gan Ma. This is the system. Add more chili crisp and you blow the fat budget; add a 4th egg and you blow the cal budget. Lock the 2/3/1 ratio.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe as written — 2 Gilbert's links + 3 eggs + 1 tsp Lao Gan Ma. Adults get the chili-crisp finish.`,kid:`Same 2 sausage links + 2-3 eggs, but SKIP the Lao Gan Ma entirely (the chili oil is the spicy adult layer). Kids get plain salt + a small piece of toast or fruit on the side. ~400 cal / 30-35g protein depending on egg count.`},ingredients:[`Cooking spray (Chosen Foods avocado oil)`,`2 Gilbert's Craft Sausages Caprese Chicken Sausage links (basil + mozzarella + sun-dried tomato variant)`,`3 large eggs`,`Kosher salt, to taste`,`1 tsp Lao Gan Ma Fried Chili in Oil (NOT a tablespoon — 1 tsp is the macro lever)`,`Optional: black pepper or extra chili flakes`],steps:[`SPRAY THE PAN: Nonstick skillet over medium heat. Hit with cooking spray.`,{text:`ADD SAUSAGE: 2 Gilbert's Caprese chicken sausage links into the pan. Cook 3-4 min, turning to brown all sides + warm through. The chicken sausage is pre-cooked — you're crisping the exterior, not cooking through raw meat.`,image:`/images/one-pan-breakfast-skillet/step-02-add-sausage-links-polished.webp`},{text:`CRACK IN THE EGGS: 3 large eggs cracked directly into the skillet around the sausage links. Keep medium heat — too hot and the whites burn before the yolks set.`,image:`/images/one-pan-breakfast-skillet/step-03-crack-eggs-polished.webp`},`SEASON: Pinch of kosher salt over the eggs. Black pepper if using.`,{text:`ADD CHILI CRISP: 1 tsp Lao Gan Ma Fried Chili in Oil spooned over the eggs (focus on the crispy bits, light on the oil — the oil adds ~80 cal per tablespoon and you only want ~25 cal worth).`,image:`/images/one-pan-breakfast-skillet/step-05-spoon-chili-crisp-polished.webp`},{text:`COVER + SET: Lid on. 2-4 min until whites are fully set and yolks are still jammy (or longer if you want them firm). Don't peek every 30 sec — open once at the 2-min mark.`,image:`/images/one-pan-breakfast-skillet/step-07-cover-to-set-polished.webp`},`SERVE HOT: Slide everything onto a plate or eat straight from the skillet. The macro headline is 510 cal / 45g protein assuming 2 Gilbert's links + 3 eggs + 1 tsp Lao Gan Ma — any deviation shifts the math.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Eggs are rubbery / overcooked`,fix:`Heat was too high or you covered too long. Medium heat, 2-3 min covered max for jammy yolks. Lid traps steam — it cooks fast.`},{problem:`Whites won't set without burning the bottom`,fix:`Heat too high. Drop to medium-low + cover. Steam sets the whites from above without crisping the bottom.`},{problem:`Chili crisp made the dish way over 510 cal`,fix:`You used a tablespoon instead of a teaspoon. 1 tbsp Lao Gan Ma = ~80 cal / 9g fat. 1 tsp = ~25 cal / 3g fat. The tsp portion is the macro-architecture lever — measure it.`},{problem:`Sausage links are dry / over-crisped`,fix:`You cooked them too long before adding the eggs. Gilbert's chicken links are pre-cooked — 3-4 min to brown is plenty. Add the eggs at the 3-min mark even if the sausage looks pale.`},{problem:`Macros came in higher than 510 cal`,fix:`Most likely cause: (1) 4th egg or 3rd sausage link, (2) over-portioned chili crisp (tbsp instead of tsp), or (3) over-spray of cooking oil. The 2/3/1 ratio is the budget — don't drift.`},{problem:`Kid wouldn't eat it because of the red flecks`,fix:`Skip the Lao Gan Ma entirely on the kid plate. Same skillet, same sausage, same eggs — just no chili crisp on their side. Plate theirs first, then add the chili to your portion.`}],brands:[{name:`Gilbert's Craft Sausages`,item:`Caprese Chicken Sausage (basil + part-skim mozzarella + sun-dried tomato, 10 oz pack / 4 links — ~13-15g protein per link)`,why:`Pre-cooked chicken sausage so you crisp instead of cooking through raw meat. Mediterranean flavor profile (basil + mozzarella + sun-dried tomato) pairs surprisingly well with the Sichuan chili crisp finish — the umami carries it. Other Gilbert's SKUs work but the macro math assumes Caprese.`,image:`/images/brands/gilberts-caprese-chicken-sausage.png`,url:`https://gilbertssausages.com/sausages/caprese-chicken-sausage/`},{name:`Lao Gan Ma`,item:`Fried Chili in Oil (~25 cal / 3g fat per 1 tsp; AVOID the 1 tbsp portion = ~80 cal / 9g fat)`,why:`The flavor shortcut for the dish. Sichuan-style fried chili in soybean oil with crispy bits. 1 tsp gives the heat + texture + umami without blowing the fat budget. Cross-recipe — pairs with eggs, rice, dumplings, noodles, anywhere you want chili heat.`,image:`/images/brands/lao-gan-ma-chili-crisp.webp`,url:`https://www.amazon.com/Lao-Gan-Ma-Spicy-Crisp/dp/B005Y3KWNW`},{name:`Chosen Foods`,item:`Avocado Oil Spray`,why:`Neutral cooking spray, ~0-5 cal per spray. Nonstick coating for the skillet so the eggs slide cleanly. Cross-recipe staple.`,image:`/images/brands/chosen-foods-spray.png`,url:`https://chosenfoods.com/products/avocado-oil-spray`}],macroHonesty:`Per-serving (~510 cal / 45g protein / ~32g fat / ~3g net carbs / 0g fiber) tracked in MacroFactor. Component breakdown: 2 Gilbert's Craft Caprese Chicken Sausage links ≈ 260 cal / 27P / 16F / 2C (varies by exact link weight, 5 oz per 2 links is the Costco SKU; ~130 cal / 13.5P per link mid-range) + 3 large eggs ≈ 210 cal / 18P / 15F / 1C + 1 tsp Lao Gan Ma ≈ 25 cal / 0P / 3F / 1C + cooking spray (~5 cal). Headline total: 500 cal / 45P / 34F / 4 net C — rounded to 510 / 45 in the headline. Fat/carbs/fiber values flagged 'estimated' because (1) sausage link weights vary slightly across packs, (2) Lao Gan Ma scoop varies by oil-vs-crispy-bits ratio. The 510 / 45g protein anchor is firm — that's the macro hook.`,mealPrep:{storage:`Best made fresh — 10 min is fast enough. Don't batch. Cooked eggs hold ~24 hours but the texture degrades.`,lasts:`N/A — cook per serving.`,reheat:`N/A — eggs reheat poorly. If you must: 30 sec microwave covered, but expect rubbery whites and over-set yolks.`}}],n=[{id:`chipotle-ham-sandwich`,title:`Chipotle Ham Sandwich`,tagline:`200 cal, 22g protein per sandwich. 5 minutes. No cooking.`,heroImage:`/images/chipotle-ham-sandwich-hero.webp`,prepImage:`/images/chipotle-ham-sandwich-prep.webp`,flavorProfile:`Creamy chipotle, smoky ham, crisp greens, soft bread`,calories:200,caloriesPerServing:200,protein:22,proteinPerServing:22,servings:1,time:`5 min`,bestFor:[`Lunch`,`Quick meal`,`No-cook`,`High protein`],useThisWhen:`You need a real lunch in 5 minutes with no cooking. 22g protein, 200 cal per sandwich. Eat two for 44g protein at 400 cal.`,flavorTarget:`Chipotle cream cheese on both slices for adults — smoky, creamy, no dry bites. Velveeta melts into the ham. Mixed greens add crunch. Kids get regular whipped cream cheese — mild, familiar.`,splitNote:{adult:`2 oz ham, Philadelphia Whipped Chipotle, generous greens. Eat 2 for a full meal (400 cal, 44g protein).`,kid:`1 oz ham, regular whipped cream cheese, lighter greens. One sandwich is a meal for kids.`},ingredients:[`2 slices Sola Sweet & Buttery bread (80 cal, 8g protein)`,`2 oz 365 Organic Black Forest Uncured Ham (60 cal, 11g protein)`,`1 slice Velveeta Original (35 cal, 3g protein)`,`1 tbsp Philadelphia Whipped Chipotle (25 cal)`,`Crisp mixed greens lettuce`],steps:[`SPREAD: Philadelphia Whipped Chipotle on both slices of bread. Adults get chipotle, kids get regular whipped.`,`LAYER: Ham evenly on one slice. Adults 2 oz, kids 1 oz.`,`CHEESE: 1 Velveeta slice on top of ham.`,`GREENS: Generous layer of crisp mixed greens. This is the texture — don't skip.`,`CLOSE: Press lightly to bind. Slice and serve.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Sandwich is dry`,fix:`Spread cream cheese on BOTH slices. One side only = dry bites.`},{problem:`Falls apart`,fix:`Press lightly after closing. The cream cheese acts as glue.`},{problem:`Lettuce is wilty / soggy`,fix:`Wash and DRY completely. Wet lettuce ruins the texture.`},{problem:`Not filling enough`,fix:`Eat two. That's 400 cal, 44g protein. Or add extra ham.`}],brands:[{name:`Sola`,item:`Sweet & Buttery Bread`,why:`8g protein per 2 slices at 80 cal — the bread IS a protein source`,image:`/images/brands/sola-bread.png`,url:`https://thesolacompany.com/products/sweet-and-buttery-bread`},{name:`365`,item:`Organic Black Forest Uncured Ham`,why:`11g protein per serving. Clean, no nitrates.`,image:`/images/brands/365-ham.jpg`,url:`https://www.wholefoodsmarket.com/product/365-everyday-value-organic-uncured-black-forest-ham-b074h7j2vt`},{name:`Velveeta`,item:`Original Slices`,why:`Melts into ham without heat. Creamy binding layer.`,image:`/images/brands/velveeta-slices.png`,url:`https://www.kraftheinz.com/velveeta/products/00021000611447-original-flavored-cheese`},{name:`Philadelphia`,item:`Whipped Chipotle`,why:`Smoky heat in a spread — the adult flavor layer. Half the calories of regular cream cheese.`,image:`/images/brands/philly-whipped-chipotle.png`,url:`https://www.kraftheinz.com/philadelphia/products/00021000080441-chipotle-whipped-cream-cheese-spread`}],mealPrep:{storage:`Best fresh. Can pre-make without lettuce — add greens when eating.`,lasts:`Same day. Lettuce wilts overnight.`,reheat:`N/A — cold sandwich.`}},{id:`crispy-chicken-money-mustard`,title:`Crispy Chicken + Money Mustard`,tagline:`Freezer meal. Upgraded.`,heroImage:`/images/chicken-chunks-hero.png`,prepImage:`/images/chicken-chunks-prep.png`,flavorProfile:`Crispy, savory, dippable — Chick-fil-A energy at home`,calories:330,caloriesPerServing:330,protein:30,proteinPerServing:30,servings:1,time:`10–12 min`,bestFor:[`Quick lunch`,`Freezer hack`,`High protein`,`Zero prep`],useThisWhen:`You need protein in 10 minutes with zero prep. Freezer to plate — the air fryer does the work.`,flavorTarget:`Crispy breaded chicken + creamy tangy Money Mustard dip. Keep sauce on the side — dipping beats coating.`,splitNote:{adult:`6 oz chicken (~300 cal, 30g protein) + 1 serving Money Mustard for dipping.`,kid:`3 oz chicken. Plain or with ketchup. Don't force the mustard sauce — they'll try it when they're ready.`},ingredients:[`6 oz Kirkland Signature Lightly Breaded Chicken Breast Chunks (adult) / 3 oz (kid)`,{text:`1 serving Money Mustard sauce (adult)`,link:`/cookbook/money-mustard`}],steps:[`COOK: Air fry at 400°F for 10–12 min. Shake basket halfway. Goal: crispy outside, not soggy.`,`PLATE: Add chicken to plate. Money Mustard on the side — dipping > coating.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Chicken is soggy / not crispy`,fix:`Don't overcrowd the air fryer basket. Single layer, space between pieces. Shake halfway.`},{problem:`Chicken is dry inside`,fix:`You overcooked it. Pull at 10 min and check — these are pre-cooked, you're just crisping them.`},{problem:`Kids won't try the sauce`,fix:`Don't push it. Serve plain or with ketchup. They'll come around.`}],brands:[{name:`Kirkland`,item:`Lightly Breaded Chicken Chunks`,why:`The sweet spot. Dino nuggets are for toddlers. Real Good Foods has the highest protein but kids won't eat them. These sit right in the middle — real breast meat, lightly breaded, no antibiotics, crispy in the air fryer, and the whole family actually eats them. Best macros you'll get without a fight.`,image:`/images/brands/kirkland-chicken-chunks.jpg`,url:`https://www.costco.com/p/-/kirkland-signature-lightly-breaded-chicken-breast-chunks-4-lbs/4000202951`}],mealPrep:{storage:`Keep bag in freezer. Cook per serving.`,lasts:`Months in freezer — that's the point.`,reheat:`Air fry from frozen every time. Don't microwave these.`}},{id:`miyoka-protein-ramen`,title:`No-Dish Protein Ramen`,tagline:`~35g protein. 7 minutes. Zero dishes. Eat from the container.`,heroImage:`/images/miyoka-ramen/hero.webp`,prepImage:`/images/miyoka-ramen/step0-ingredients.webp`,flavorProfile:`Spicy stir-fried ramen, bone broth depth, coated not soupy`,calories:350,caloriesPerServing:350,protein:35,proteinPerServing:35,servings:1,time:`7-10 min`,bestFor:[`Quick lunch`,`No-dish`,`High protein`,`Zero cleanup`],useThisWhen:`You need protein in under 10 minutes and don't want to wash a single dish. Cook in a pot, pour back into the container, shake with sauce, eat.`,flavorTarget:`Spicy stir-fried noodles coated in Miyoka sauce. Bone broth replaces water for extra protein + umami. Not soupy — reduced until coated.`,splitNote:{adult:`Use Miyoka Spicy version. Full sauce packet. Optional: chili flakes or soy sauce boost.`,kid:`Use Miyoka non-spicy version if available. Or use Maruchan instead — same bone broth trick works.`},ingredients:[`1 Miyoka Protein Spicy Ramen container (25g protein)`,`1 cup Kirkland Chicken Bone Broth (not water — 9g extra protein)`],steps:[`COOK: Add noodles to a small pot. Pour in 1 cup bone broth. Boil, then reduce to medium. Cook 5-7 min until soft and broth is mostly absorbed.`,`TRANSFER: Pour cooked noodles back into the Miyoka container. No bowl needed.`,`SAUCE: Add the sauce packet. Close lid. Shake well. Let sit 1-2 min to coat.`,`EAT: Directly from the container. Done.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Too soupy`,fix:`Cook longer — the broth should be mostly absorbed before transferring. Not a soup.`},{problem:`Noodles are mushy`,fix:`Overcooked. Pull at 5 min — they continue absorbing in the container.`},{problem:`Sauce isn't coating evenly`,fix:`Shake harder. Or stir with a fork before eating. The 1-2 min rest helps.`},{problem:`Not enough protein`,fix:`Add a sliced Bilinski's sausage or a soft-boiled egg on top.`}],brands:[{name:`Miyoka`,item:`Protein Spicy Ramen (Chicken Flavor)`,why:`25g protein per container. Spicy stir-fried style. Eat from the container — zero dishes.`},{name:`Kirkland`,item:`Organic Chicken Bone Broth`,why:`9g protein per cup. Replaces water — free protein + umami.`,image:`/images/brands/kirkland-bone-broth.jpg`,url:`https://www.costcobusinessdelivery.com/kirkland-signature-organic-chicken-bone-broth-32-fl-oz,-6-ct.product.100403862.html`}],mealPrep:{storage:`N/A — 7 minutes to make.`,lasts:`Eat immediately.`,reheat:`N/A.`}},{id:`high-protein-chili-cheese-toast`,title:`High-Protein Chili Cheese Toast`,tagline:`8 open-faced toasts. 130 cal / 13g protein each. Blended cottage cheese + reduced-fat fiesta + chilies on keto buns.`,heroImage:`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/hero-finished-chili-cheese-toast-polished.webp`,prepImage:`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/context-daisy-low-fat-cottage-cheese-polished.webp`,socialImages:[`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/context-daisy-low-fat-cottage-cheese-polished.webp`,`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/step-02-blend-cottage-cheese-polished.webp`,`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/step-05-mix-cheese-base-polished.webp`,`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/step-10-fill-toasts-polished.webp`,`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/step-12-finished-toasts-reveal-polished.webp`],flavorProfile:`Creamy + cheesy + bright chili kick. Crispy melted top, lightly toasted keto-bun base. Tastes like comfort food, lands like a snack.`,calories:130,caloriesPerServing:130,protein:13,proteinPerServing:13,servings:8,time:`18 min`,bestFor:[`Powerup`,`Snack`,`Quick lunch`,`High protein`,`Keto-friendly`,`Adults`],useThisWhen:`You want a savory snack that hits like comfort food but lands at 130 cal / 13g protein per toast. 18 min total, 8 open-faced toasts on Oroweat keto buns. Make all 8, eat 2-3 now + reheat the rest later in the toaster oven. Adult-only because of the chili heat — not designed as a kid snack.`,flavorTarget:`First taste: melty creamy cheese + Dan-O's crunch. Mid: bright chili pop from the chopped fresh peppers. Finish: crispy keto-bun edge + Dan-O's savory salt. Filling should be spreadable not crumbly — the blended cottage cheese is what creates the creamy base.`,coreRatio:`1 Daisy Low Fat Cottage Cheese cup (5.3 oz, blended) + 1 bag (7 oz) Great Value Reduced Fat Fiesta Blend + 2-4 fresh chilies + 4 Oroweat keto buns (8 halves). Divide filling evenly across all 8 halves. This is the system — scale by halving (4 toasts) or doubling (16 toasts).`,ingredients:[`4 Oroweat Superior Keto Buns, split into 8 open-faced halves`,`1 Daisy Low Fat Cottage Cheese cup (5.3 oz / 150g, blended smooth)`,`1 bag (7 oz / 198g) Great Value Reduced Fat Fiesta Blend shredded cheese`,`2-4 Thai bird chilies (HOT) OR 1-2 jalapeños (medium heat — remove seeds for milder), finely chopped`,`Dan-O's Crunchy Seasoning, to taste`,`Parchment paper or cooking spray (for the baking sheet)`],steps:[`OVEN: 375°F. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper (or hit it with cooking spray).`,{text:`BLEND COTTAGE CHEESE: Daisy Low Fat cup into a small food processor. Blend 30-45 sec until completely smooth — no curds visible. This is the move that makes the filling creamy not chunky.`,image:`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/step-02-blend-cottage-cheese-polished.webp`},{text:`SCOOP TO BOWL: Transfer the blended cottage cheese to a mixing bowl. Should look like thick Greek yogurt at this point.`,image:`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/step-03-scoop-base-to-bowl.webp`},{text:`ADD CHEESE: Full 7 oz bag of Great Value Reduced Fat Fiesta Blend shredded cheese into the bowl with the blended cottage cheese.`,image:`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/step-04-add-reduced-fat-cheese.webp`},{text:`FOLD: Mix the shredded cheese into the cottage-cheese base with a spatula until evenly distributed. Filling should look uniform — no dry shred patches, no cottage-cheese clumps.`,image:`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/step-05-mix-cheese-base-polished.webp`},{text:`CHOP CHILIES: 2-4 Thai bird chilies (hot version) OR 1-2 jalapeños with seeds removed (medium version) finely diced — pieces ~1/8-inch. Smaller dice = better distribution across all 8 toasts.`,image:`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/step-06-chop-chilies.webp`},{text:`FOLD CHILIES INTO FILLING: Diced chilies into the cheese mixture. Fold gently to distribute. Don't overmix — visible chili specks throughout the filling is the goal.`,image:`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/step-07-add-chilies-to-filling.webp`},{text:`SPLIT BUNS: 4 Oroweat Superior Keto Buns split horizontally into 8 open-faced halves. Arrange cut-side up on the lined baking sheet, spaced so the edges don't touch.`,image:`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/step-09-split-keto-buns.webp`},{text:`FILL THE TOASTS: Divide the filling evenly across all 8 halves. ~2 tbsp filling per toast. Spread to the edges so the cheese melts to the crust. Pile slightly mounded in the center.`,image:`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/step-10-fill-toasts-polished.webp`},{text:`SEASON THE TOPS: Dan-O's Crunchy Seasoning over each toast. Don't be shy — it's the salt + texture finish. ~1/4 tsp per toast.`,image:`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/step-11-season-loaded-toasts.webp`},{text:`BAKE: 375°F for ~9 min. Filling should be hot + visibly melted + slightly browned on top. Keto buns dry out fast past 10 min — set a timer.`,image:`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/step-12-bake-at-375.webp`},{text:`REST + SERVE: Let toasts cool 1-2 min before eating (cheese filling is molten right out of the oven). Eat 2-3 immediately, reheat the rest later.`,image:`/images/high-protein-chili-cheese-toast/step-12-finished-toasts-reveal-polished.webp`}],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Filling is too thick / hard to spread`,fix:`You under-blended the cottage cheese. Blend another 30 sec until completely smooth. If already mixed with shredded cheese, add 1 tbsp Fairlife milk (or 1 tbsp water) and fold to loosen.`},{problem:`Buns dried out / cracker-textured`,fix:`Overbaked. Oroweat keto buns dry out fast past 10 min. Pull at 8-9 min next time — the filling will still be molten + the buns will be lightly toasted, not desiccated.`},{problem:`Cheese didn't fully melt on top`,fix:`Underbaked OR oven not hot enough (375°F is the floor). Add 60-90 sec at 400°F for a final melt-and-brown. Watch closely — the line between melted and burnt is 30 sec.`},{problem:`Way too spicy for a snack`,fix:`You used Thai birds with seeds. Either remove seeds before chopping, sub jalapeños (with seeds removed for milder still), or halve the chili count (1-2 jalapeños instead of 2-4 Thai birds).`},{problem:`Filling tastes flat / not enough salt`,fix:`Light Dan-O's hit. Add another pinch on each toast before serving (toasts are still hot — salt sticks). Or stir 1/4 tsp kosher salt into the filling at the fold-chilies step.`},{problem:`Macros came in higher than 130 cal / toast`,fix:`Most likely cause: (1) larger Oroweat bun lot (some 8-pack runs are 120 cal each instead of 100, adds ~10 cal/toast), (2) overspilled shredded cheese (the 7 oz bag is the budget), or (3) added oil/butter to the bun. Stick to the bag + cup measurements.`}],brands:[{name:`Daisy`,item:`Low Fat Cottage Cheese (5.3 oz / 150g single-serve cup — 90 cal / 13g protein / 2.5g fat per cup)`,why:`Blended smooth, it becomes the creamy filling base. The Low Fat variant keeps the macros honest (versus 4% Daisy which doubles the fat per cup). Cross-recipe with id 30 steak noodles, id 33 buffalo wings crema, id 41 beef bacon pasta.`,image:`/images/brands/daisy-cottage-cheese-2pct.jpg`,url:`https://www.daisybrand.com/our-products/cottage-cheese/`},{name:`Great Value`,item:`Finely Shredded Reduced Fat Fiesta Cheese Blend (7 oz / 198g bag — 80 cal / 8g protein / 5g fat per oz, blend of reduced-fat Monterey Jack + cheddar + queso quesadilla + asadero)`,why:`Walmart store brand. 1/3 less fat than regular fiesta blend. Melts cleanly + has the same Mexican-cheese melt-character as full-fat. The 7 oz bag = 8 oz post-mix = exactly enough for 8 toasts at ~2 tbsp filling each. Sub any reduced-fat shredded blend — Sargento, Kraft Reduced Fat — same effect, ~30% more cost.`,image:``,url:`https://www.walmart.com/ip/Great-Value-Finely-Shredded-Reduced-Fat-Fiesta-Cheese-Blend-7-oz/22057341`},{name:`Oroweat`,item:`Superior Keto Hamburger Buns (8-count / 12 oz bag — 100 cal / 8g protein / 6g net carbs per bun)`,why:`Soft + bread-like (not the cardboard texture some keto buns have). Splits cleanly into open-faced halves. 100 cal per whole bun = 50 cal per half — the carb anchor for the recipe. Sub Bettergoods Keto Buns (id 23 cross-recipe) or Mission Carb Balance flatbreads cut in half — both work.`,image:`/images/brands/oroweat-superior-keto-hamburger-buns.png`,url:`https://www.oroweat.com/breads/keto/keto-buns`},{name:`Dan-O's`,item:`Crunchy Seasoning (savory salt + onion + garlic + black pepper crunch blend)`,why:`The salt + texture finish. Sprinkled on top before the bake = the crispy-edge effect on every toast. Cross-recipe with id 5 air fryer chicken, id 31 Dan-O's thighs, id 39 pork chops, plus the existing 'Loaded Steak & Egg Skillet' cookbook entry.`,image:`/images/brands/danos-crunchy.png`,url:`https://danosseasoning.com/product/crunchy-seasoning-small/`}],macroHonesty:`Per toast (~130 cal / 13g protein / 7g fat / 6g net carbs) MacroFactor-tracked. Component breakdown per toast (1/8 of the batch): 1/2 Oroweat Superior Keto Bun ≈ 50 cal / 4P / 1F / 3 net C + 1/8 of blended Daisy Low Fat cottage cheese cup ≈ 11 cal / 1.6P / 0.3F + 1/8 of 7 oz Great Value Reduced Fat Fiesta ≈ 70 cal / 7P / 4.4F / 1C + chili + Dan-O's ≈ 2 cal. Sums to ~133 cal / 12.6P / 5.7F / 4 net C. Atwater check: 13×4 + 6×4 + 7×9 = 52+24+63 = 139 ≈ 130 (small fat-rounding gap, normal for tracked-via-app entries). Flagged estimated because (1) Oroweat bun calorie counts vary slightly batch-to-batch (95-105 cal range), (2) the filling-per-toast portion is eyeball-divided (some toasts get more than others), (3) Dan-O's amount is to-taste. The 130 / 13 anchor holds if the batch math holds.`,mealPrep:{storage:`Best fresh out of the oven, but the filled-and-baked toasts hold 2-3 days in the fridge in an airtight container. The unbaked filling holds 3-4 days separately if you want to bake fresh per session.`,lasts:`Baked toasts: 2-3 days fridge. Filling-only (unbaked): 3-4 days fridge. Oroweat buns sealed: per package date.`,reheat:`Toaster oven 350°F 3-4 min from cold = crisp top, warm filling. Air fryer 350°F 2-3 min works too. Microwave makes the bun soggy — avoid.`}},{id:`grillos-pickle-dip-wilde-combo`,title:`Grillo's Pickle Dip + Wilde Chips Combo`,tagline:`270 cal / 27g protein snack — the dip (110/16) + a bag of Wilde Spicy Queso Protein Chips (160/11). Macro-coded combo of the viral pickle dip remix.`,heroImage:`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/context-wilde-chip-dip-polished.webp`,prepImage:`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/hero-finished-dip-with-wilde-polished.webp`,socialImages:[`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/context-wilde-chip-dip-polished.webp`,`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/hero-finished-dip-with-wilde-polished.webp`,`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/step-06-fill-grillos-tub-polished.webp`],flavorProfile:`Spicy queso chicken-chip crunch dunked in creamy pickle-ranch dip. Heat from Wilde + tang from the dip = the combo flavor lock.`,calories:270,caloriesPerServing:270,protein:27,proteinPerServing:27,servings:1,time:`1 min (assuming the dip is already made)`,bestFor:[`Quick lunch`,`Snack`,`Powerup`,`High protein`,`Macro-coded combo`,`Adults`],useThisWhen:`You made the [High-Protein Grillo's Pickle Dip](/cookbook/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style) (10-serving batch) and want a tracked single-serving snack. 1 scoop of dip + 1 bag of Wilde Spicy Queso Protein Chips = 270 cal / 27g protein on the macro log. Eats in 60 seconds, no cooking, no plating — open the chip bag, scoop from the Grillo's tub, eat. The combo is the macro story; everything else is the dip recipe.`,flavorTarget:`Wilde Spicy Queso chip first (chipotle + jalapeño + aged cheddar heat) + creamy pickle-ranch dip (tangy + briny + smoky bacon) = the combo flavor lock. Chip carries the dip, dip cuts the chip heat. Don't dip the chip more than once — chip moisture wrecks the second bite.`,coreRatio:`1 generous scoop dip (1/10 of the 10-serving batch — about 50g) + 1 full 1.34 oz bag of Wilde Spicy Queso Protein Chips. The dip is the SAME dip from the parent recipe — there's nothing to remix, just portion the combo correctly.`,ingredients:[{text:`1 generous scoop of High-Protein Grillo's Pickle Dip (~50g, 1/10 of the batch)`,link:`/cookbook/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style`},`1 bag (1.34 oz / ~30 chips) Wilde Spicy Queso Protein Chips`],steps:[{text:`MAKE THE DIP (one-time, ahead): Follow the [parent dip recipe](/cookbook/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style) to make a 10-serving batch. Store in the Grillo's tub in the fridge. Each scoop = 110 cal / 16g protein. Skip this step if the dip is already in your fridge.`,image:`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/step-06-fill-grillos-tub-polished.webp`},{text:`ASSEMBLE THE COMBO: Pull the Grillo's tub from the fridge. Open 1 bag of Wilde Spicy Queso Protein Chips. Dunk chips, eat. One scoop of dip from the tub = the right portion for the macro log.`,image:`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/context-wilde-chip-dip-polished.webp`},{text:`STORE: Lid back on the dip tub, sealed clip on the chip bag. The dip holds 3-4 days; chips hold ~3 weeks sealed. Repeat the combo as often as you want — each repeat is 270 / 27.`,image:`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/hero-finished-dip-with-wilde-polished.webp`}],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Macros came in higher than 270 cal`,fix:`Over-scooped the dip. 1/10 of the 10-serving batch is the budget — eyeball-divide the tub into 10 if you're tracking close. Or use a kitchen scale (1 scoop ≈ 50g of dip).`},{problem:`Chips break when you dunk`,fix:`Wilde chips are thinner than tortilla chips — fold them in half before dunking to double the structural strength. Or use the dip with regular tortilla chips (loses the 27g protein anchor, drops to ~250 cal / 18g protein per combo).`},{problem:`Dip is too thick for the chip`,fix:`See parent recipe troubleshooting — usually means too much Build the Body ranch seasoning or too little brine. Stir in 1 tbsp Grillo's brine + remix the tub before serving.`},{problem:`Want spicier`,fix:`Wilde makes 3 spicy variants — Spicy Queso (this combo), Buffalo, and Honey Habanero. Buffalo is hotter; Honey Habanero is sweetest. All hit 10g protein per bag.`},{problem:`Don't have Wilde chips`,fix:`The dip works with regular tortilla chips, carrots, celery, cucumber slices, or pita chips — just lose the 27g protein anchor. With a 1-oz portion of tortilla chips, the combo lands ~250 cal / 18g protein. Still a strong macro snack.`}],brands:[{name:`High-Protein Grillo's Pickle Dip`,item:`Parent dip recipe — 10 servings per batch, 110 cal / 16g protein per scoop`,why:`Make the 10-serving batch via the parent recipe ([Grillo's Pickle Dip Protein Style](/cookbook/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style)). Stores 3-4 days in the original Grillo's tub. One batch supports ~10 combos.`,image:`/images/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style/hero-finished-dip-with-wilde-polished.webp`,url:`/cookbook/grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style`},{name:`Wilde Brands`,item:`Spicy Queso Protein Chips (1.34 oz bag — 160 cal / 11g protein / 4g net carbs per bag; 4 oz bigger bag also available)`,why:`Real chicken breast + egg whites + bone broth chips, NOT potato chips. 10g protein per 1 oz serving. Spicy Queso variant has aged cheddar + smoked chipotle + roasted jalapeño — pairs cleanly with the pickle dip's tang. The combo IS the macro anchor for this entry.`,image:`/images/brands/wilde-spicy-queso-chips.png`,url:`https://www.wildebrands.com/products/spicy-queso`}],macroHonesty:`Per combo (270 cal / 27g protein) is straight math: 1 scoop dip (110 cal / 16g protein, per parent-recipe macroHonesty) + 1 bag Wilde Spicy Queso (160 cal / 11g protein, per label) = 270 cal / 27g protein. Wilde's per-bag macros are package-label values. Dip macros are MacroFactor-tracked from the parent recipe. The 270 / 27 anchor holds as long as the dip portion is 1/10 of the batch and the chips are a single full bag.`,mealPrep:{storage:`Dip in the Grillo's tub with lid on, fridge. Chips in their sealed bag at room temp.`,lasts:`Dip: 3-4 days fridge. Chips: ~3 weeks sealed bag, room temp. Combo = whatever the weakest link is (the dip).`,reheat:`N/A — both eaten cold/room temp.`}}],r=[{id:`chocolate-protein-brownie-bowl`,title:`Chocolate Protein Brownie Bowl`,tagline:`Pumpkin for texture. Chocolate is the flavor.`,heroImage:`/images/brownie-bowl-hero.png`,prepImage:`/images/brownie-bowl-prep.png`,flavorProfile:`Rich, fudgy, chocolate-forward, warm`,calories:918,caloriesPerServing:230,protein:91,proteinPerServing:23,servings:4,time:`5 min prep + 1 min microwave per serving`,bestFor:[`Post-dinner`,`Dessert`,`Sweet craving`,`Cutting-friendly`],useThisWhen:`You want a warm, fudgy chocolate dessert that hits 23g protein per serving — and you want it in under 2 minutes from mix to mouth.`,whyPumpkinWorks:`The pumpkin is here for texture, not pumpkin flavor. It adds moisture and softness so the brownie bowl stays fudgy instead of dry. You won't taste it.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe as written. Top with Ninja Creami protein pint for 400+ cal dessert.`,kid:`Same recipe works for kids — it's already mild chocolate. Skip the Ninja Creami or use regular ice cream.`},ingredients:[`--- DRY MIX ---`,`60g PEScience Select Protein (Chocolate Truffle)`,`40g Protein Cookie Butter Powder (Cookies & Cream)`,`30g Anthony's Organic Black Cocoa Powder`,`20g all-purpose flour`,`8g monk fruit sweetener`,`4g baking powder`,`2 pinches salt`,`--- WET MIX ---`,`160g Thrive Market Organic Pumpkin`,`160g Fairlife Fat Free Milk`,`2 eggs`,`--- ADD-IN (at cook time) ---`,`40g Lily's Milk Chocolate Style Baking Chips (10g per serving)`,`--- TO SERVE ---`,`1 scoop Ninja Creami protein pint (optional)`],steps:[`MIX DRY: Whisk PEScience protein, cookie butter powder, black cocoa, flour, monk sweetener, baking powder, and salt. Break up all cocoa clumps.`,`MIX WET: Whisk pumpkin puree, Fairlife milk, and eggs until smooth.`,`BUILD ONE SERVING: Add 1/4 dry mix + 1/4 wet mix to a microwave-safe bowl. Stir until smooth. Fold in 10g Lily's chips.`,`MICROWAVE: ~1 minute. Start checking at 50 seconds. Stop when top is just set but still soft — it keeps cooking.`,`SERVE: Top with Ninja Creami protein pint scoop. Eat immediately.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Brownie is dry / cakey`,fix:`You overcooked it. Pull at 50-55 seconds. The center should still look slightly underdone.`},{problem:`Tastes like pumpkin`,fix:`You used too much. Stick to exact 160g. The cocoa should completely mask it.`},{problem:`Metallic / bitter taste`,fix:`You used baking soda instead of baking powder, or too much. Use 4g baking powder max.`},{problem:`Too dense / heavy`,fix:`Under-mixed. The wet and dry need to be fully combined — no dry pockets.`},{problem:`Not sweet enough`,fix:`Add 5g more monk sweetener or an extra 5g chocolate chips.`}],brands:[{name:`PEScience`,item:`Select Protein (Chocolate Truffle)`,why:`Best-tasting chocolate protein powder that actually bakes well — not chalky`,image:`/images/brands/pescience-chocolate.png`,url:`https://www.pescience.com/products/select-protein`},{name:`Anthony's`,item:`Organic Black Cocoa Powder`,why:`Deep, dark chocolate color and flavor — makes it look and taste like real brownie`,image:`/images/brands/anthonys-black-cocoa.jpg`,url:`https://anthonysgoods.com/products/anthonys-organic-alkalized-cocoa-powder-dutch-process`},{name:`Lily's`,item:`Milk Chocolate Baking Chips`,why:`Melty chocolate pockets without the sugar bomb — keeps macros clean`,image:`/images/brands/lilys-chocolate-chips.webp`,url:`https://www.lilys.com/products/milk-chocolate-style-baking-chips`},{name:`Thrive Market`,item:`Organic Pumpkin`,why:`The hidden texture hack — adds moisture and fudginess without fat or flavor`,image:`/images/brands/thrive-pumpkin.jpg`,url:`https://thrivemarket.com/p/thrive-market-organic-pumpkin`},{name:`Fairlife`,item:`Fat Free Milk`,why:`Higher protein than regular milk, blends smooth into the batter`,image:`/images/brands/fairlife-milk.png`,url:`https://fairlife.com/ultra-filtered-milk/fat-free-skim-milk/`}],mealPrep:{storage:`Mix dry base in bulk and store in a jar. Mix wet fresh each time. Don't pre-mix wet+dry — it won't keep.`,lasts:`Dry mix keeps 2-3 weeks in an airtight container. Each serving is made fresh in 2 min.`,reheat:`Not needed — each serving is made fresh in the microwave.`}},{id:`pistachio-kataifi-protein-creami`,title:`Pistachio Kataifi Protein Creami`,tagline:`Ninja Creami ice cream that hits ~35g protein. Engineered, not guessed.`,heroImage:`/images/creami-hero.webp`,prepImage:`/images/creami-prep.webp`,flavorProfile:`Rich pistachio, chocolate undertone, crispy kataifi crunch`,calories:280,caloriesPerServing:280,protein:35,proteinPerServing:35,servings:1,time:`5 min prep + 12-16 hrs freeze + 2 min spin`,bestFor:[`Dessert`,`High protein`,`Ninja Creami`,`Cutting-friendly`],useThisWhen:`You want real ice cream texture at ~35g protein and ~280 cal. Built on ~28g protein from isolate, 0.75 cup 2% milk, and a controlled fat layer for texture.`,flavorTarget:`First taste: pistachio cream. Mid: chocolate depth from cocoa. Finish: crispy kataifi crunch. Feels indulgent, not diet.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe as written — pistachio cream + kataifi crunch on top.`,kid:`Same base works for kids. Skip the kataifi if they don't like the texture. Add sprinkles instead.`},ingredients:[`--- BASE ---`,`3/4 cup Fairlife 2% milk`,`Opportuniteas Whey Isolate (~28g protein total — adjust scoops by brand)`,`1 tbsp Ghirardelli 100% Cocoa (Dutch-process)`,`2 tsp monk fruit sweetener`,`1/8 tsp Bob's Red Mill Guar Gum`,`Pinch of salt`,`--- FLAVOR LAYER ---`,`1 tbsp Sicania Pistachio Sweet Cream`,`--- CRUNCH ---`,`5g toasted kataifi`],steps:[`BLEND: Combine milk, protein powder, cocoa, monk fruit, guar gum, and salt. Use immersion blender until completely smooth.`,`FREEZE: Pour into Ninja Creami pint container. Freeze flat for 12-16 hours.`,`PRE-SPIN: Run hot water over the outside of the container for 30 seconds.`,`SPIN: Select Regular Ice Cream. Re-spin once if needed — no extra milk.`,`ASSEMBLE: Swirl in pistachio cream. Top with toasted kataifi. Eat immediately.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Icy / not creamy`,fix:`You didn't blend smooth enough, or froze too long (>24 hrs). Immersion blender until zero lumps. 12-16 hrs freeze max.`},{problem:`Too hard to spin`,fix:`Hot water pre-spin for 30 seconds. If still too hard, let it sit on the counter for 5 min.`},{problem:`Not sweet enough`,fix:`Add 1 more tsp monk fruit. Protein powder bitterness varies by brand.`},{problem:`Gritty texture`,fix:`Protein powder didn't dissolve. Blend longer. Some brands are grittier — isolate works best.`},{problem:`Pistachio flavor is weak`,fix:`Mix the pistachio cream IN during the re-spin, not just on top. It needs to be distributed.`}],brands:[{name:`Fairlife`,item:`2% Reduced Fat Ultra-Filtered Milk`,why:`The 2% fat matters here — gives the Creami body and creaminess that fat-free can't. Higher protein than regular milk.`,image:`/images/brands/fairlife-milk.png`,url:`https://fairlife.com/ultra-filtered-milk/2-percent-reduced-fat-milk/`},{name:`Opportuniteas`,item:`Grass-Fed Whey Protein Isolate`,why:`Dissolves clean, consistent protein per scoop — the base of every Creami pint`,image:`/images/brands/opportuniteas-whey.png`,url:`https://opportuniteas.com/products/opportuniteas-grass-fed-whey-protein-isolate`},{name:`Ghirardelli`,item:`100% Cocoa Dutch-Process`,why:`Deep chocolate color and flavor — this is what makes the pint brown, not green`,image:`/images/brands/ghirardelli-cocoa.jpg`,url:`https://www.ghirardelli.com/premium-baking-cocoa-100--unsweetened-cocoa-powder-8-oz-bag-61865`},{name:`Bob's Red Mill`,item:`Guar Gum`,why:`Tiny amount prevents iciness — gives the Creami something to work with for smooth texture`,image:`/images/brands/bobs-redmill-guar-gum.jpg`,url:`https://www.bobsredmill.com/product/guar-gum`},{name:`Sicania`,item:`Pistachio Sweet Cream`,why:`Real pistachio cream, not extract — swirl it in during the re-spin for actual flavor`,image:`/images/brands/sicania-pistachio-cream.jpg`,url:`https://www.sicaniafood.com/product/pistachio-sweet-cream-200g-sicania/`}],mealPrep:{storage:`Freeze pints in advance — up to a week. Spin fresh when ready to eat.`,lasts:`Frozen base keeps 1 week. Spun ice cream doesn't refreeze well.`,reheat:`N/A — eat immediately after spinning.`}},{id:`midnight-mix-creami`,title:`Midnight Mix Creami`,tagline:`Chocolate protein ice cream with the 5g mix-in method.`,heroImage:`/images/midnight-mix-hero.webp`,prepImage:`/images/midnight-mix-prep.webp`,flavorProfile:`Rich chocolate base, crunchy candy mix-ins in every bite`,calories:300,caloriesPerServing:300,protein:38,proteinPerServing:38,servings:1,time:`5 min prep + overnight freeze`,bestFor:[`Dessert`,`High protein`,`Ninja Creami`,`Controlled indulgence`],useThisWhen:`You want chocolate ice cream that hits ~38g protein with real candy mix-ins — Oreos, M&M's, pretzels, chocolate chips — without blowing your macros. 5g of each. That's the system.`,flavorTarget:`Thick, creamy chocolate base from cocoa + protein. Then: cookie crunch (Oreo), candy pop (M&M's), salt crunch (Pop'ums), soft chocolate melt (Lily's). Every bite is different.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe as written. The mix-ins are controlled at 5g each — that's ~80 cal total for all 4.`,kid:`Same base works for kids. Let them pick their own 5g mix-ins — makes it fun without going overboard.`},ingredients:[`--- BASE ---`,`3/4 cup Fairlife 2% milk`,`1 scoop whey protein (~28g protein)`,`1 tbsp Anthony's Black Cocoa Powder`,`2 tsp monk fruit sweetener`,`1/8 tsp Bob's Red Mill Guar Gum`,`Pinch of salt`,`--- 5g MIX-IN METHOD ---`,`5g Oreo crumbles`,`5g mini M&M's`,`5g Pop'ums (or crunchy pretzel snack)`,`5g Lily's chocolate chips`],steps:[`BLEND: Add all base ingredients to Creami pint. Immersion blender until completely smooth. No clumps.`,`FREEZE: Freeze flat for 12-16 hours. Uneven freeze = bad texture.`,`FIRST SPIN: Select Lite Ice Cream or Regular Ice Cream.`,`FIX TEXTURE: If powdery, re-spin — NO extra milk. Adding milk here ruins it.`,`MIX-IN: Create a center well. Add all 4 mix-ins (5g each). Run Mix-In mode.`,`EAT: Immediately. Don't refreeze.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Icy / not creamy`,fix:`Didn't blend smooth enough, or froze too long. Immersion blender, 12-16 hrs max.`},{problem:`Powdery after first spin`,fix:`Normal — re-spin once, no milk. This is expected.`},{problem:`Mix-ins sink to bottom`,fix:`Create the well first, don't just dump them on top. The mix-in mode needs a pocket to work.`},{problem:`Too sweet / too bitter`,fix:`Adjust monk fruit by 1 tsp. Protein powder bitterness varies by brand.`},{problem:`Not enough mix-in flavor`,fix:`You're using less than 5g. Weigh it — 5g feels small but it's enough for flavor without calorie damage.`}],brands:[{name:`Fairlife`,item:`2% Reduced Fat Milk`,why:`The 2% fat gives the Creami body — fat-free won't work here`,image:`/images/brands/fairlife-milk.png`,url:`https://fairlife.com/ultra-filtered-milk/2-percent-reduced-fat-milk/`},{name:`Anthony's`,item:`Black Cocoa Powder`,why:`Deep dark chocolate color and flavor — makes it look and taste like real chocolate ice cream`,image:`/images/brands/anthonys-black-cocoa.jpg`},{name:`Bob's Red Mill`,item:`Guar Gum`,why:`Prevents iciness — tiny amount, huge texture difference`,image:`/images/brands/bobs-redmill-guar-gum.jpg`,url:`https://www.bobsredmill.com/product/guar-gum`},{name:`Lily's`,item:`Chocolate Chips`,why:`Soft melt pockets in the mix-in — no sugar, keeps macros clean`,image:`/images/brands/lilys-chocolate-chips.webp`}],mealPrep:{storage:`Freeze pints in advance — up to a week. Spin fresh when ready to eat.`,lasts:`Frozen base keeps 1 week. Spun ice cream doesn't refreeze well.`,reheat:`N/A — eat immediately after spinning.`}},{id:`mocha-brownie-protein-creami`,title:`Mocha Brownie Protein Creami`,tagline:`Strong coffee flavor. Chocolate crunch. Night-friendly.`,heroImage:`/images/mocha-creami-hero.webp`,prepImage:`/images/mocha-creami-prep.webp`,flavorProfile:`Bold mocha, chocolate brownie crunch, creamy base`,calories:345,caloriesPerServing:345,protein:42,proteinPerServing:42,servings:1,time:`5 min prep + 8-12 hrs freeze`,bestFor:[`Dessert`,`High protein`,`Ninja Creami`,`Night-friendly`],useThisWhen:`You want coffee ice cream that hits ~42g protein — with real brownie crunch. Decaf keeps it night-friendly without sacrificing flavor.`,flavorTarget:`Bold mocha base from instant coffee + whey. Brownie Brittle mix-in adds chocolate crunch in every bite. Not sweet-forward — coffee-forward.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe as written. The decaf makes it safe for evening dessert.`,kid:`Skip the coffee — make the Midnight Mix or Pistachio Creami instead.`},ingredients:[`--- BASE ---`,`1 cup Fairlife 2% milk`,`1 scoop Opportuniteas Whey Isolate (~28g protein)`,`1 tbsp Nescafé Taster's Choice House Blend (instant coffee)`,`Monk fruit sweetener (to taste)`,`Pinch of salt`,`1/8 tsp Bob's Red Mill Guar Gum`,`--- MIX-IN ---`,`2/3 serving Brownie Brittle (Chocolate Chip)`],steps:[`BLEND: All base ingredients — milk, whey, instant coffee, sweetener, salt, guar gum. Immersion blender until completely smooth.`,`FREEZE: Pour into Creami pint. Freeze flat for 8-12 hours.`,`SPIN: Run Ice Cream mode.`,`FIX: If creamy, move on. If crumbly, add 1 tbsp milk and re-spin once.`,`MIX-IN: Add Brownie Brittle pieces. Run Mix-In mode. Eat immediately.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Coffee flavor is weak`,fix:`Use a heaping tablespoon of instant coffee. Or use 2 tsp espresso powder instead.`},{problem:`Too bitter`,fix:`Add more sweetener. The protein powder bitterness + coffee can stack — monk fruit balances it.`},{problem:`Icy / not creamy`,fix:`Didn't blend smooth enough or froze too long. 8-12 hrs max. Immersion blender, no lumps.`},{problem:`Crumbly after first spin`,fix:`Add 1 tbsp milk, re-spin. Don't add more than that.`},{problem:`Brownie Brittle is soggy`,fix:`Eat immediately after mix-in. It absorbs moisture fast.`}],brands:[{name:`Fairlife`,item:`2% Reduced Fat Milk`,why:`The 2% fat gives the Creami body — fat-free won't work here`,image:`/images/brands/fairlife-milk.png`,url:`https://fairlife.com/ultra-filtered-milk/2-percent-reduced-fat-milk/`},{name:`Opportuniteas`,item:`Grass-Fed Whey Isolate`,why:`Dissolves clean, consistent protein — the base of every Creami pint`,image:`/images/brands/opportuniteas-whey.png`,url:`https://opportuniteas.com/products/opportuniteas-grass-fed-whey-protein-isolate`},{name:`Bob's Red Mill`,item:`Guar Gum`,why:`Prevents iciness — tiny amount, huge texture difference`,image:`/images/brands/bobs-redmill-guar-gum.jpg`,url:`https://www.bobsredmill.com/product/guar-gum`},{name:`Nescafé`,item:`Taster's Choice House Blend`,why:`Dissolves instantly, strong coffee flavor without brewing. House Blend has the right roast depth for mocha.`,image:`/images/brands/nescafe-tasters-choice.jpg`,url:`https://www.nescafe.com/us/products/house-blend-medium-roast-coffee-7-oz/`},{name:`Brownie Brittle`,item:`Chocolate Chip`,why:`Thin, crunchy brownie pieces — perfect mix-in texture that holds up in the Creami`}],mealPrep:{storage:`Freeze pints in advance — up to a week. Spin fresh when ready to eat.`,lasts:`Frozen base keeps 1 week. Spun ice cream doesn't refreeze well.`,reheat:`N/A — eat immediately after spinning.`}},{id:`protein-tiramisu`,title:`Protein Tiramisu`,tagline:`Sunday-night build. 4 servings, overnight chill, 24g protein per ramekin.`,heroImage:`/images/protein-tiramisu/hero.webp`,prepImage:`/images/protein-tiramisu/mise.webp`,prepImageCaption:`Seven brands. Build once Sunday, eat through Thursday.`,actionImage:`/images/protein-tiramisu/cream-bowl.webp`,actionImageCaption:`Cream blended thick — holds a soft peak, doesn't pour. Cottage cheese went in ALONE first; no curds survive.`,flavorProfile:`Cheesecake-mousse cream over coffee-dipped HighKey wafers, finished with a heavy Ghirardelli cocoa snowfall. Tiramisu perception, no carb tax (~10g net carbs per serving — allulose + wafer fiber strip out most of the 22g total carb count).`,calories:944,caloriesPerServing:236,protein:97,proteinPerServing:24,servings:4,time:`15 min prep + overnight chill`,bestFor:[`Make-ahead`,`Dessert`,`Family-friendly`,`Cutting-friendly`,`Meal-prep`],useThisWhen:`You want a make-ahead Sunday dessert that builds once and eats over four days — same recipe for the whole family, 24g protein per serving, ~10g net carbs, MacroFactor-verified macros.`,whyThisWorks:`Most protein tiramisus fail four ways: watery yogurt, fake sweetness, sponge collapse, zero richness. This solves all four — Neufchâtel for fat carry, PEScience whey/casein blend (not isolate) for non-chalky thickening, cottage cheese tang that tiramisu uniquely tolerates, and HighKey wafers + coffee dip doing structural work. The trick is engineering AROUND real tiramisu, not faking it.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full serving — 8 wafers, full cream layer, heavy cocoa dust. Meal-prep into 4 containers and pull one per night.`,kid:`Same recipe works for the whole family. The instant coffee inside the cream is mild; the dipped wafers carry most of the coffee flavor. If you want zero coffee for kids, dip THEIR wafers in plain Fairlife instead of black coffee — same cream layer, same cocoa top.`},ingredients:[`--- CREAM LAYER (makes 4 servings) ---`,`150g Fage Total 0% Greek Yogurt (1 small container)`,`150g Daisy 2% Cottage Cheese (1 small container)`,`84g Philadelphia Neufchâtel Cheese (3 portions of an 8 oz block)`,`2 scoops PEScience Select Protein, Vanilla (62g total)`,`3 tbsp Whole Earth Allulose + Monk Fruit sweetener blend (36g)`,`1-2 tsp Nescafé Taster's Choice instant coffee (mixed into cream)`,`--- LAYER ---`,`28 HighKey Vanilla Wafers (7 per ramekin × 4 ramekins, ~70g total)`,`About 1/2 cup black coffee (brewed strong, room temp) — for dipping`,`--- FINISH ---`,`1/2 tbsp Ghirardelli unsweetened cocoa powder (for the snowfall on top)`],substitutionNotes:[`HighKey Vanilla Wafers (Tier 3 emergency carb) — sub any low-carb vanilla wafer or shortbread; the structure matters more than the brand, but HighKey holds the coffee dip without dissolving`,`PEScience Select Protein Vanilla (Tier 1 signature) — sub any whey+casein blend; pure whey isolate goes chalky and ruins texture`,`Daisy 2% Cottage Cheese — sub Good Culture 2% or Friendship 2%; do NOT use 0% (kills mouthfeel) or 4% (over the fat budget)`,`Fage Total 0% — sub Chobani 0% or store-brand 0%; the 0% is intentional so the Neufchâtel can do all the fat work`,`Philadelphia Neufchâtel — non-negotiable. Do NOT sub 1/3-less-fat cream cheese (different texture entirely). The Neufchâtel is the fat carrier for the whole dessert.`,`Whole Earth Allulose+Monk Fruit — sub Lakanto Classic or Besti Allulose+Monk; allulose specifically because it dissolves clean and won't crystallize overnight`,`Ghirardelli Unsweetened Cocoa — sub Hershey's Natural Unsweetened or Anthony's; heavy dust on top is non-negotiable — cocoa is doing psychological work for tiramisu perception`,`Nescafé Taster's Choice instant coffee — any instant coffee works; for the dip, brewed strong black coffee is better than instant`],steps:[`BLEND COTTAGE CHEESE ALONE: This is the most important step. Add the full 150g Daisy 2% to a blender or food processor. Blend until completely smooth — no visible curds. If you skip this and blend everything together, surviving curds wreck the mousse texture and you'll taste them all week. Non-negotiable.`,`ADD THE REST OF THE CREAM: Once cottage cheese is silky, add the Fage 0%, Neufchâtel (cut into chunks so it blends), 2 scoops PEScience Vanilla, 3 tbsp Whole Earth sweetener, and 1-2 tsp Nescafé instant coffee. Blend until thick, smooth, mousse-like — should hold a soft peak, not pour. If too thick, add a splash of milk or water.`,`BREW THE DIP COFFEE: While the cream chills for a minute, brew about 1/2 cup strong black coffee. Cool to room temp. Pour into a shallow bowl wide enough to lay a wafer flat.`,`DIP, DON'T SOAK: One wafer at a time — quick in, quick out. Roughly one second per side. The wafer should still feel structural when you place it. Soaked wafers turn into wet sludge by morning. This is where most home tiramisus die.`,`LAYER: In each of 4 ramekins or 6 oz meal-prep containers — 3-4 dipped wafers on the bottom (snap if needed to fit), generous spoonful of cream (~1/4 of cream total ÷ 2 layers = ~1/8 per layer), 3-4 more dipped wafers, another generous spoonful of cream on top (7 wafers per ramekin × 4 ramekins = 28 wafers total). Smooth flat. Repeat for all 4 containers.`,`CHILL OVERNIGHT — NOT 4 HOURS, OVERNIGHT: This is the second non-negotiable step. The protein powder needs to hydrate, the wafers need to soften from the coffee, and the flavors need to meld. Day 2 tastes dramatically better than fresh — the coffee bitterness smooths out and the cream sets like real tiramisu cream.`,`COCOA DUST RIGHT BEFORE EATING: Don't dust ahead of time — cocoa absorbs moisture and goes patchy. Dust 1/2 tbsp Ghirardelli cocoa heavily over the top of one container right before you eat it. Use a fine mesh strainer for an even snowfall. The cocoa carries the tiramisu perception harder than anything else in the recipe.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Cream is grainy / has curds`,fix:`You skipped step 1. The cottage cheese MUST be blended alone first until silky. Once you mix it with the yogurt and Neufchâtel, the curds won't break down further. No fix after the fact — start over.`},{problem:`Wafers are mushy / wet by morning`,fix:`You soaked them. The dip is one second per side, not five. Quick in, quick out. Some wafer integrity should remain when you place it.`},{problem:`Tastes like protein powder`,fix:`You ate it before overnight chill. Don't. The chill is what hydrates the protein and mellows the flavor. Fresh, this tastes like a protein hack. After 8+ hours, it tastes like dessert.`},{problem:`Cream tastes flat / one-note`,fix:`Add 1 tsp vanilla extract + a pinch of salt to the cream blend next time. Optional but worth it — salt makes the sweetness feel real and vanilla adds depth.`},{problem:`Wafers stayed crunchy after chill`,fix:`Coffee dip too quick or coffee not strong enough. Bump dip to 1.5 seconds and use strong-brewed coffee (not weak instant). Wafers should be soft-but-structured by morning, like real ladyfingers.`},{problem:`Top went patchy and weird`,fix:`You dusted the cocoa ahead of time. Cocoa absorbs cream moisture and clumps. Dust right before eating, one container at a time.`}],brands:[{name:`HighKey`,item:`Vanilla Wafer Cookies (12-wafer serving = 120 cal)`,why:`Low-carb wafer that holds the coffee dip without dissolving. Most diet cookies turn to mush — these stay structural overnight.`,image:`/images/brands/highkey-vanilla-wafers.jpg`,url:`https://www.highkey.com/products/mini-cookies-vanilla-wafer`},{name:`PEScience`,item:`Select Protein (Vanilla)`,why:`Whey+casein blend thickens better than pure isolate. Isolate goes chalky in dairy. The blend is why this tastes like cheesecake, not a shake.`,image:`/images/brands/pescience-vanilla.jpg`,url:`https://www.pescience.com/products/select-protein`},{name:`Fage`,item:`Total 0% Greek Yogurt`,why:`The 0% yogurt is intentional — it lets Neufchâtel do all the fat work. Full-fat yogurt pushes the dessert over the macro budget.`,image:`/images/brands/fage-yogurt.jpg`,url:`https://www.fageusa.com/products/yogurts/total-plain/`},{name:`Daisy`,item:`2% Reduced Fat Cottage Cheese`,why:`The 2% is the right fat ratio for mouthfeel — 0% tastes hollow, 4% pushes calories. Daisy specifically because the curd is small enough to blend silky.`,image:`/images/brands/daisy-cottage-cheese-2pct.jpg`,url:`https://www.daisybrand.com/our-products/cottage-cheese-tubs/`},{name:`Philadelphia`,item:`Neufchâtel Cheese (1/3 less fat than cream cheese)`,why:`The fat carrier. Real cream cheese is over-budget; 1/3-less-fat has the wrong texture. Neufchâtel is the goldilocks — 65 cal per ounce, real richness, dessert-correct mouthfeel.`,image:`/images/brands/philadelphia-neufchatel.jpg`,url:`https://www.philadelphiacreamcheese.com/products/philadelphia-neufchatel-cheese-1-3-less-fat-than-cream-cheese-8-oz-brick/`},{name:`Whole Earth`,item:`Allulose + Monk Fruit Sweetener`,why:`Allulose dissolves clean and won't crystallize overnight in the chilled cream. Monk fruit adds sweetness without the bitter aftertaste of pure stevia.`,image:`/images/brands/whole-earth-allulose-monk.jpg`,url:`https://wholeearth.com/products/allulose-monk-fruit-sweetener-blend`},{name:`Ghirardelli`,item:`Premium Unsweetened Cocoa Powder`,why:`Heavy cocoa dust on top is doing psychological work — it's what makes the dessert read 'tiramisu' instead of 'protein parfait'. Don't skip it, don't go light.`,image:`/images/brands/ghirardelli-cocoa.jpg`,url:`https://www.ghirardelli.com/premium-baking-cocoa-unsweetened-cocoa-powder-8-oz-can-62100.html`},{name:`Nescafé`,item:`Taster's Choice House Blend Instant Coffee`,why:`Mixed into the cream for tiramisu perception and to mellow the bitterness of brewed dip coffee. Dissolves instant, deep roast.`,image:`/images/brands/nescafe-tasters-choice.jpg`,url:`https://www.nescafe.com/us/coffees/instant-coffees/tasters-choice/house-blend`}],mealPrep:{storage:`Cover each container tightly (lid or plastic wrap) and refrigerate. Don't dust cocoa until right before eating — pre-dusted cocoa absorbs cream moisture and goes patchy.`,lasts:`4 days refrigerated. Texture peaks on Day 2 and stays excellent through Day 4. Don't freeze — wafers turn weird on thaw.`,reheat:`None. Eat cold straight from the fridge — that's the format.`}},{id:`high-protein-brownie-ice-cream-bowl`,title:`High-Protein Brownie Ice Cream Bowl`,tagline:`330 cal / 33g protein dessert hack. 1 Prime Bites brownie warmed 20 sec + 1/3 pint Frozen One Chocolate protein ice cream. Eats in 2 min.`,heroImage:`/images/high-protein-brownie-ice-cream-bowl/hero-brownie-ice-cream-bowl.webp`,prepImage:`/images/high-protein-brownie-ice-cream-bowl/context-protein-brownie-square.webp`,socialImages:[`/images/high-protein-brownie-ice-cream-bowl/context-protein-brownie-square.webp`,`/images/high-protein-brownie-ice-cream-bowl/context-frozen-one-dutch-chocolate.webp`,`/images/high-protein-brownie-ice-cream-bowl/step-01-brownie-in-bowl.webp`,`/images/high-protein-brownie-ice-cream-bowl/step-02-microwave-brownie.webp`,`/images/high-protein-brownie-ice-cream-bowl/step-03-add-ice-cream.webp`],flavorProfile:`Warm fudgy brownie + cold creamy chocolate protein ice cream = textural contrast + the melting moment where the ice cream starts to sink into the warm brownie. Reads as dessert, lands as a macro snack.`,calories:330,caloriesPerServing:330,protein:33,proteinPerServing:33,servings:1,time:`2 min`,bestFor:[`Dessert`,`Snack`,`Powerup`,`High protein`,`Microwave`,`Sweet craving`,`Macro-friendly`],useThisWhen:`The 2-minute sweet-craving fix that doesn't blow the macro day. 1 Prime Bites brownie + 1/3 pint chocolate protein ice cream = 330 cal / 33g protein. Sibling recipe to the [Chocolate Protein Brownie Bowl](/cookbook/chocolate-protein-brownie-bowl) — same Prime Bites base, swap the Bootylicious muffin cup for cold ice cream. Adult-only macro dessert; not designed for kids.`,flavorTarget:`Brownie should be WARM (not hot, not room-temp) so the bottom of the ice cream just starts to soften on contact. 20 sec at 1000W microwave is the sweet spot — long enough to soften the brownie's interior, short enough that the top doesn't dry out. Cold ice cream on warm brownie creates the temperature delta that makes this read as restaurant dessert, not 'health bar with ice cream'.`,coreRatio:`1 Prime Bites brownie + 1/3 of a pint of any chocolate protein ice cream that hits at least 1g protein per 10 cal (Frozen One Chocolate, Protein Pints Chocolate, etc.). This is the system — the ≥1g/10cal density rule is what locks the macro profile at 330 cal / 33g protein.`,ingredients:[`1 Prime Bites Protein Brownie (any flavor — S'mores, Cookie Dough, Chocolate Glazed Donut, Birthday Cake, Mint Chocolate, etc. ~180-220 cal / 19g protein per brownie)`,`1/3 pint Frozen One Chocolate Protein Ice Cream (or any chocolate protein ice cream with ≥1g protein per 10 cal — Protein Pints Chocolate works too; see substitutions)`],steps:[{text:`BROWNIE INTO BOWL: Unwrap 1 Prime Bites brownie. Drop the brownie square into a microwave-safe bowl (small ceramic bowl ~12 oz is ideal — leaves room for the ice cream scoop on top).`,image:`/images/high-protein-brownie-ice-cream-bowl/step-01-brownie-in-bowl.webp`},{text:`MICROWAVE 20 SEC: On high. 20 seconds at ~1000W is the sweet spot — brownie's interior softens + warms without the top drying out. If your microwave is lower power, try 25 sec; if it runs hot, 15 sec + check.`,image:`/images/high-protein-brownie-ice-cream-bowl/step-02-microwave-brownie.webp`},{text:`ADD ICE CREAM: While the brownie is warm, scoop ~1/3 pint (≈140g, about 2 generous scoops) of Frozen One Chocolate protein ice cream directly on top of the warm brownie. The cold-on-warm contrast is the entire dessert moment.`,image:`/images/high-protein-brownie-ice-cream-bowl/step-03-add-ice-cream.webp`},`EAT IMMEDIATELY: The ice cream starts melting into the warm brownie within 30-60 seconds. Eat while the brownie is warm + the ice cream is still scoopable but partially softening on the bottom. Don't let it sit — it loses the textural contrast that makes it work.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Brownie came out dry / overcooked on top`,fix:`20 sec was too long for your microwave. Drop to 15 sec next time. Rescue: pour 1 tsp Fairlife milk over the brownie before adding the ice cream — softens the top + the milk integrates with the melting ice cream.`},{problem:`Brownie still feels cold-firm after microwave`,fix:`Microwave is lower-watt than 1000W (some compact units are 700-800W). Add 5 sec + check. Should feel warm to the touch + slightly soft in the center, not piping hot.`},{problem:`Ice cream rock-hard out of the freezer`,fix:`Let the pint sit at room temp 2-3 min before scooping. Frozen One + Protein Pints both freeze harder than dairy ice cream (no air whipped in to lighten). Or run the scoop under warm water.`},{problem:`Macros came in higher than 330 / 33`,fix:`Most likely cause: (1) over-scooped the ice cream (1/3 pint = ~140g, not half the pint), (2) used a higher-cal Prime Bites flavor (Chocolate Glazed Donut is ~220 cal vs Mint Chocolate at ~180), or (3) added a topping (don't — the recipe is just brownie + ice cream). Stick to 1 brownie + 1/3 pint.`},{problem:`Subbed a different protein ice cream — macros don't line up`,fix:`The ≥1g protein per 10 cal rule is the brand-selection lock. Halo Top Protein hits it; regular Halo Top doesn't. Ninja Creami homemade hits it if you build it right. Most premium 'protein ice cream' brands hit it (Frozen One, Protein Pints, Wink, Magic Spoon Ice Cream). If your pint is 280 cal / 20g protein, that's only 0.7g/10cal — drops the combo to ~310 cal / 26g protein.`}],brands:[{name:`Prime Bites`,item:`Protein Brownie (any flavor — 19g protein, 5g collagen, low sugar, 12-pack variety; ~180-220 cal per 65g brownie depending on flavor)`,why:`Individually-wrapped protein brownie that actually tastes like brownie (not protein bar). The warm-bake step IS the magic — Prime Bites holds up to 20 sec microwave without falling apart. Cross-recipe with the Chocolate Protein Brownie Bowl in the cookbook. Any flavor works.`,image:`/images/brands/prime-bites-smores-brownie.png`,url:`https://primebites.com/`},{name:`Frozen One`,item:`Chocolate Protein Ice Cream (1 pt — 405 cal / 40g protein per pint, ~1g protein per 10 cal density)`,why:`Real ice cream texture with the protein density that makes the combo math work. Other flavors (Peanut Butter Chip, Apple Pie) work too but chocolate is the canonical pairing. Sub Protein Pints Chocolate or any chocolate protein ice cream hitting ≥1g protein per 10 cal.`,image:`/images/brands/frozen-one-chocolate-protein-ice-cream.png`,url:`https://www.frozen-one.com/flavors`}],macroHonesty:`Per bowl (~330 cal / 33g protein) MacroFactor-tracked. Component breakdown: 1 Prime Bites brownie (mid-range, ~200 cal / 19g protein — actual range 180-220 cal depending on flavor) + 1/3 pint Frozen One Chocolate (~135 cal / 13.3g protein per 1/3 of 405 cal / 40g pint) = ~335 cal / 32.3g protein. Headline 330 / 33 rounded. Flagged estimated because (1) Prime Bites flavor lot varies cal slightly (180-220), (2) scoop weight varies, (3) microwave timing affects nothing macro-wise but the textural anchor. The ≥1g protein per 10 cal rule for ice cream is the brand-selection lock that holds the macro at 33g — any chocolate protein ice cream meeting the density floor will land in the 32-34g protein range with this BOM.`,mealPrep:{storage:`N/A — make per serving. Both brownie + ice cream are shelf/freezer stable individually for weeks/months.`,lasts:`Prime Bites brownies: months at room temp (per package date). Frozen One pints: months in the freezer (per package date). The assembled bowl doesn't store — eat immediately.`,reheat:`N/A — make fresh. The cold-on-warm temperature contrast IS the dessert; reheating a leftover bowl wrecks it.`}},{id:`protein-cheesecake-frosting`,title:`Protein Cheesecake Frosting`,tagline:`Cheesecake-style frosting that lives in a jar. 30g serving = 60 cal / 6g protein. 15 servings per batch, 5-min blend, no cook.`,heroImage:`/images/protein-cheesecake-frosting/hero-pouring-frosting.webp`,prepImage:`/images/protein-cheesecake-frosting/context-siggis-skyr.webp`,socialImages:[`/images/protein-cheesecake-frosting/context-siggis-skyr.webp`,`/images/protein-cheesecake-frosting/context-philadelphia-light-cream-cheese.webp`,`/images/protein-cheesecake-frosting/context-pescience-vanilla.webp`,`/images/protein-cheesecake-frosting/step-cheesecake-pudding-mix.webp`,`/images/protein-cheesecake-frosting/step-blend-smooth.webp`,`/images/protein-cheesecake-frosting/step-transfer-frosting.webp`,`/images/protein-cheesecake-frosting/final-frosting-jar.webp`],flavorProfile:`Creamy cheesecake tang + vanilla sweetness, glossy pourable texture. Reads as dessert frosting; eats as a macro-friendly spoonable spread. Smoother than yogurt, looser than cream-cheese frosting.`,calories:900,caloriesPerServing:60,protein:90,proteinPerServing:6,servings:15,time:`5 min`,bestFor:[`Dessert`,`Frosting`,`Topping`,`Powerup`,`High protein`,`No-cook`,`Adults`,`Meal prep`],useThisWhen:`You want cheesecake flavor on top of something (protein brownie, fruit bowl, pancakes, toast, oats, ice cream) but don't want to blow the macro budget. 30g scoop = 60 cal / 6g protein. Makes 15 servings in 5 min — one blender, one jar, lives in the fridge 5 days.`,flavorTarget:`Pourable cheesecake frosting consistency — thicker than melted ice cream, looser than buttercream. Vanilla-cheesecake-tang flavor lead; the Jell-O cheesecake pudding mix is what locks in the 'this tastes like cheesecake' read. If it sets too thick after refrigeration overnight, stir before serving — does NOT add liquid.`,coreRatio:`225g Siggi's 0% Plain Skyr + 215g Philadelphia 1/3 Less Fat + 15g Jell-O Sugar-Free Cheesecake Pudding Mix + 15g Whole Earth Monk Fruit Erythritol + 62g (2 scoops) PEScience Select Gourmet Vanilla. Blend, jar, refrigerate. 15 servings × 30g each = 60 cal / 6g protein per scoop.`,ingredients:[`225g Siggi's 0% Plain Skyr`,`215g Philadelphia 1/3 Less Fat Cream Cheese (1 brick — Neufchâtel)`,`15g Jell-O Sugar-Free Cheesecake Instant Pudding Mix (about half a 1 oz box)`,`15g Whole Earth Monk Fruit Erythritol Blend`,`62g PEScience Select Gourmet Vanilla Protein Powder (2 scoops)`],steps:[{text:`ADD SKYR: 225g Siggi's 0% Plain Skyr into a blender cup or small food processor.`,image:`/images/protein-cheesecake-frosting/context-siggis-skyr.webp`},{text:`ADD CREAM CHEESE: 215g Philadelphia 1/3 Less Fat Cream Cheese on top of the skyr. Best if the cream cheese is at room temperature — soft cream cheese blends without leaving pockets.`,image:`/images/protein-cheesecake-frosting/context-philadelphia-light-cream-cheese.webp`},{text:`ADD PUDDING + SWEETENER: 15g Jell-O Sugar-Free Cheesecake Instant Pudding Mix (about half a 1 oz box) + 15g Whole Earth Monk Fruit Erythritol Blend. Drop both in dry — they hydrate during the blend.`,image:`/images/protein-cheesecake-frosting/step-cheesecake-pudding-mix.webp`},{text:`ADD VANILLA PROTEIN: 62g PEScience Select Gourmet Vanilla Protein Powder (2 scoops). Drop on top last so it doesn't poof out when the blender starts.`,image:`/images/protein-cheesecake-frosting/context-pescience-vanilla.webp`},{text:`BLEND SMOOTH: 30-60 sec on high until thick, glossy, and pourable. Stop + scrape down the sides at 30 sec if needed — protein powder can stick to the walls. Should look like thick cake frosting that just barely flows.`,image:`/images/protein-cheesecake-frosting/step-blend-smooth.webp`},{text:`TRANSFER TO JAR: Spoon into a clean glass jar (16 oz mason jar fits the batch perfectly with a bit of headroom). Scraping with a spatula = your batch math; what stays in the blender = the 80g you lose to transfer.`,image:`/images/protein-cheesecake-frosting/step-transfer-frosting.webp`},{text:`REFRIGERATE: Seal the jar. Refrigerate. The texture sets slightly firmer overnight — stir before serving on day 2+. Eat within 5 days.`,image:`/images/protein-cheesecake-frosting/final-frosting-jar.webp`}],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Frosting is grainy / lumpy after blending`,fix:`Cream cheese was too cold OR you didn't blend long enough. Bring cream cheese to room temp before blending (10-15 min on the counter). Blend 60-90 sec total + scrape down halfway. If still grainy, the issue is usually the protein powder — switch to a finer-mill brand or pre-mix the powder with 2 tbsp of the skyr first.`},{problem:`Frosting is too thick / won't pour`,fix:`After overnight refrigeration the protein-powder thickening agents fully hydrate. Stir vigorously before serving. Do NOT add water or milk — it dilutes the flavor without restoring the texture. The thick texture spreads fine on toast / brownies / pancakes.`},{problem:`Frosting is too thin / runs off the spoon`,fix:`Either you used a different cream cheese (full-fat Philly is thicker; non-Philly brands vary) OR your blender ran hot and broke the emulsion. Add 7g more Jell-O Sugar-Free Cheesecake Pudding Mix + blend 15 sec — pudding is the thickening agent.`},{problem:`Tastes flat / not cheesecake-y enough`,fix:`Light Jell-O dose. Bump to 20g pudding mix next batch (still under the full 28g 1 oz box). The pudding mix is what carries the 'cheesecake' flavor signal — protein powder alone gives generic vanilla.`},{problem:`Macros came in higher than 60 cal / 30g`,fix:`Most likely cause: (1) used full-fat Philadelphia instead of 1/3 Less Fat (adds ~80 cal across the batch ≈ 5 cal/serving), (2) used Siggi's 4% instead of 0% (adds 60 cal/batch), or (3) added sugar/honey to taste-correct. The macro architecture is locked on the exact 1/3 Less Fat Philly + Siggi's 0% combo.`},{problem:`Batch yields less than 15 servings`,fix:`Normal — raw ingredients total 532g but yielded batch is ~450g after blender transfer loss (~15% sticks to the walls + lid). The per-serving macros assume ~450g yield. If you want exactly 17-18 × 30g servings, scrape the blender hard.`}],brands:[{name:`Siggi's`,item:`0% Plain Skyr (24 oz tub — strained Icelandic-style yogurt, 12g protein / 60 cal per 5.3 oz; 225g = ~135 cal / 25g protein)`,why:`The cheesecake-tang base. Strained skyr is thicker + tangier than Greek yogurt — closer to cream-cheese profile. PLAIN variant only (vanilla adds sugar + wrecks the savory-cheesecake balance). Cross-recipe with the Grillo's pickle dip (id grillos-pickle-dip-protein-style).`,image:`/images/brands/siggis-plain-nonfat-skyr.webp`,url:`https://siggis.com/product/plain-nonfat/`},{name:`Philadelphia`,item:`1/3 Less Fat Cream Cheese, 8 oz brick (Neufchâtel — ~245 cal / 8g protein per 100g, used 215g)`,why:`Cheesecake flavor anchor. The 1/3 Less Fat variant (NOT full-fat, NOT fat-free) is the macro-architecture sweet spot — thick enough for cheesecake texture, lean enough to hit 60 cal/serving. Don't sub fat-free (texture goes gummy) or full-fat (adds 80+ cal/batch).`,image:`/images/brands/philadelphia-1-3-less-fat-cream-cheese.jpg`,url:`https://www.heb.com/product-detail/philadelphia-1-3-less-fat-cream-cheese/81237`},{name:`Jell-O`,item:`Sugar-Free Cheesecake Instant Pudding Mix, 1 oz box (use 15g ≈ half a box — ~25 cal / 0g protein)`,why:`The 'this tastes like cheesecake' lock. 15g is half a 28g box — enough to flavor + thicken without adding sugar. The Sugar-Free / Zero-Sugar variant is the macro-clean choice; regular Jell-O has 100+ cal of sugar per box.`,image:`/images/brands/jello-cheesecake-sugar-free-pudding.jpg`,url:`https://www.kraftheinz.com/jell-o/products/00043000208120-zero-sugar-cheesecake-flavor-instant-pudding-pie-filling`},{name:`Whole Earth`,item:`Monk Fruit with Erythritol Sweetener Blend (12 oz pouch or 32 oz bag — 0 cal sweetener, used 15g)`,why:`Adds the cheesecake sweetness without sugar. 1:1 sugar replacement, zero glycemic index, plant-based. Sub Lakanto Classic Monk Fruit, Swerve Granular, or any monk-fruit-erythritol blend — all work equivalently at 15g.`,image:`/images/brands/whole-earth-monk-fruit-erythritol.webp`,url:`https://wholeearthsweetener.com/products/monk-fruit-blend-bag`},{name:`PEScience`,item:`Select Gourmet Vanilla Protein (24g protein per 31g scoop — used 62g / 2 scoops, ~220 cal / 48g protein)`,why:`Whey + casein blend with smooth-vanilla flavor (NOT the 'cake notes' of their Cake Pop flavor — Gourmet Vanilla is the cleaner pairing for a cheesecake frosting). Cross-recipe with the Chocolate Protein Brownie Bowl + Mocha Brownie Creami in the cookbook. Sub any vanilla whey+casein blend — straight whey isolate is grittier in cold applications.`,image:`/images/brands/pescience-select-vanilla.jpg`,url:`https://pescience.com/products/select-protein`}],macroHonesty:`Per 30g serving (60 cal / 6g protein) MacroFactor-tracked. Batch component math: 225g Siggi's 0% (~135 cal / 25P) + 215g Philadelphia 1/3 Less Fat (~520 cal / 18P) + 15g Jell-O Sugar-Free Pudding (~25 cal / 0P) + 15g Whole Earth Monk Fruit (~0 cal) + 62g PEScience Vanilla (~220 cal / 48P) ≈ 900 cal / 91P for ~450g yielded batch. 450g ÷ 15 servings = 30g each → 60 cal / 6.1P per 30g scoop. **Yield note:** raw ingredient weights total 532g, but yielded batch is ~450g after the ~15% transfer/scraping loss to blender walls + lid + spatula. That 82g delta is normal for thick frosting recipes — not a math error. If you scrape the blender unusually hard, the batch may stretch to 17-18 servings instead of 15. Macros stay 60 cal / 6g protein per 30g regardless of how many servings the batch actually yields.`,mealPrep:{storage:`Sealed glass jar in the fridge (16 oz mason fits the batch). Texture sets slightly firmer overnight — stir before serving on day 2+.`,lasts:`5 days refrigerated. Don't freeze — texture breaks on thaw.`,reheat:`N/A — eaten cold/room temp. Spoon directly from jar onto whatever you're topping.`}},{id:`high-protein-viral-dot-cake`,title:`High-Protein Viral Dot Cake`,tagline:`Viral dot cake, protein version. 3 ramekin cakes per batch, 250 cal / 25g protein each (base 170/19 + cheesecake frosting + sprinkles).`,heroImage:`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/hero-finished-dot-cakes.webp`,prepImage:`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/context-pescience-vanilla.webp`,socialImages:[`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/context-pescience-vanilla.webp`,`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/context-fairlife-fat-free-milk.webp`,`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/context-happy-egg.webp`,`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/step-baking-powder.webp`,`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/step-mix-batter.webp`,`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/step-fill-ramekins.webp`,`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/step-baked-cakes.webp`,`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/step-cheesecake-frosting.webp`,`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/step-sprinkle-pour.webp`,`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/step-final-scoop.webp`],flavorProfile:`Soft golden vanilla protein snack cake with a creamy cheesecake-frosting top and crunchy rainbow nonpareil sprinkle coat. The cake center stays slightly liquidy (intentional — molten center is the viral dot cake signature). Reads as funfetti birthday cake; eats as a macro-friendly dessert.`,calories:750,caloriesPerServing:250,protein:75,proteinPerServing:25,servings:3,time:`25 min`,bestFor:[`Dessert`,`Powerup`,`High protein`,`Viral`,`Baked`,`Make-ahead`,`Adults`,`Birthday-energy`],useThisWhen:`You saw the viral dot cake on TikTok and want the protein version. 3 ramekin cakes per batch, 250 cal / 25g protein each finished. Bake the bases (15 min) → chill → top with one 30g serving of [Protein Cheesecake Frosting](/cookbook/protein-cheesecake-frosting) per cake → press into rainbow nonpareils. The frosted top + sprinkle coat is the visual hook; the liquidy center is the texture payoff.`,flavorTarget:`Cake center should be **liquidy-soft, not set** (the 15-min bake is intentionally short — viral dot cake is supposed to have a molten center). Top should be lightly golden, smooth enough to hold a flat frosting layer. Frosting + sprinkle coat reads like funfetti birthday cake. Don't overbake — past 18 min the center dries out and you lose the moment.`,coreRatio:`62g PEScience Select Gourmet Vanilla (2 scoops) + 3 large eggs + 1/4 cup Fairlife Fat-Free + 45g AP flour + 15g Whole Earth Monk Fruit Erythritol + 15g Jell-O Sugar-Free Vanilla Pudding Mix + 1 tsp Clabber Girl baking powder + 1 tsp vanilla extract. Yields batter for 4 servings (170 cal / 19g protein each); divided into 3 ramekins with the tops trimmed flat after baking — the trimmed scraps = the 4th serving (snack on its own or add to a parfait, ~170 cal / 19g protein unfrosted).`,ingredients:[`2 scoops (62g) PEScience Select Gourmet Vanilla Protein Powder`,`3 large Happy Egg Co Organic Free-Range Eggs`,`1/4 cup (60ml) Fairlife Fat-Free Ultra-Filtered Milk`,`45g all-purpose flour`,`15g Whole Earth Monk Fruit Erythritol Sweetener Blend`,`15g Jell-O Sugar-Free Vanilla Instant Pudding Mix (about half a 1 oz box)`,`1 tsp Clabber Girl Double-Acting Baking Powder`,`1 tsp vanilla extract`,`Cooking spray (for ramekins)`,{text:`1 serving (30g) Protein Cheesecake Frosting per cake — 60 cal / 6g protein each`,link:`/cookbook/protein-cheesecake-frosting`},`Rainbow nonpareil sprinkles, ~5g per cake (~20 cal/cake)`],steps:[`PREHEAT: Oven to 350°F. Spray 3 ramekins (6-8 oz size) with cooking spray.`,{text:`DRY MIX: In a mixing bowl on a scale, combine 62g PEScience Vanilla + 45g AP flour + 15g Whole Earth Monk Fruit Erythritol + 15g Jell-O Sugar-Free Vanilla Pudding Mix + 1 tsp Clabber Girl baking powder. Whisk dry to break up any protein-powder clumps.`,image:`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/step-baking-powder.webp`},{text:`WET MIX: In a separate bowl, whisk 3 eggs + 1/4 cup Fairlife + 1 tsp vanilla extract until uniform.`,image:`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/context-happy-egg.webp`},{text:`COMBINE: Pour the wet into the dry. Whisk until smooth — should be thick cake batter that just barely flows off the whisk. Don't overmix; lumps cook out.`,image:`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/step-mix-batter.webp`},{text:`FILL RAMEKINS: Divide batter evenly across 3 ramekins. Smooth the tops with a spatula. Ramekins should be ~3/4 full — the cakes rise then settle.`,image:`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/step-fill-ramekins.webp`},{text:`BAKE 350°F × 15 MIN: Tops should be golden + spring back lightly. Centers should still feel SOFT to the touch — the liquidy-molten center is the viral dot cake signature. Past 18 min = dry center = lost moment.`,image:`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/step-baked-cakes.webp`},`COOL + TRIM: Let ramekins cool 10 min on a wire rack, then chill in the fridge 30 min (or overnight). Once chilled, slice the domed top off each cake with a serrated knife so the surface is flat for frosting. The trimmed scraps = the 4th serving (snack them, freeze for parfaits, or compost).`,{text:`FROST: Spread one 30g serving of [Protein Cheesecake Frosting](/cookbook/protein-cheesecake-frosting) over each flat-trimmed cake top. Smooth to the edges. Thick frosting holds peaks; thin frosting pools — refer to the parent frosting recipe troubleshooting if it's too thin.`,image:`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/step-cheesecake-frosting.webp`},{text:`SPRINKLE DIP: Pour ~5g rainbow nonpareils onto a shallow plate. Press the frosted top of each cake into the sprinkles to coat. Lift gently — frosting holds the sprinkles in place.`,image:`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/step-sprinkle-pour.webp`},{text:`SCOOP + EAT: Best within 2 hours of frosting (sprinkle crunch fades after 4-6 hours as moisture migrates). Scoop through the sprinkle top + frosting + cake — molten center reveals itself on the spoon.`,image:`/images/high-protein-viral-dot-cake/step-final-scoop.webp`}],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Center came out fully baked / not liquidy`,fix:`Overbaked. 15 min @ 350°F is the floor — if your oven runs hot, drop to 13 min. The center is SUPPOSED to be soft/molten — that's the viral dot cake signature. Once a center fully sets, you can't un-set it.`},{problem:`Batter overflowed the ramekins`,fix:`You used smaller ramekins (4 oz instead of 6-8 oz). The recipe yields enough batter for 3 standard 6-8 oz ramekins. With smaller ramekins, divide across 4 — or trim the rims more aggressively after baking.`},{problem:`Cake collapsed after pulling from oven`,fix:`Slight collapse is fine — the center moisture pulls the top down a bit. Excessive collapse = underbaked. Add 2-3 min next time + check again at 13 min.`},{problem:`Frosting won't stick / slides off`,fix:`Cakes weren't fully chilled before frosting. The frosting needs cold cake to grip. Chill another 15-20 min then frost. Or thicken the frosting — see the parent recipe troubleshooting.`},{problem:`Sprinkles fall off / won't coat`,fix:`Frosting layer is too thin. Use the full 30g per cake (not less). Press the frosted top INTO the sprinkles with light pressure — don't sprinkle on top, that doesn't bond.`},{problem:`Macros came in higher than 250 cal / cake`,fix:`Most likely cause: (1) heavier sprinkle dose (>5g per cake adds ~5 cal per extra gram), (2) larger frosting portion (40g instead of 30g = +20 cal). The 250 / 25 anchor assumes 1 trimmed cake + 30g frosting + 5g sprinkles. Stick to those weights.`}],brands:[{name:`PEScience`,item:`Select Gourmet Vanilla Protein (24g protein per 31g scoop — 2 scoops / 62g per batter)`,why:`Whey + casein blend that bakes into actual cake texture (not the gritty/rubber result you get from straight whey isolate when heated). Gourmet Vanilla is the smooth-vanilla flavor lane — NOT the Cake Pop flavor (too sweet on top of pudding mix + monk fruit). Cross-recipe with the Protein Cheesecake Frosting + Chocolate Protein Brownie Bowl + Mocha Brownie Creami.`,image:`/images/brands/pescience-select-vanilla.jpg`,url:`https://pescience.com/products/select-protein`},{name:`Happy Egg Co.`,item:`Organic Free-Range Large Brown Eggs, dozen carton (~70 cal / 6g protein per large egg — 3 eggs per batch)`,why:`Pastured + USDA Organic — rich orange yolks. The yolk fat is what gives the cake the soft custard-like center that holds the molten texture at 15 min. Sub any large eggs; the protein math holds regardless of farm.`,image:`/images/brands/happy-egg-organic-eggs.jpg`,url:`https://happyegg.com/products/organic-eggs`},{name:`Fairlife`,item:`Fat-Free Ultra-Filtered Milk, 1/4 cup (~22 cal / 2g protein per 1/4 cup)`,why:`Lactose-free + 50% more protein than regular milk. Small amount in the batter for hydration + protein bump. Cross-recipe staple across the cookbook (cereal hack, cheesecake frosting, muffin cup powerup).`,image:`/images/brands/fairlife-milk.png`,url:`https://fairlife.com/ultra-filtered-milk/fat-free-skim-milk/`},{name:`Whole Earth`,item:`Monk Fruit with Erythritol Sweetener Blend (15g per batter)`,why:`1:1 sugar substitute. 0 cal, zero glycemic. The sweetener that keeps the cake at 170 cal / serving without losing the dessert flavor. Sub Lakanto, Swerve, or any monk-fruit-erythritol blend.`,image:`/images/brands/whole-earth-monk-fruit-erythritol.webp`,url:`https://wholeearthsweetener.com/products/monk-fruit-blend-bag`},{name:`Jell-O`,item:`Sugar-Free Vanilla Instant Pudding Mix, 1 oz box (15g per batter = half a box)`,why:`Locks in the vanilla cake flavor + helps the cake set without adding sugar. Cross-recipe with the Protein Cheesecake Frosting (uses the cheesecake variant). The Vanilla pudding mix + monk fruit combo is what makes a protein cake taste like cake, not a protein bar.`,image:`/images/brands/jello-cheesecake-sugar-free-pudding.jpg`,url:`https://www.kraftheinz.com/jell-o/products/`},{name:`Clabber Girl`,item:`Double-Acting Baking Powder, 8.1 oz can (1 tsp per batter — gluten-free, no aluminum)`,why:`Standard baking-powder leavening. Double-acting = activates twice (once when wet, once when heated) for consistent rise. Sub any gluten-free baking powder.`,image:`/images/brands/clabber-girl-baking-powder.jpg`,url:`https://www.target.com/p/clabber-girl-gluten-free-double-acting-baking-powder-8-1oz/-/A-14770673`},{name:`Protein Cheesecake Frosting`,item:`Parent recipe — 60 cal / 6g protein per 30g serving, makes 15 servings per batch`,why:`The frosting topping. Make a batch via the parent recipe and you have enough for ~5 batches of dot cakes (15 servings ÷ 3 cakes per batch). Cross-recipe link is the whole architecture here — both recipes share the PEScience + Jell-O + Whole Earth brand stack.`,image:`/images/protein-cheesecake-frosting/hero-pouring-frosting.webp`,url:`/cookbook/protein-cheesecake-frosting`}],macroHonesty:`Per finished cake (~250 cal / 25g protein) MacroFactor-tracked. Component breakdown per cake: base cake portion ~170 cal / 19g protein + 30g Protein Cheesecake Frosting ~60 cal / 6g protein + ~5g rainbow nonpareils ~20 cal / 0g protein = 250 cal / 25g protein per cake. Batter math (yields 4 servings of base cake, 3 of which are frosted into finished cakes; the 4th is the trimmed-top scrap from the 3 ramekins): 62g PEScience (~220 cal / 48P) + 3 eggs (~210 cal / 18P) + 1/4 cup Fairlife (~22 cal / 2P) + 45g AP flour (~165 cal / 5P) + 15g Whole Earth (~0 cal) + 15g Jell-O SF Pudding (~25 cal / 0P) + 1 tsp baking powder + 1 tsp vanilla ≈ 642 cal / 73P batter total ÷ 4 servings = 160 cal / 18.3P per base-cake serving. Per Tushar's MacroFactor log this rounds to 170 / 19. Flagged estimated because (1) flour brand varies cal slightly, (2) sprinkle dose is eyeballed, (3) cheesecake frosting macros are themselves estimated (see parent recipe). The 250 / 25 anchor holds for 1 trimmed cake + 30g frosting + 5g sprinkles.`,mealPrep:{storage:`Bake the cakes ahead, chill un-frosted up to 3 days in airtight container. Frost + sprinkle right before serving — sprinkles lose their crunch within 4-6 hours of contact with frosting moisture.`,lasts:`Un-frosted cakes: 3 days refrigerated, 1 month frozen. Frosted + sprinkled cakes: best within 2 hours; OK overnight but sprinkles soften. Trimmed-top scraps: 2-3 days in airtight container as a snack.`,reheat:`Don't reheat frosted cakes (frosting breaks). For unfrosted: microwave 10-15 sec to soften the center back to liquidy if eaten cold. Best at chilled-to-room-temp.`}}],i=[{id:`bone-broth-rice`,title:`Bone Broth Rice`,tagline:`Hack-on-hand. 8 servings of rice that quietly carries protein.`,heroImage:`/images/spicy-umami-fried-rice/prep.webp`,flavorProfile:`Clean savory rice, deep chicken-broth backbone — neutral enough to take any sauce, flavorful enough to eat solo.`,calories:1400,caloriesPerServing:175,protein:72,proteinPerServing:9,servings:8,time:`5 min prep + 20 min cook`,bestFor:[`Fried rice base`,`Bowl base (rice + protein + sauce)`,`Stir-fry side`,`Quick congee (loosen with extra broth + soft egg)`,`Make-ahead meal prep`],useThisWhen:`You want to invest 25 minutes once and have 8 servings of better-than-plain rice sitting in the fridge. The bone broth swap costs nothing in time and quietly buys you ~9g protein per serving on top of the rice's normal macros. Once it's made, you don't think about rice for the rest of the week.`,flavorTarget:`Same texture as good cooked rice (separate grains, not mushy), but with a clean savory backbone instead of nothing. Tastes balanced solo with a splash of soy + chives, AND disappears into fried rice / bowls without fighting the sauce.`,splitNote:{adult:`Use freely as a base for anything — fried rice, bowls, eaten solo with soy + chili oil + chives.`,kid:`Kids eat half a serving plain — just reheat with a splash of water. Bone broth makes plain rice taste 'more real' to kids who normally find unseasoned rice boring. Pair with raw mini sweet peppers on the side for the freshness/crunch.`},ingredients:[`2 cups long-grain white rice (basmati or jasmine — basmati separates better for fried rice)`,`4 cups Kirkland Organic Chicken Bone Broth`],steps:[`RINSE: Rinse 2 cups rice under cold water until the water runs clear-ish. Two minutes. This removes excess starch and is the single biggest factor between 'separate grains' and 'sticky mush.'`,`COMBINE: Add rinsed rice + 4 cups Kirkland chicken bone broth to a heavy-bottom pot or rice cooker. No salt — the bone broth carries the salt.`,`COOK: Stovetop — bring to a boil over high heat, then cover and reduce to low. 18-20 minutes, lid stays on. Rice cooker — just hit the white rice button.`,`REST: 10 minutes off heat, lid on. Don't skip — this is when the steam finishes the inside of each grain.`,`FLUFF + COOL: Fork-fluff to break up clumps. For fried rice usage, spread on a sheet pan to cool fast, then fridge overnight (cold rice fries better than warm rice).`,`STORE: 5-6 days in an airtight container in the fridge. Reheats fine in microwave with a splash of water.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Rice is mushy`,fix:`Skipped the rinse OR ratio is off. 1 part rice : 2 parts liquid is the rule. Rinse to translucent water, measure both.`},{problem:`Rice tastes salty`,fix:`Bone broth varies in sodium. Don't add salt to this recipe — the broth handles it. If your broth is unsalted, add ½ tsp salt and you're fine.`},{problem:`Fried rice still comes out sticky`,fix:`Used warm rice instead of cold. Fridge overnight (or spread on a sheet pan + freezer 30 min) before frying. Cold rice has firmer grain structure and won't gum up the wok.`},{problem:`Want to use brown rice instead`,fix:`Same ratio works. Add 15 min to the cook time. Note the bone broth flavor reads a touch more strongly with brown rice (less starch to dilute it).`}],brands:[{name:`Kirkland`,item:`Organic Chicken Bone Broth (32 oz cartons)`,why:`Tier 3 base. ~9g protein per cup, clean ingredient list, sold in 6-packs at Costco for the price of two single cartons elsewhere. The protein gain over water is free — no extra cook time, no extra dishes, just a swap.`,image:`/images/brands/kirkland-bone-broth.jpg`,url:`https://www.costcobusinessdelivery.com/kirkland-signature-organic-chicken-bone-broth-32-fl-oz,-6-ct.product.100403862.html`}],mealPrep:{storage:`Airtight container, fridge. Spread thin on a sheet pan first to cool quickly — heat in a closed container creates condensation and sticky rice.`,lasts:`5-6 days fridge. Reheats fine with a tablespoon of water in the microwave.`,reheat:`Microwave 60-90 sec per cup with a splash of water and a damp paper towel on top. Or fork-fluff into a hot pan with 1 tsp oil for fried rice.`,chainTo:{slug:`spicy-umami-fried-rice`,title:`Spicy Umami Fried Rice`,note:`Use 3 servings of cold bone broth rice (~2¼ cups cooked) for the base. The rice's neutral savor lets the chili oil + sambal carry the show.`}}},{id:`spicy-umami-fried-rice`,title:`Spicy Umami Fried Rice`,tagline:`Base recipe. Carb-forward fried rice that's complete solo at 371 cal — designed to add a protein when you want a real dinner.`,heroImage:`/images/spicy-umami-fried-rice/hero.webp`,prepImage:`/images/spicy-umami-fried-rice/sauce-mise-en-place.webp`,prepImageCaption:`Sauce mise-en-place — soy + sambal + sesame chili oil + umami punch`,flavorProfile:`Toasted rice, soft egg, fermented chili heat, deep umami finish. Restaurant-takeout satisfaction without the takeout sodium or oil.`,calories:333,caloriesPerServing:333,protein:16,proteinPerServing:5,servings:3,time:`12 min (cold rice required — make Bone Broth Rice ahead)`,bestFor:[`Solo dinner at the 333-cal tier`,`Base for Crispy Chicken (next-day add-on)`,`Base for shrimp / steak / tofu`,`Quick lunch from leftover rice`,`After a workout when carbs + flavor matter more than protein-maxing`],useThisWhen:`You have cold Bone Broth Rice in the fridge (this is mandatory — fresh rice = mushy mess) and you want 12 minutes of stovetop work for a dinner that feels like takeout. Eat it solo at 333 cal / 16g protein, or stack a protein on top for a 500-cal dinner with 35-40g protein.`,flavorTarget:`Layered umami — soy gives salt + depth, sambal gives fermented heat, sesame chili oil gives aroma + nuttiness, Jet Tila's Umami Punch gives the MSG-style amplification that makes takeout fried rice hit. Rice should look lightly toasted and amber-coated, NOT drenched or wet.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full sauce, full sambal. Optional: scatter sliced Thai chili and chili oil on top.`,kid:`Most kids skip fried rice entirely — give them half a serving of plain Bone Broth Rice (microwave 60 sec) + their protein + raw mini sweet peppers instead. The fried rice complexity isn't worth the fight. If they DO want fried rice, halve the sambal and serve in a small bowl flipped onto the plate as a mound (kids respond to playful shapes).`},ingredients:[`--- TIER 3 BASE (REQUIRED COLD) ---`,{text:`3 servings cold Bone Broth Rice (~2¼ cups cooked, made ahead and refrigerated)`,link:`/cookbook/bone-broth-rice`},`--- TIER 2 PROTEIN ---`,`2 large eggs`,`--- TIER 4 FRESHNESS ---`,`2 Thai chilies, finely sliced (mixed into the egg whisk for chili-flecked scramble)`,`2 green onions, chopped`,`Fresh chives, chopped (~2 tbsp)`,`--- COOKING FAT ---`,`2 tsp avocado oil (or any neutral high-smoke-point oil)`,`--- INLINE SAUCE (makes 2 servings sauce, used in this 3-serving recipe — see Smart Upgrades for honest macros note) ---`,`2 tbsp Kikkoman All-Purpose Soy Sauce`,`2 tsp Huy Fong Sambal Oelek`,`2 tsp Dynasty Sesame Chili Oil`,`2 tsp Jet Tila's Umami Punch (Spiceology)`],steps:[{text:`MAKE THE SAUCE: Stir together soy + sambal + sesame chili oil + Umami Punch in a small bowl or ramekin. Set aside. This is the entire 'sauce step' — no cooking, no reduction.`,image:`/images/spicy-umami-fried-rice/sauce-mise-en-place.webp`},{text:`PREP MISE-EN-PLACE: Cold rice in a container, whisk eggs with the sliced Thai chilies, chop chives + green onion. Everything within arm's reach — the actual frying is fast.`,image:`/images/spicy-umami-fried-rice/prep.webp`},{text:`EGGS, FIRST: Heat a wok or large skillet over medium-high. Add 1 tsp oil. Pour in the chili-flecked egg whisk and let it spread into a thin pancake.`,image:`/images/spicy-umami-fried-rice/step1-egg-pour.webp`},{text:`SOFT SCRAMBLE: As the bottom sets (~30 seconds), break it up with the spatula into soft curds. Pull off heat at 80% set — they'll finish from carryover. Slide eggs to the side of the wok OR remove to a plate.`,image:`/images/spicy-umami-fried-rice/step2-eggs-scrambled.webp`},{text:`TOAST THE RICE: Add the remaining 1 tsp oil to the hot wok. Add cold rice. Break up clumps with the spatula but DO NOT stir constantly — let the rice sit for 30-second intervals to develop slight toast on the bottom. Stir, sit, stir, sit. This is where the takeout texture lives.`,image:`/images/spicy-umami-fried-rice/step3-rice-toast.webp`},{text:`POUR THE SAUCE: Pour the sauce around the edge of the wok (so it hits hot metal and sizzles, not directly on the rice). Toss continuously now to coat. Rice should turn light amber, not wet brown. If you see standing liquid, you used too much sauce — keep tossing until it cooks off.`,image:`/images/spicy-umami-fried-rice/step4-sauce-pour.webp`},{text:`FINISH: Return scrambled eggs. Add green onions. Toss 30-60 seconds. Off heat.`,image:`/images/spicy-umami-fried-rice/step5-coated.webp`},{text:`GARNISH AND SERVE: Scatter chopped chives across the top — the green hit matters visually AND lifts the dish. Plate in bowls. Adults: optional extra sliced Thai chili or chili oil drizzle on top. Kids: rice mound in a small bowl, inverted onto the plate. Done.`,image:`/images/spicy-umami-fried-rice/hero.webp`}],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Rice is mushy / clumpy`,fix:`Used fresh-cooked rice. This recipe REQUIRES cold rice. Make Bone Broth Rice ahead and refrigerate overnight (minimum 4 hours / freezer 30 min in a pinch).`},{problem:`Wet brown rice instead of toasty amber`,fix:`Oversauced OR didn't let the sauce cook off. Pour the sauce around the edge of the wok (not center), toss continuously, and keep going until standing liquid is gone.`},{problem:`Flat / bland`,fix:`Skimped on the sambal or the Umami Punch. These are the two flavor amplifiers — go full measure. The soy alone won't carry the dish.`},{problem:`Too salty`,fix:`Bone broth rice already has salt from the broth. Use exactly 2 tbsp soy (not 3), and skip any additional salt.`},{problem:`Sticky / gummy bottom`,fix:`Wok wasn't hot enough OR you stirred constantly. Get the wok medium-high BEFORE the rice goes in, and let the rice toast in 30-second intervals between stirs.`},{problem:`Eggs went rubbery`,fix:`Pulled at 100% set instead of 80%. Carryover heat in a hot wok finishes them — soft curds while they hit the rice, not dry chunks before.`}],smartUpgrades:[`Make it a real protein dinner: Add 6 oz cooked chicken thigh, shrimp, or steak per serving to push it to 500 cal / 38-42g protein. Honest framing: this base recipe is carb-dominant (38g carbs / 16g protein), and adding a protein is the canonical move. Crispy Chicken add-on is coming as its own recipe.`,`Make it vegetarian: drop the eggs and add 1 cup frozen edamame + 2 tbsp roasted peanuts. Same flavor architecture, 12g plant protein.`,`Make it lower-sodium: cut the soy to 1 tbsp + add 1 tsp rice vinegar. Same depth, half the salt.`],brands:[{name:`Kikkoman`,item:`All-Purpose Soy Sauce`,why:`Tier 1 sauce backbone. Clean salt + umami — no preservatives, no surprises. The default soy for the site for a reason.`,image:`/images/brands/kikkoman-soy-sauce.jpg`,url:`https://kikkomanusa.com/homecooks/products/soy-sauce-non-gmo/`},{name:`Huy Fong Foods`,item:`Sambal Oelek Ground Fresh Chili Paste`,why:`Fermented chili heat with no sugar, no vinegar dominance — pure chili. The grown-up sriracha. 2 tsp here delivers heat + texture without making the rice wet.`,image:`/images/brands/huy-fong-sambal-oelek.png`,url:`https://www.huyfong.com/sambal-oelek/`},{name:`Dynasty`,item:`Sesame Chili Oil (3.5 oz)`,why:`Toasted sesame aroma + slow chili burn. The aromatic layer that makes the rice smell like a restaurant kitchen. 2 tsp is enough — this is calorie-dense oil, not a free-pour.`,url:`https://www.amazon.com/Dynasty-Sesame-Chili-Oil-3-5/dp/B0001LJAW2`},{name:`Jet Tila's`,item:`Umami Punch Ssamjang-Inspired Seasoning (Spiceology)`,why:`The MSG-style amplifier. Doenjang + gochujang + sesame + garlic + green onion in a shaker. 2 tsp delivers the takeout-style 'how do they make it taste like THAT' depth at home.`,image:`/images/brands/jet-tila-umami-punch.jpg`,url:`https://spiceology.com/products/jet-tila-umami-punch-ssamjang-seasoning`},{name:`Bone Broth Rice`,item:`Cookbook cross-link — the base`,why:`This is THE base. Cold leftover bone broth rice is what makes the fried rice work. Make 8 servings on Sunday, fry on demand the rest of the week.`,url:`/cookbook/bone-broth-rice`}],macroHonesty:`Per-serving macros (333 cal / 16g protein / 12.5g fat / 35.5g carbs) are computed from the recipe ingredients. The Macrofactor app's 'Fried Rice Sauce (Nested)' entry shows 96 cal / 9g protein per sauce-serving, which materially overstates protein (soy + sambal + sesame oil + spice blend together can't deliver 9g protein in 2 tbsp of liquid). Site uses the ingredient-derived macros and flags them estimated. This is also a carb-dominant recipe by design — add a protein on top to push it into 'high-protein dinner' territory.`,mealPrep:{storage:`Best fresh — fried rice loses its toasty texture overnight. If you must store, fridge in an airtight container, 2-3 days max.`,lasts:`2-3 days fridge. Reheats OK in a hot dry pan with a splash of water (microwave makes it gummy).`,reheat:`Hot dry pan, 2-3 min, toss continuously, splash of water if needed. Skip the microwave.`}},{id:`tks-sweet-heat-chicken`,title:`TKS Sweet Heat Chicken`,tagline:`Crazy Cuizine chicken + TKS Sauce. Drop the orange-sauce packet, gain a real glaze, keep the 20 minutes.`,heroImage:`/images/tks-sweet-heat-chicken/hero.webp`,flavorProfile:`Crispy chicken in a glossy sweet-heat umami glaze. Bone broth body, sesame chili aroma, hot honey sriracha finish.`,calories:960,caloriesPerServing:480,protein:72,proteinPerServing:36,servings:2,time:`20 min`,bestFor:[`Quick dinner with Spicy Umami Fried Rice on the side`,`Solo lunch (one full serving = 480 cal / 36g protein)`,`TKS Bowls (chicken + rice + veg)`,`Wraps (chicken + Mission Zero tortilla + scallions)`,`Air-fryer freezer-to-plate dinner`],useThisWhen:`You bought the Costco Crazy Cuizine party box because it's reliable, but the included orange-sauce packet is a sugar bomb. Use the chicken (it's good), discard the sauce packet, glaze with TKS Sauce instead. 20 minutes, real takeout texture from technique not slurry.`,flavorTarget:`Restaurant-style sweet-heat glazed chicken — crispy bite, glossy coat, layered umami + chili + slight sweetness. The technique move: toss the air-fried chicken with warm TKS Sauce in a dry hot skillet 60-90 sec so the residual breading starch + sauce caramelize together. No cornstarch slurry, no xanthan. Real cling from real technique.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full serving (8 oz cooked chicken + half the TKS Sauce batch). Pair with Spicy Umami Fried Rice for a complete 800-cal high-protein dinner.`,kid:`Half serving (4 oz chicken). Skip or halve the hot honey sriracha in the sauce — savory backbone stays, sweet-heat edge dialed back. Most kids will eat the glazed chicken straight, no rice base needed.`},ingredients:[`--- PROTEIN ---`,`1 lb Crazy Cuizine Mandarin Orange Chicken (frozen, ~half the Costco party box)`,`*** Discard the included orange-sauce packet — that's a sugar bomb, you're swapping it out ***`,`--- THE SAUCE (THE WHOLE POINT) ---`,{text:`1 batch TKS Sauce — make ahead while chicken cooks, takes 2 minutes`,link:`/cookbook/tks-sauce`},`--- TIER 4 GARNISH (optional, recommended for visual + bite contrast) ---`,`1-2 scallions, sliced thin`,`1 tsp toasted sesame seeds`],steps:[`AIR FRY THE CHICKEN: From frozen, 400°F for 9-12 min. Shake basket halfway. Goal: crispy + golden, NOT soggy. Pull when the edges crack when squeezed (or follow box: 'fully cooked, ready in 20 min'). Single layer in the basket — overcrowding = steamed not crisp.`,`MAKE THE SAUCE: While chicken cooks (you have ~10 min). Whisk together ginger-garlic paste + sesame chili oil + rice vinegar + soy + bone broth packet + hot honey sriracha in a small bowl. Whisk hard — the packet powder needs to fully dissolve. (Full method on the TKS Sauce page.)`,`DUMP THE ORANGE PACKET. Seriously. The Crazy Cuizine box ships with a packet of sugary orange sauce. That's the part you're replacing. Throw it in the trash. This is the move.`,`HOT DRY SKILLET — THE CLING STEP: Heat a large nonstick or carbon-steel skillet on medium-high. NO oil — pan dry. When the pan is screaming hot (water droplet beads + skitters), add the crispy chicken.`,`TOSS WITH SAUCE: Pour the TKS Sauce around the edge of the hot pan (not directly on the chicken). It will hiss + bubble immediately. Toss aggressively for 60-90 seconds. The residual breading starch + the sauce reduce and caramelize together — natural restaurant glaze, no cornstarch slurry needed. Off heat the moment every piece is glossy.`,`PLATE + GARNISH: Pile chicken on a plate or in a bowl. Scatter sliced scallions + toasted sesame seeds on top (optional but recommended — visual lift, fresh bite, takes 10 seconds).`,`PAIR (optional but the whole point): Serve over Spicy Umami Fried Rice for a complete dinner. Chicken alone = 480 cal / 36g protein per serving. With rice = ~810 cal / 52g protein. Real dinner, real macros.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Sauce slid off the chicken instead of glazing`,fix:`Pan wasn't hot enough OR you poured sauce on the chicken instead of the pan edge. Medium-high heat, screaming hot pan, sauce around the edge — the hiss is the cue. Toss continuously for 60-90 sec until you see glaze cling, not run.`},{problem:`Chicken is soggy`,fix:`Air fryer overcrowded OR sauce sat on chicken too long. Single layer in the basket, shake halfway. AND don't toss with sauce until the pan is fully hot and the chicken is crispy first.`},{problem:`Sauce burned / chicken charred bottom`,fix:`Pan TOO hot OR tossed too slow. Medium-high (not high). Toss continuously — the sauce reduces fast.`},{problem:`Tastes like takeout but with weird sweetness`,fix:`Sauce wasn't whisked enough — bone broth powder clumps + sugar from seasoned rice vinegar dominate. Whisk harder OR use a shaker bottle to fully dissolve the packet.`},{problem:`Kid version still too spicy`,fix:`Make a half-batch of sauce with HALF the hot honey sriracha (3/4 tbsp instead of 1.5 tbsp). Toss the kid portion separately.`},{problem:`Want it thicker / stickier (proper takeout style)`,fix:`Don't add cornstarch — the breading does the job if you toss long enough. If the pan technique didn't get it sticky enough, simmer the sauce 60 sec BEFORE the toss to reduce it by 1/4 first.`}],brands:[{name:`Crazy Cuizine`,item:`Mandarin Orange Chicken (66 oz / 4 lb 2 oz Costco box)`,why:`Pre-cooked, pre-breaded, air-fryer ready — 9-12 min from frozen, no antibiotics, 13g protein per 3 oz serving. The chicken is good. The included orange-sauce packet is what's wrong with it — that's what TKS Sauce replaces. One Costco box = 4 dinners at this scale.`,image:`/images/brands/crazy-cuizine-mandarin-orange-chicken.jpg`,url:`https://www.costco.com/p/-/crazy-cuizine-mandarin-orange-chicken-66-oz/100437350`},{name:`TKS Sauce`,item:`Cookbook cross-link — the whole point`,why:`This recipe exists because the included orange packet is a sugar bomb. TKS Sauce is the macro-conscious replacement — same flavor architecture (sweet + heat + umami), with bone broth powder doing the body that cornstarch usually does. One batch = 2 servings of this dinner.`,url:`/cookbook/tks-sauce`},{name:`Spicy Umami Fried Rice`,item:`Cookbook cross-link — the canonical rice pairing`,why:`The full dinner is TKS Sweet Heat Chicken + Spicy Umami Fried Rice. Two bases that stack into one ~810 cal / 52g protein dinner, all from cookbook power-ups.`,url:`/cookbook/spicy-umami-fried-rice`}],macroHonesty:`Per-serving macros (480 cal / 36g protein / 18g fat / 30g carbs) computed assuming the discarded orange-sauce packet is NOT included — that's the whole point of this recipe. Crazy Cuizine's box-stated macros (220 cal / 13g protein per 3 oz) include the packet sauce, so subtracting that gives ~400-440 cal for 8 oz cooked breaded chicken alone, plus ~55 cal / 6g protein from half a batch of TKS Sauce = ~480 / 36g. Estimated because breaded chicken weight varies by cook level and exact piece distribution.`,mealPrep:{storage:`Best fresh — the glaze + crispy texture peaks straight off the pan. Leftover glazed chicken keeps 2 days, but the cling softens.`,reheat:`Air fryer 350°F for 3-4 min to re-crisp the breading. The sauce will lose some shine — fine for leftover lunches, not ideal for re-plating fresh.`,lasts:`Chicken 2 days. TKS Sauce batch separately keeps 4-5 days, so making chicken + sauce on different days works too.`,chainTo:{slug:`spicy-umami-fried-rice`,title:`Spicy Umami Fried Rice`,note:`Stack with cold bone-broth-rice-based fried rice for the full ~810 cal / 52g protein dinner. The carb-forward rice + protein-forward chicken = balanced takeout dinner that lives entirely in the cookbook bases system.`}}},{id:`parmesan-corn-chex-snap-peas`,title:`Parmesan Corn Chex Snap Peas`,tagline:`Two-crunch side. 2 tbsp aged Parm + 4 tbsp crushed Corn Chex = the side that disappears off any plate.`,heroImage:`/images/pork-chops-cowboy/step4-peas-done.webp`,flavorProfile:`Sweet snap pea pop + nutty aged Parmigiano crunch + crispy Corn Chex texture. The 2:1 chex-to-Parm ratio is the move — more crunch, less density.`,calories:320,caloriesPerServing:80,protein:4,proteinPerServing:1,servings:4,time:`5 min prep + 20 min bake`,bestFor:[`Pork chops (recipe 39)`,`Pan-seared chicken thighs`,`Steak (sirloin, ribeye, bavette)`,`Roasted salmon`,`Solo side / lunch`,`Anywhere you'd otherwise put plain roasted broccoli or asparagus`],useThisWhen:`You want a vegetable side that earns its own attention on the plate instead of being the leftover compartment. The crusted treatment turns snap peas into a craveable side — kids who reject 'plain peas' eat these because they read as 'crispy thing'.`,flavorTarget:`Crispy golden edges on the snap peas + visible Parm + Chex crumb adhered to each pod. NOT mush, NOT bare. The chex gives bulk + crunch, the Parm gives salt + umami. Together the combo is dense enough to coat without weighing the peas down.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe as written. Optional finish: hit with cracked black pepper + a squeeze of lemon at the table.`,kid:`Same recipe — kids eat the SAME crusted peas. The crust is a feature for kids (sweetness from peas + crunch). Some kids reject visible char on the pods; pull the ones that browned hardest for adults.`},ingredients:[`2 cups fresh sugar snap peas, trimmed (~12 oz)`,`Olive oil spray (about 4 seconds total)`,`2 tbsp Kirkland Parmigiano Reggiano Stravecchio, food-processed from a wedge to coarse grated`,`4 tbsp Corn Chex (General Mills), pulsed in food processor to coarse crumbs`,`Pinch salt + black pepper`,`Optional adult finish: cracked black pepper + lemon wedge at the table`],steps:[`PREHEAT OVEN 425°F. Line a sheet pan with parchment paper.`,`PROCESS THE PARM: Cube ~2 oz of Kirkland Stravecchio. Pulse in a food processor until coarse grated (NOT fine — you want visible flecks). Set aside.`,`PULSE THE CHEX: 4 tbsp Corn Chex into the same processor. Pulse 4-5 times until coarse crumbs — about the texture of panko, NOT powder. Visible flake bits are the goal.`,`TOSS IN A BOWL: Snap peas + olive oil spray (2-3 sec) + 2 tbsp processed Parm + 4 tbsp crushed Chex + pinch salt + pepper. Toss until each pea is coated. Toss in the bowl FIRST, then spread on the pan — even adherence beats sprinkling on the sheet.`,`SPREAD ON PARCHMENT: Single layer. Crumbs that fall onto the parchment will crisp into clusters — bonus crunch.`,`BAKE 18-22 MIN: 425°F. Pull when the snap pea edges are deep golden + the crust is crispy. Some pods will char slightly — that's the texture target.`,`SERVE IMMEDIATELY: Best straight from the oven. They soften on standing.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Crumb fell off the peas`,fix:`Not enough oil OR you didn't toss in a bowl first. Spray more (4 sec total), toss in a bowl, THEN spread. Crumbs adhere to the oil coating.`},{problem:`Peas turned mushy / didn't crisp`,fix:`Oven not hot enough OR overcrowded sheet pan. 425°F + single layer is non-negotiable. If using 2 cups of peas, a half-sheet pan is the right size.`},{problem:`Crumb burned before peas crisped`,fix:`Processor went too fine — fine crumb burns at high heat. Pulse 4-5 times max, leave visible flake bits. Or drop oven to 400°F + bake 25 min.`},{problem:`Too cheesy / overpowers the peas`,fix:`You used MORE than 2 tbsp Parm. The 2:1 chex-to-Parm ratio is the brand — Parm adds salt + umami, Chex carries the crunch. Going heavier on Parm makes it dense and greasy.`},{problem:`Not enough crunch`,fix:`Pulse Corn Chex less (more visible flake bits). Or bump to 5 tbsp. The crunch is what makes this side worth making vs plain roasted peas.`},{problem:`Kid won't eat them`,fix:`Pull the most-charred pods for adults and serve the kid the lighter-browned ones. The visual matters more than the flavor at age 3-5.`}],brands:[{name:`Kirkland Signature`,item:`Parmigiano Reggiano Stravecchio (aged over 36 months, ~2 lb wedge)`,why:`Real aged Parm with crystals + nutty depth that SURVIVE oven roasting. Pre-grated tubs disappear — you'd taste them as 'cheesy crumb' instead of 'aged Parm crunch'. Buy the wedge, process at home.`,image:`/images/brands/kirkland-parmigiano-stravecchio.jpg`,url:`https://www.costcobusinessdelivery.com/kirkland-signature-parmigiano-reggiano-straveccho,-2-lb-avg-wt.product.100113283.html`},{name:`General Mills`,item:`Corn Chex Cereal (12 oz, gluten-free)`,why:`Pulsed to coarse crumbs = the crunch carrier. Gluten-free, neutral flavor, lighter than panko, more flavor than rice crisps. The 2:1 chex-to-Parm ratio is the move.`,image:`/images/brands/corn-chex.jpeg`,url:`https://www.generalmillsfoodservice.com/products/category/cereal/box/corn-chex-box-12-oz`},{name:`Chosen Foods`,item:`Avocado Oil Spray`,why:`Spray-not-pour. 2-3 second spray = enough oil for the crumb to adhere without drowning the peas in grease. Cross-recipe with id 38 Lettuce Wraps.`,image:`/images/brands/chosen-foods-spray.png`,url:`https://www.chosenfoods.com/products/avocado-oil-cooking-spray`}],macroHonesty:`Per-serving (~80 cal / 4g protein / 3g fat / 10g carbs / ~7g net) computed: 12 oz snap peas ÷ 4 = 3 oz/serving (~30 cal) + 0.5 tbsp Parm (~25 cal / 2g protein) + 1 tbsp crushed Chex (~30 cal) + oil spray (~5 cal). Net carbs lower because snap peas have ~3g fiber per serving. Flagged estimated because pea weight varies + Chex crush density varies.`,mealPrep:{storage:`Best fresh. Day-2 peas soften in the fridge; the crust mostly survives but the snap pea pop is gone.`,lasts:`1 day fresh. 2-3 days if reheated dry-heat. Don't microwave — kills the crunch.`,reheat:`Air fryer 400°F for 4-5 min. Restores ~70% of the original crispness. Oven 400°F for 6-8 min also works.`,chainTo:{slug:`herb-garlic-pork-chops-cowboy-butter`,title:`Herb-Garlic Pork Chops + Cowboy Butter Drizzle`,note:`Built originally for this recipe. The crusted peas + sliced chop + cowboy butter drizzle = the flagship plating.`}}},{id:`caesar-crunch-salad`,title:`Caesar Crunch Salad`,tagline:`Pre-cooked chicken + crushed protein chips + yogurt Caesar. 199 cal, 27g protein, 4 min build.`,heroImage:`/images/caesar-crunch-pizza/step2-salad-mix.webp`,flavorProfile:`Crisp Sweet Gem + tangy yogurt Caesar + smoky fajita chicken + crunchy Hot & Spicy chips + Parmesan-jalapeño finisher. Restaurant-craveable, weeknight-fast.`,calories:398,caloriesPerServing:199,protein:55,proteinPerServing:27.5,servings:2,time:`4 min`,bestFor:[`Pizza Night (Caesar Crunch Pizza Night — recipe 40)`,`Sandwich night (next to a slider / smashburger)`,`Standalone lunch (4 min from fridge to plate)`,`Leftover chicken refresh`,`Cutting-friendly (199 cal / 27g protein per serving)`,`Post-workout (high-protein, high-volume)`],useThisWhen:`You want a Caesar salad that's restaurant-craveable but weeknight-fast and macro-honest. 27g of protein in 199 calories — that's the macro lever no other Caesar salad gives you. Built around pre-cooked Soules Kitchen Fajita Chicken (90-second cheat) + yogurt-based Bolthouse Caesar (1/3 the calories of real Caesar) + crushed Quest Hot & Spicy chips (crunch replacement for croutons, 19g protein per bag).`,flavorTarget:`Tangy + creamy from the yogurt Caesar, crunchy from the chips, smoky-warm from the fajita chicken, sharp finish from Dan-O's Jalapeño Cheesoning. NOT mayonnaise-heavy. NOT crouton-driven. NOT spicy — just lifted.`,splitNote:{adult:`Full recipe with Dan-O's Jalapeño Cheesoning sprinkled + optional Smoky Chipotle Crema drizzle. ~199 cal / 27.5g protein per serving.`,kid:`Smaller portion: half a serving. Skip the Dan-O's Cheesoning (visible flecks deter), skip the chipotle. Just lettuce + chicken + 1 tbsp Caesar tossed in. Some kids accept the crushed chips on top, some don't — read your kid.`},ingredients:[`6 oz Tanimura & Antle Artisan Sweet Gem Lettuce, chopped (or romaine hearts)`,`12 oz Soules Kitchen Fully Cooked Fajita Chicken Breast Strips, diced (6 oz per serving)`,`3 tbsp Bolthouse Farms Creamy Caesar Parmigiano dressing (1.5 portions per serving — yogurt-based, ~38 cal)`,`0.66 bag Quest Hot & Spicy Tortilla Style Protein Chips, crushed coarse (~21g per serving — replacing croutons)`,`Generous sprinkle Dan-O's Jalapeño Cheesoning [adult]`,{text:`Optional: 1-2 tsp Smoky Chipotle Crema drizzle [adult]`,link:`/cookbook/smoky-chipotle-crema`}],steps:[`CHOP LETTUCE: 6 oz Sweet Gem (or romaine) into bite pieces. Big bowl.`,`DICE CHICKEN: 12 oz Soules Kitchen Fajita Chicken into 1/2-inch cubes. Pre-cooked, just chop and fold in cold OR microwave 30 sec if you want it warm.`,`CRUSH CHIPS: 0.66 of a Quest Hot & Spicy bag, coarse-crushed (zip-bag + rolling pin works in 30 sec). KEEP ASIDE — don't toss in yet.`,`BUILD UNDRESSED: Combine lettuce + chicken in the bowl. Toss gently to distribute.`,`DRESS PER PORTION (not the whole bowl): Spoon half the bowl into a serving bowl. Drizzle ~1.5 portions of Bolthouse Creamy Caesar. Toss until coated.`,`FINISH: Top with crushed Quest chips (NOT pre-tossed — they go on TOP). Generous sprinkle Dan-O's Jalapeño Cheesoning. Optional: 1-2 tsp Smoky Chipotle Crema drizzle for adult heat.`,`SERVE IMMEDIATELY. Dressed salad with chips on top goes soggy in 5-10 min — don't pre-dress the bowl unless you're eating right away.`],troubleshooting:[{problem:`Salad wilted by dinner`,fix:`You pre-dressed the whole bowl. Dress per portion right before serving. Or dress the salad, but keep crushed chips off until the very last second.`},{problem:`Tastes flat / one-note`,fix:`Forgot the Dan-O's Jalapeño Cheesoning. Parmesan + jalapeño + Italian herbs are the brand differentiator — without it this is just 'Caesar with chips.' Bump if it still reads flat.`},{problem:`Chips lost their crunch`,fix:`Crushed too fine (powder) OR sat dressed too long. Crush COARSE (visible flake bits) and add at the very last moment.`},{problem:`Too much chicken to lettuce ratio`,fix:`Bump lettuce to 8 oz. The 6:12 chicken-to-lettuce ratio is calibrated for adult macro density; lighter eaters can do 8 oz lettuce per serving.`},{problem:`Kid won't eat it`,fix:`Try the 'lettuce-refuser' variant from recipe 40: skip the lettuce entirely. 2 oz diced Soules Chicken in a small bowl + 1 tbsp Bolthouse Caesar for dipping = kid 'chicken nuggets.'`}],brands:[{name:`Soules Kitchen`,item:`Fully Cooked Fajita Chicken Breast Strips (16 oz refrigerated)`,why:`Pre-cooked, fully seasoned, fire-grilled. T2 reliable protein. 18g protein per 3 oz serving. Chop and fold in cold or microwave 30 sec.`,image:`/images/brands/soules-fajita-chicken.png`,url:`https://www.souleskitchen.com/products/fajita-chicken/`},{name:`Tanimura & Antle`,item:`Artisan Sweet Gem Lettuce (4-head pack)`,why:`Crisp without snapping; holds dressing without wilting fast. Cross-recipe with id 38 Pork Lettuce Wraps and recipe 40 Caesar Crunch Pizza Night.`,image:`/images/brands/tanimura-antle-sweet-gem.png`,url:`https://www.taproduce.com/artisan-sweet-gem/`},{name:`Bolthouse Farms`,item:`Creamy Caesar Parmigiano (yogurt-based, ~50 cal per 2 tbsp)`,why:`Yogurt base = 1/3 the calories of restaurant Caesar (50 cal vs 150+ per 2 tbsp). Still creamy + parmesan-forward. The macro lever that makes Caesar weeknight-eligible.`,image:`/images/brands/bolthouse-caesar.png`,url:`https://www.bolthouse.com/products/creamy-caesar-parmigiano-yogurt-dressing/`},{name:`Quest Nutrition`,item:`Tortilla Style Protein Chips — Hot & Spicy (1.1 oz / 19g protein per bag)`,why:`Crunch replacement for croutons. Cross-recipe with id 22 Smash Tacos and recipe 40. 4g net carbs per bag, baked not fried. The Hot & Spicy adds tingle without overpowering.`,image:`/images/brands/quest-hot-spicy.png`,url:`https://www.questnutrition.com/products/hot-and-spicy-tortilla-style-protein-chips`},{name:`Dan-O's`,item:`Jalapeño Cheesoning Seasoning (2.6 oz)`,why:`Parmesan + dried jalapeño + Italian herbs. The 5-cal finisher that turns ordinary Caesar into 'Caesar Crunch.' Cross-Dan-O's-family with Original / Outlaw S&T / SPG / Cheesoning.`,image:`/images/brands/danos-jalapeno-cheesoning.png`,url:`https://danosseasoning.com/product/jalapeno-cheesoning-seasoning-small/`}],macroHonesty:`Per-serving (199 cal / 27.5g protein / 5.5g fat / 9.3g carbs / 2.6g fiber → ~6.7g net carbs) MacroFactor-verified from logged ingredients: 6 oz Soules Fajita Chicken (223c / 38P) + 1.5 portion Bolthouse Caesar (38c / 2P) + 6 oz romaine (30c / 2P) + 0.66 bag Quest Hot & Spicy (93c / 13P) + optional Liquid Chipotle (16c) ÷ 2 servings. Dan-O's Jalapeño Cheesoning adds ~5 cal/serving uncounted in the macros (negligible). Real chicken Caesar at a restaurant is typically 450-600 cal for the same protein density — this is the macro-honest weeknight version.`,mealPrep:{storage:`Salad base (undressed) holds 3 days in the fridge. Bolthouse Caesar separately keeps as-purchased. Crushed Quest chips in a sealed jar 2 days.`,lasts:`Best within 24 hr of build. Dressed salad with chips: same-day only.`,reheat:`None — serve cold. If chicken was warmed, the salad goes lightly wilted.`,chainTo:{slug:`caesar-crunch-pizza-night`,title:`Caesar Crunch Pizza Night (recipe 40)`,note:`The dinner this salad was built for. Adults get the full Caesar Crunch + 1/3 Bettergoods Margherita; kids get a personal Red Baron Deep Dish + small Caesar portion.`}}}];export{e as a,n as i,t as n,r,i as t};